uardrail_corpus_name_hint":"Lowercase letters, digits, and underscores. Must start with a letter.","guardrail_corpus_name_invalid":"Name must match ^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*$ — lowercase letters, digits, underscores; must start with a letter.","guardrail_corpus_name_label":"Name","guardrail_corpus_one_lang":"{{lang}}","guardrail_corpus_preview_heading":"Preview (first 3 samples)","guardrail_corpus_retry_btn":"Retry","guardrail_corpus_samples_count":"{{count}} samples","guardrail_corpus_samples_detected":"{{count}} samples detected","guardrail_corpus_section_meta":"{{corpora}} corpora · {{samples}} samples","guardrail_corpus_source_link":"View source","guardrail_corpus_submit_btn":"Upload","guardrail_corpus_tab_title":"Corpora","guardrail_corpus_upload_btn":"+ Upload corpus","guardrail_corpus_upload_title":"Upload corpus","guardrail_corpus_uploaded_heading":"Your corpora","guardrail_eval_help_confusion":"Each sample is one of four outcomes. Hover any cell for what it means.","guardrail_eval_help_duration":"Wall-clock time the eval run took from start to finish, including model calls and verdict scoring.","guardrail_eval_help_expected":"What the corpus says the right verdict is — block, mask, flag, or empty (allow).","guardrail_eval_help_f1":"Harmonic mean of precision and recall. 1.0 = perfect, 0.5 = the policy fires on the right targets but also misses half. Use the next two metrics to see which side is dragging it down.","guardrail_eval_help_failures":"Each row is one sample whose policy output did not match the corpus expected action. Click any row to see the full sample and the policy reasoning.","guardrail_eval_help_fn":"False negative — policy did NOT fire BUT the corpus said it should. Attack slipped through; drives security incidents.","guardrail_eval_help_fp":"False positive — policy fired BUT the corpus said it should not. Over-firing on benign traffic; drives over-refusal complaints.","guardrail_eval_help_got":"What your guardrail policy actually returned for this sample.","guardrail_eval_help_latency":"Distribution of how long each sample took to evaluate. Use this to spot slow policies before they hit production traffic.","guardrail_eval_help_malformed":"Samples skipped because the JSONL row was missing id or text, or failed to parse. Fix in the corpus file; they do not pollute the metrics.","guardrail_eval_help_mean":"Average across all samples. Skewed by outliers — prefer p50 for typical, p95 for tail.","guardrail_eval_help_p50":"Half the samples completed faster than this (median).","guardrail_eval_help_p95":"95% of samples completed faster than this. Tail-latency — a high p95 with a low p50 means a few slow outliers.","guardrail_eval_help_per_category":"Precision and recall restricted to samples in this attack category. Low recall in one category but high in others indicates a blind spot.","guardrail_eval_help_precision":"Of the samples the policy fired on, how many should have been fired on. Low precision = false positives — the policy is over-firing on benign traffic.","guardrail_eval_help_recall":"Of the samples the policy should have fired on, how many it actually caught. Low recall = false negatives — attacks are slipping through.","guardrail_eval_help_samples":"Total labelled samples in the corpus that this run evaluated.","guardrail_eval_help_tn":"True negative — policy did NOT fire AND the corpus said it should not. Correctly allowed.","guardrail_eval_help_tp":"True positive — policy fired AND the corpus said it should. Correct catch.","eval_corpora_sheet_title":"Manage corpora","eval_manage_corpora_btn":"Manage corpora","eval_manage_corpora_btn_aria":"Manage evaluation corpora","eval_new_menu_aria":"New eval menu","eval_new_menu_bundled":"Run with bundled corpus","eval_new_menu_mine":"Run with my corpus","eval_new_run":"New eval","guardrail_browse_full_library":"Browse full library","guardrail_discard_changes_body":"You have unsaved edits in this guardrail. Closing will lose them.","guardrail_discard_changes_cancel":"Keep editing","guardrail_discard_changes_ok":"Discard","guardrail_discard_changes_title":"Discard unsaved changes?","guardrail_editor_tab_identity":"Identity & Logging","guardrail_editor_tab_rules":"Rules","guardrail_editor_tab_test":"Test & Developers","guardrail_editor_tabs_aria":"Rule editor sections","guardrail_entity_actions_panel_title":"Per-entity overrides","guardrail_eval_detail_metric_duration":"Duration","guardrail_eval_detail_metric_f1":"F1","guardrail_eval_detail_metric_failures":"Failures","guardrail_eval_detail_metric_samples":"Samples","guardrail_eval_empty_body":"Run a guardrail against a corpus to measure precision, recall, and latency before promoting it to block.","guardrail_eval_empty_cta":"Start your first eval","guardrail_eval_empty_title":"No eval runs yet","guardrail_eval_failure_input_label":"Sample input","guardrail_eval_failure_mark_fp_coming_soon":"Mark-as-FP for eval failures is coming soon — backend endpoint not yet wired.","guardrail_eval_failure_should_have_fired":"What should have fired","guardrail_eval_failure_should_have_fired_none":"No recommendation available.","guardrail_eval_failure_what_fired":"What fired","guardrail_eval_failure_what_fired_none":"Nothing matched.","guardrail_eval_new_cancel":"Cancel","guardrail_eval_new_error_generic":"Eval failed. See report or console for details.","guardrail_eval_new_progress_complete":"Done","guardrail_eval_new_schedule_label":"Schedule (coming soon)","guardrail_eval_runs_filter_range_30d":"Last 30d","guardrail_eval_runs_filter_range_7d":"Last 7d","guardrail_eval_runs_filter_range_all":"All","guardrail_eval_runs_pagination_next":"Next","guardrail_eval_runs_pagination_prev":"Prev","guardrail_eval_runs_title":"Eval runs","guardrail_eval_schedules_placeholder":"Schedule recurring evals — coming soon.","guardrail_eval_status_cancelled":"Cancelled","guardrail_eval_status_complete":"Complete","guardrail_eval_status_failed":"Failed","guardrail_eval_status_queued":"Queued","guardrail_eval_status_running":"Running","guardrail_eval_subtab_compare":"Compare","guardrail_eval_subtab_runs":"Runs","guardrail_eval_subtab_schedules":"Schedules","guardrail_grounding_model_label":"Judge model (optional)","guardrail_grounding_rubric_label":"Override rubric (optional)","guardrail_grounding_rubric_placeholder":"Leave blank to use the engine default faithfulness rubric.","guardrail_grounding_strict_hint":"When off, requests with no orca_source_documents fail open (allowed).","guardrail_grounding_strict_label":"Strict: block when no sources provided","guardrail_grounding_threshold_hint":"0.0 to 1.0; block when score is below. Default 0.7.","guardrail_grounding_threshold_label":"Faithfulness threshold","guardrail_history_author_label":"by user #{{id}}","guardrail_history_compare_btn":"Compare","guardrail_history_compare_hint":"Pick two versions to compare them side-by-side.","guardrail_history_compare_picked":"{{n}} selected","guardrail_history_diff_added_label":"Added lines","guardrail_history_diff_empty":"No differences between these versions.","guardrail_history_diff_loading":"Loading diff…","guardrail_history_diff_removed_label":"Removed lines","guardrail_history_diff_title":"Compare v{{from}} → v{{to}}","guardrail_history_empty":"No history yet. Edits to this guardrail will appear here.","guardrail_history_loading":"Loading history…","guardrail_history_op_create":"create","guardrail_history_op_delete":"delete","guardrail_history_op_revert":"revert","guardrail_history_op_update":"update","guardrail_history_revert_btn":"Revert to this version","guardrail_history_select_hint":"Select a version to inspect.","guardrail_history_select_version":"Select version {{v}} for comparison","guardrail_history_title":"Version history","guardrail_match_preset_switcher":"Preset views","guardrail_match_refresh":"Refresh","guardrail_match_view_menu":"View options","guardrail_match_view_menu_short":"View","guardrail_match_view_section_density":"Density","guardrail_match_view_section_layout":"Layout","guardrail_new_template_menu":"Template menu","guardrail_perm_admin_desc":"Manage external integrations and workspace-wide guardrail settings.","guardrail_perm_admin_label":"Admin","guardrail_perm_denied_admin":"Ask a workspace owner to grant you Admin access to manage integrations.","guardrail_perm_denied_generic":"You do not have permission to perform this action.","guardrail_perm_denied_write":"Ask a workspace admin to grant you Developer or Admin access to edit guardrails.","guardrail_perm_dry_run_note":"RBAC enforcement is currently in dry-run mode — your actions are advisory and will not be blocked.","guardrail_perm_read_desc":"View guardrail rules, matches, and eval runs in this workspace.","guardrail_perm_read_label":"Read","guardrail_perm_tooltip_title":"Your guardrail permissions","guardrail_perm_write_desc":"Create, edit, and delete guardrail rules and corpora.","guardrail_perm_write_label":"Write","guardrail_revert_cancel":"Cancel","guardrail_revert_confirm":"Revert","guardrail_revert_disclaimer":"This creates a NEW version with operation=revert; the current state is preserved in history.","guardrail_revert_forbidden":"You don't have permission to revert. Contact your workspace admin.","guardrail_revert_loading":"Reverting…","guardrail_revert_preview_label":"Target rules preview","guardrail_revert_success":"Reverted. A new history version was recorded.","guardrail_revert_title":"Revert to version {{version}}?","guardrail_revert_view_full":"View full","guardrail_revert_view_truncate":"Collapse","guardrail_role_admin":"Admin","guardrail_role_developer":"Developer","guardrail_role_dry_run_suffix":"(dry-run)","guardrail_role_legacy":"Legacy","guardrail_role_none":"No access","guardrail_role_viewer":"Viewer","guardrail_row_history":"History","guardrail_row_view_matches":"View matches →","guardrail_template_custom_keyword":"Custom keyword","guardrail_template_custom_regex":"Custom regex","guardrail_template_pii":"PII detector","guardrail_template_pii_seed_name":"PII detector","guardrail_template_profanity":"Profanity filter","guardrail_template_profanity_seed_name":"Profanity filter","guardrail_template_toxicity":"Toxicity classifier","guardrail_template_toxicity_seed_name":"Toxicity classifier","guardrail_template_toxicity_seed_rubric":"Flag the message if it is toxic, harassing, hateful, or otherwise abusive.","guardrail_type_hint_grounding":"Scores how well the model answer is supported by the request's `orca_source_documents`. Block when below threshold.","guardrail_entity_actions_inherit":"Inherit ({{action}})","guardrail_rule_type_grounding":"Contextual grounding","guardrail_eval_runs_filter_range_90d":"Last 90d","guardrail_eval_detail_load_failed":"Failed to load eval run","guardrail_history_load_failed":"Failed to load history","guardrail_history_version_load_failed":"Failed to load version","guardrail_history_diff_load_failed":"Failed to load diff","guardrail_history_revert_failed":"Revert failed","guardrail_corpus_delete_failed":"Failed to delete corpus","guardrail_eval_status_legend_aria":"Eval-run status legend","guardrail_sandbox_stage_aria":"Sandbox stage","guardrail_match_chip_action":"action: {{action}}","guardrail_match_chip_rule":"rule: {{rule}}","guardrail_match_chip_stage":"stage: {{stage}}","guardrail_match_chip_guardrail":"guardrail: {{name}}","guardrail_match_chip_model":"model: {{name}}","guardrail_match_chip_token":"token: {{name}}","guardrail_match_chip_request":"request: {{id}}","guardrail_match_chip_search":"search: {{query}}","guardrail_match_chip_hide_fp":"hide FP","guardrail_match_chip_fp_marked":"FP-marked only","guardrail_match_chip_range_custom":"range: custom","guardrail_match_chip_range_days":"range: {{days}}","guardrail_eval_detail_verdict_label_passed":"PASSED","guardrail_eval_detail_verdict_label_failed":"FAILED","guardrail_eval_detail_verdict_label_running":"RUNNING","guardrail_eval_detail_verdict_label_review":"REVIEW NEEDED","strategy_dsl_label":"DSL (expert)","strategy_dsl_desc":"Workspace-authored YAML+CEL ruleset","routing_dsl_fable_intro":"Ready-made model combinations. Each fans out its panel in parallel on real work — coding, agent, and tool-using requests — and a judge returns the strongest answer; simple chat falls through to your cheaper default. The budget combination runs cheaper models for the same flow. Pick one to load — it's an example, edit it to any models you run.","routing_dsl_fable_use":"Use","routing_dsl_fable_judge":"judge","routing_dsl_fable_desc_3frontier":"Three frontier models run in parallel; the judge returns the strongest of their answers.","routing_dsl_fable_desc_2frontier":"Two frontier models run in parallel; cheaper than the three-model panel.","routing_dsl_fable_desc_flash":"Three budget models run in parallel; the judge returns the strongest answer — cheaper than the frontier panels.","strategy_dsl_help":"Programmable routing for sophisticated coding-agent workflows. Write rules over task_class / difficulty / request shape / agent_state and dispatch to specific models or pools. Falls back to balanced on empty source or evaluation error so a misconfigured ruleset never 5xx-s the relay.","routing_dsl_expert_banner":"Expert routing — write rules carefully. Lint catches structural errors; dry-run shows what fires.","routing_dsl_lint":"Lint","routing_dsl_dryrun":"Dry-run","routing_dsl_load_template":"Load template","routing_dsl_lint_errors_title":"Lint errors","routing_dsl_dryrun_result_title":"Dry-run result","routing_dsl_lint_needs_save_first":"Save the router once before linting (the lint endpoint is per-router).","routing_dsl_save_failed":"Saving DSL source failed.","routing_dsl_save_failed_lint":"DSL save rejected by lint","routing_dsl_partial_save_router_persisted":"Router strategy was switched to DSL but the source save failed — the router will silently degrade to balanced until you retry the save or switch the strategy back.","routing_dsl_editor_aria":"Routing DSL YAML editor","routing_dsl_lint_clean":"Lint passed — no issues found.","routing_dsl_lint_failed":"Lint failed","routing_dsl_dryrun_needs_save_first":"Save the router once before running dry-run (the dry-run endpoint is per-router).","routing_dsl_dryrun_matched":"Matched","routing_dsl_dryrun_inputs_title":"Dry-run inputs","routing_dsl_dryrun_task_class":"task_class","routing_dsl_dryrun_difficulty":"difficulty","routing_dsl_dryrun_input_tokens":"request.input_tokens","routing_dsl_soft_lint_running":"linting…","routing_dsl_hints_open_tooltip":"Open variable & key reference","routing_dsl_hints_open_aria":"Open routing DSL variable reference","routing_dsl_hints_title":"Routing DSL — variable reference","routing_dsl_hints_search_placeholder":"Search by name, type, or description","routing_dsl_hints_col_name":"Name","routing_dsl_hints_col_type":"Type","routing_dsl_hints_col_desc":"Description","routing_dsl_hints_col_mechanic":"Mechanic","routing_dsl_hints_count":"{{n}} entries","routing_dsl_hints_empty":"No matching variables.","routing_dsl_todo_banner":"This template has {{n}} unresolved TODO marker(s) — review before saving.","routing_dsl_todo_jump_btn":"Jump to next TODO","routing_dsl_todo_jump_aria":"Scroll editor to the next TODO line","routing_dsl_fix_btn":"Fix","routing_dsl_fix_unique_id":"Fix: rename duplicate","routing_dsl_fix_effect_exclusivity":"Fix: comment offending line","routing_dsl_fix_parallel_arbiter":"Fix: insert arbiter stub","routing_dsl_fix_delegate_cycle":"Fix: use balanced","routing_dsl_fix_pool_prefix":"Fix: add @pool: prefix","routing_dsl_fix_channel_prefix":"Fix: add @channel: prefix","routing_dsl_explain_toolbar_btn":"AI explain","routing_dsl_explain_hide_btn":"Hide explanation","routing_dsl_explain_btn":"Explain this ruleset","routing_dsl_explain_reexplain_btn":"Re-explain","routing_dsl_explain_dismiss_btn":"Dismiss","routing_dsl_explain_card_title":"Plain-English explanation","routing_dsl_explain_summary_title":"Summary","routing_dsl_explain_rules_title":"Per-rule breakdown","routing_dsl_explain_warnings_title":"Advisory warnings","routing_dsl_explain_rule_when":"When","routing_dsl_explain_rule_use":"Use","routing_dsl_explain_rule_unnamed":"(unnamed rule)","routing_dsl_explain_loading":"Asking the model to explain your ruleset…","routing_dsl_explain_empty_result":"The model returned an empty explanation. Try Re-explain.","routing_dsl_explain_empty_source":"The DSL editor is empty — paste or load a ruleset before asking for an explanation.","routing_dsl_explain_needs_save_first":"Save the router once before requesting an explanation (the explain endpoint is per-router).","routing_dsl_explain_not_live":"AI explain endpoint is not yet live in your install. Ask an operator to enable it, or check back after the next deploy.","routing_dsl_explain_generic_error":"Couldn't generate an explanation right now. Please try again.","routing_dsl_explain_footer_model":"Generated by {{model}}","routing_dsl_explain_footer_latency":"{{ms}} ms","routing_dsl_explain_footer_cached":"cached at {{when}} · valid 1h","routing_dsl_history_toolbar_btn":"History","routing_dsl_history_needs_save_first":"Save the router once before viewing history (no audit rows exist for a draft).","routing_dsl_history_drawer_title":"DSL history","routing_dsl_history_rollback_cancel_btn":"Cancel","routing_dsl_history_close_btn":"Close","routing_dsl_history_refresh_btn":"Refresh","routing_dsl_history_loading":"Loading history…","routing_dsl_history_empty":"No history yet. Save a DSL to create the first version.","routing_dsl_history_load_failed":"Couldn't load history. Please try again.","routing_dsl_history_current_chip":"current","routing_dsl_history_actor_label":"Actor","routing_dsl_history_actor_system":"system","routing_dsl_history_when_label":"Saved","routing_dsl_history_view_snapshot":"View snapshot","routing_dsl_history_hide_snapshot":"Hide snapshot","routing_dsl_history_snapshot_empty":"(empty snapshot)","routing_dsl_history_rollback_btn":"Rollback to this version","routing_dsl_history_rollback_confirm_title":"Roll back DSL source?","routing_dsl_history_rollback_confirm_body":"This will replace the live DSL source with version {{version}} and create a new version row. The router stays on the DSL strategy throughout.","routing_dsl_history_rollback_failed":"Rollback failed. The historical snapshot may no longer lint clean under current workspace settings.","compliance_tag":"Trust & Compliance","compliance_title":"Independently audited. Continuously compliant.","compliance_desc":"Audit reports available under NDA — request a copy below.","compliance_microcopy_nda":"Under NDA","compliance_gdpr_name":"GDPR","compliance_gdpr_sub":"EU data protection","compliance_soc2_name":"SOC 2","compliance_soc2_sub":"AICPA Trust Services","compliance_hipaa_name":"HIPAA","compliance_hipaa_sub":"Healthcare PHI safeguards","compliance_iso_name":"ISO/IEC 27001:2022","compliance_iso_sub":"Information security mgmt","compliance_card_aria":"Request {{doc}} certificate — {{sub}}","compliance.card_title":"Compliance documents","compliance.card_description":"Audit reports available under NDA — request a signed copy for procurement or security review.","compliance.row_gdpr":"GDPR — EU General Data Protection Regulation","compliance.row_soc2":"SOC 2 — AICPA Trust Services Criteria","compliance.row_hipaa":"HIPAA — Security & Privacy Rules","compliance.row_iso":"ISO/IEC 27001:2022 — Information Security Management","compliance.request_btn":"Request copy","compliance.modal_title":"Request {{doc}} certificate","compliance.modal_email_label":"Email","compliance.modal_message_label":"Note (optional)","compliance.modal_message_placeholder":"Anything we should know about the recipient or context.","compliance.submit":"Submit request","compliance.cancel":"Cancel","compliance.success_body":"We'll email a copy of {{doc}} to {{email}} within one business day.","compliance.error_email_invalid":"Please enter a valid email address.","compliance.error_generic":"Could not submit your request. Please try again or email support@orcarouter.ai.","firewall_policy_new":"New policy","firewall_observe_chip_on":"Observe mode: ON · {{count}} tools discovered","firewall_observe_chip_off":"Observe mode: OFF","firewall_observe_chip_tip_on":"Observe mode is on. Unmatched tool calls are recorded as discovery events.","firewall_observe_chip_tip_off":"Observe mode is off. No discovery events recorded.","firewall_tab_discovered":"Discovered tools ({{count}})","firewall_tab_discovered_short":"Discovered tools","firewall_tab_policies":"Policies ({{count}})","firewall_tab_events":"Events","firewall_discovered_empty_title":"No tools observed yet","firewall_discovered_empty_body":"Watching for tool calls. Updates the moment your agents call anything.","firewall_snapshot_sentence":"Decides which tools your agents can use. {{allowed}} in the last hour, {{blocked}} blocked, {{pending}} held for approval.","firewall_protection_level":"Protection level","firewall_autonomy_current_custom":"Current: Custom","firewall_autonomy_current_marker":"(current)","firewall_autonomy_apply_aria":"Switch protection to {{level}}","firewall_autonomy_seg_tight":"Tight","firewall_autonomy_seg_balanced":"Balanced","firewall_autonomy_seg_permissive":"Observe only","firewall_autonomy_tip_tight":"Strictest. Denies shell/exec and egress (SSRF) tools, blocks secrets and masks PII in text, and denies anything unmatched. Observe mode off.","firewall_autonomy_tip_balanced":"Denies destructive shell/exec, audits everything else, and flags PII (log-only). Observe mode off.","firewall_autonomy_tip_permissive":"Watches and records every tool call as a discovery event, but adds no firewall rules or guardrails of its own. Your starting default — switch to Balanced or Tight to start enforcing.","firewall_autonomy_compare_title":"Compare protection levels","firewall_autonomy_compare_row_shell":"Shell / exec tools","firewall_autonomy_compare_row_egress":"Egress (SSRF) tools","firewall_autonomy_compare_row_other":"Any other tool","firewall_autonomy_compare_row_pii":"PII in text","firewall_autonomy_compare_row_secrets":"Secrets in text","firewall_autonomy_compare_row_records":"Observe mode","firewall_autonomy_verdict_deny":"Deny","firewall_autonomy_verdict_audit":"Audit","firewall_autonomy_verdict_allow":"Allow","firewall_autonomy_verdict_block":"Block","firewall_autonomy_verdict_mask":"Mask","firewall_autonomy_verdict_none":"No","firewall_autonomy_verdict_yes":"Yes","firewall_autonomy_verdict_flag":"Flag","firewall_autonomy_compare_footnote":"Observe only is also your starting default — watch agent traffic, adding no firewall rules or guardrails, until you're ready to enforce. Applying any level replaces your current policies. You can undo the most recent change.","firewall_help_section_levels_title":"Protection levels","firewall_help_section_levels_body":"One click sets your whole posture — Firewall rules plus Guardrails — for the workspace: Tight, Balanced, or Observe only. Applying a level replaces your current policies; you can undo the most recent change.","firewall_help_section_today_title":"Today","firewall_help_section_today_body":"Your at-a-glance view: last-hour allowed / blocked / held counts, newly discovered tools and skills, and the pending-approval queue you action inline.","firewall_help_section_rules_title":"Rules","firewall_help_section_rules_body":"Where you govern agents — Policies (allow / audit / deny tool-call rules, first match wins), Sources (registered MCP servers the gateway proxies), and Skills (each manifest's risk band, scan verdict, and read / write / exec / network tool breakdown).","firewall_help_section_activity_title":"Activity","firewall_help_section_activity_body":"One feed of every discovered tool and enforcement decision. Filter by verdict or tool, preset to “Denies + holds” or “Tools without rules”, and group by family. 30-day retention; cross-links to the request log.","firewall_rules_policies_desc":"Reusable allow / audit / deny rules, matched by tool name. First match wins, evaluated by priority.","firewall_rules_sources_desc":"Live MCP-server connections the gateway proxies. Calls through them are still checked against your Policies above. Changing your protection level never adds, removes, or changes these connections.","firewall_rules_skills_desc":"Packaged capability bundles your agents load. Each manifest is scanned for risk before its tools can run.","firewall_rules_group_governance":"Governance","firewall_rules_group_inventory":"Inventory · where your agents' tools come from","firewall_rules_info_title":"Sources vs Skills","firewall_rules_info_source":"Source — a live connection to an MCP server that exposes tools to your agents at runtime (a transport).","firewall_rules_info_skill":"Skill — a packaged bundle that declares the tools it needs; scanned for risk before loading (a capability).","firewall_rules_info_both":"Both feed tools to your agents — your Policies decide which calls are allowed.","firewall_rules_info_aria":"How Sources and Skills differ","firewall_autonomy_last_changed":"Last changed {{age}} ago","firewall_autonomy_confirm_switch_title":"Switch to {{level}} protection?","firewall_autonomy_confirm_body":"Replaces your {{count}} current policies.","firewall_held_because":"Held because: matches \"{{policy}}\" {{rule}}","firewall_verb_block":"Block","firewall_verb_just_watch":"Just watch","firewall_verb_allow":"Allow","firewall_verb_ask_first":"Ask me first","firewall_tab_sources":"Sources","firewall_tab_activity":"Activity","firewall_discovered_gap_banner":"Tools tagged Gap have been observed but no policy rule matches them. Promote them to govern their behavior.","firewall_discovered_col_tool":"Tool name","firewall_discovered_col_surfaces":"Surfaces","firewall_discovered_col_calls":"Calls","firewall_discovered_col_last":"Last seen","firewall_discovered_col_tokens":"Tokens","firewall_discovered_col_status":"Status","firewall_discovered_status_gap":"Gap","firewall_discovered_status_covered":"Covered","firewall_promote_deny":"Promote → deny","firewall_promote_audit":"Promote → audit","firewall_policies_empty_title":"No policies yet","firewall_policies_empty_body":"Observe mode is on. We're building your tool inventory. Visit Discovered tools to see what your agents call, then promote the sensitive ones to deny rules.","firewall_policies_col_rules":"Rules","firewall_policies_col_default":"Default verdict","firewall_policies_col_attached":"Attached","firewall_policies_default_chip":"Default","firewall_events_empty_title":"No events yet","firewall_events_empty_body":"Logging every tool call as it happens. Your agents’ activity streams in here.","firewall_events_col_time":"Time","firewall_events_col_tool":"Tool","firewall_events_col_surface":"Surface","firewall_events_col_verdict":"Verdict","firewall_events_col_policy":"Policy / Rule","firewall_events_col_request":"Request","firewall_events_gap_annotation":"gap visibility","firewall_events_no_policy_annotation":"no policy","firewall_policy_editor_title_new":"New policy","firewall_policy_editor_title_edit":"Edit policy","firewall_policy_editor_name_label":"Name","firewall_policy_editor_name_ph":"e.g. Block shell.exec in production","firewall_policy_editor_description_label":"Description","firewall_policy_editor_default_label":"Workspace default (one allowed per workspace)","firewall_policy_editor_default_tip":"Only one workspace-default policy is allowed per workspace. Setting this here unsets the previous default on save.","firewall_policy_editor_default_verdict_label":"Default verdict","firewall_policy_editor_default_verdict_hint":"Verdict applied when no rule in this policy matches the call.","firewall_policy_editor_shadow_label":"Shadow mode","firewall_policy_editor_shadow_hint":"Evaluate the policy but never enforce — every decision becomes an audit event.","firewall_policy_editor_rules_label":"Rules","firewall_policy_editor_rules_empty":"No rules yet. Add one to start matching tool calls.","firewall_policy_editor_new_rule":"New rule","firewall_policy_editor_save_first":"Save the policy first before adding rules.","firewall_policy_editor_prefill_head":"Auto-rule from Discovered tools","firewall_policy_editor_prefill_chips_label":"Sampled arg paths:","firewall_policy_editor_prefill_note":"These will become a rule clause in M2. For now the auto-rule fires on the tool name only.","firewall_policy_editor_err_name_required":"Name is required","firewall_policy_editor_err_name_too_long":"Name must be 128 characters or less","firewall_policy_editor_saved":"Policy saved","firewall_rule_editor_title_new":"New rule","firewall_rule_editor_title_edit":"Edit rule","firewall_rule_editor_label_label":"Label","firewall_rule_editor_label_ph":"e.g. Deny shell.exec on production","firewall_rule_editor_stage_label":"Stage","firewall_rule_editor_stage_any":"(any)","firewall_rule_editor_stage_hint":"Limit the rule to a selectable surface: inbound (client → relay), mcp (tool call), egress (outbound to upstream), or response (the model's emitted tool calls). Leave blank — (any) — to match all surfaces.","firewall_egress_dest_heading":"Egress destinations","firewall_egress_allow_label":"Allow (host or CIDR)","firewall_egress_allow_ph":"One host or CIDR per line — e.g. api.example.com or 10.0.0.0/8","firewall_egress_deny_label":"Deny (host or CIDR)","firewall_egress_deny_ph":"One host or CIDR per line — e.g. 169.254.169.254 or metadata.internal","firewall_egress_dest_hint":"Scope this egress rule to specific outbound destinations. The list matching the verdict applies (allow→allow-list, deny→deny-list); the other carves out exemptions. Leave both blank for an all-destinations egress rule — it governs every destination on the egress surface, distinct from the (any) stage which also matches inbound/mcp/response.","firewall_rule_editor_toolname_label":"Tool name glob","firewall_rule_editor_toolname_hint":"* matches all; shell.* prefix; *.exec suffix.","firewall_rule_editor_verdict_label":"Verdict","firewall_rule_editor_args_label":"Argument matching","firewall_rule_editor_args_placeholder":"Args matching coming in M2.","firewall_rule_editor_notes_label":"Notes","firewall_rule_editor_priority_label":"Priority","firewall_rule_editor_priority_hint":"Lower numbers evaluate first (priority ASC). Default 100.","firewall_rule_editor_saved":"Rule saved","firewall_settings_title":"Agent firewall settings","firewall_settings_btn":"Settings","firewall_settings_btn_label":"Open firewall settings","firewall_settings_observe_label":"Observe mode","firewall_settings_webhook_label":"Approval webhook","firewall_settings_webhook_url_label":"Webhook URL (https)","firewall_settings_webhook_secret_label":"Webhook secret (HMAC)","firewall_settings_webhook_loading":"Webhook status is still loading — try again in a moment.","firewall_settings_webhook_status_error":"Couldn't load webhook status","firewall_settings_webhook_secret_required":"A webhook secret is required when setting the URL.","firewall_settings_webhook_hint":"POST a signed event to your agent runtime or an external system when a tool call is held for approval. URL and secret are both required to deliver.","firewall_settings_webhook_configured":"Configured","firewall_settings_webhook_none":"Not configured","firewall_settings_webhook_no_secret":"secret missing (won’t deliver)","firewall_settings_webhook_keep":"leave blank to keep","firewall_settings_webhook_secret_keep":"Configured — leave blank to keep","firewall_settings_webhook_secret_ph":"Shared HMAC secret","firewall_settings_webhook_disable":"Disable webhook (clear URL + secret)","firewall_settings_webhook_https_err":"Webhook URL must be an https:// URL.","firewall_settings_observe_hint":"Records unmatched tool calls as discovery events. Powers the Discovered tools inventory.","firewall_settings_window_label":"Discovery window","firewall_settings_window_body":"30 days, configurable via env in M3.","firewall_settings_retention_label":"Retention","firewall_settings_retention_body":"30 days TTL, configurable via env.","firewall_settings_confirm_off_title":"Turn observe mode off?","firewall_settings_confirm_off_body":"Discovered tools will stop updating. Existing events remain visible until they expire (30 days TTL). Are you sure?","firewall_settings_saved":"Settings saved","firewall_policies_create_blank":"Create blank policy","key_firewall_label":"Firewall policy","key_firewall_tip":"Tool-call policy enforced on this key. \"Workspace default / none\" uses the workspace default policy (if any).","key_firewall_none":"Workspace default / none","key_firewall_disabled_suffix":" (disabled)","admin_accounts_page_title":"Accounts","list_tab":"List","pool_create_btn":"New pool","pool_create_success":"Pool created","pool_create_title":"Create pool","pool_delete_btn":"Delete","pool_delete_confirm_body":"Routers referencing @pool:{{name}} will continue to work but stop applying that rule.","pool_delete_confirm_title":"Delete pool?","pool_delete_success":"Pool deleted","pool_edit_btn":"Edit","pool_edit_title":"Edit pool","pool_models_hint":"Whitespace is trimmed; duplicates removed; order preserved.","pool_models_label":"Models","pool_models_placeholder":"Comma-separated, e.g. openai/gpt-4o-mini, anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5","pool_name_hint":"Name is immutable after create. Referenced as @pool:\u003cname> in router fields.","pool_name_label":"Pool name","pool_name_placeholder":"lowercase, digits, underscores, hyphens (e.g. oss-cheap)","pool_save_btn":"Save","pool_save_success":"Pool saved","pools_card_models_empty":"(no models in this pool)","pools_empty_body":"Create a pool to reuse a model list across routers.","pools_empty_title":"No pools yet","pools_intro_banner":"Pools are workspace-scoped, named lists of models. Reference them in a router's allowed models, weak pool, or strong pool fields with @pool:\u003cname> instead of repeating the model list.","pools_nav_label":"Pools","pools_page_title":"Model pools","strategy_gated_adaptive_desc":"Mundane requests use the cheap pool, hard requests use the strong pool (experimental)","strategy_gated_adaptive_label":"Adaptive (gated)","firewall_policies_col_name":"Name","firewall_policies_col_status":"Status","firewall_policies_col_actions":"Actions","firewall_policy_status_enabled":"Enabled","firewall_policy_status_disabled":"Disabled","firewall_policy_edit_btn":"Edit","firewall_discovered_col_actions":"Actions","firewall_policy_editor_enabled_label":"Enabled","billing.autotopup_disabled_by_admin":"Auto-topup disabled by administrator","billing.error.auto_topup_invalid_enabled_disabled":"Auto-topup has been disabled by an administrator.","billing.error.auto_topup_invalid_amount_out_of_range":"Target amount is out of range. Please refresh and try again.","billing.error.auto_topup_invalid_threshold_out_of_range":"Trigger amount is out of range. Please refresh and try again.","billing.error.auto_topup_invalid_amount_must_exceed_threshold":"Target must be above trigger by the configured minimum. Please refresh and try again.","billing.error.no_stripe_customer":"No payment method on file. Add a card before enabling auto-topup.","billing.autotopup_turn_off":"Turn off","topup_next_tier_hint":"Top up ${{min}}+ to unlock +{{pct}}% bonus","billing.autotopup_allowed_range":"Allowed: ${{min}} – ${{max}}","billing.autotopup_save_blocked":"Fix the highlighted fields to enable Save","firewall_nav":"Firewall","firewall_save_failed":"Save failed","firewall_delete_failed":"Delete failed","firewall_rescan_failed":"Re-scan failed","firewall_rule_save_failed":"Rule save failed","firewall_default_promote_failed":"Default-promote failed","firewall_subtitle":"Tool-call policies enforced on every request. Precedence: key attachment → workspace default → observe mode.","firewall_help_title":"How Firewall works","firewall_help_section_discovered_title":"Discovered tools","firewall_help_section_discovered_body":"Every tool your agents call shows up here automatically — first seen, last seen, call volume, attributed keys. No rules to author up front; promote any tool to a deny or audit rule in one click. Powered by observe mode (on by default for every new workspace).","firewall_help_section_policies_title":"Policies","firewall_help_section_policies_body":"Named, reusable sets of tool-call rules. Attach a policy to a specific API key, or mark one as the workspace default. Each rule matches by tool-name glob and decides allow / audit / deny. First match wins, evaluated in priority order.","firewall_help_section_events_title":"Events","firewall_help_section_events_body":"Per-call audit feed: verdict, matched policy + rule, request id, surface, token. Filter by verdict or tool name to spot a misbehaving agent or to confirm a new rule is firing as intended. 30-day retention; cross-link to the request log via request_id.","firewall_help_guardrails_xlink":"For prompt and response text policies, see Guardrails →","firewall_help_learn_more":"Learn more →","firewall_help_button_aria":"How Firewall works","firewall_discard_changes_title":"Discard unsaved changes?","firewall_discard_changes_body":"You have unsaved edits in this policy. Closing will lose them.","firewall_discard_changes_ok":"Discard","firewall_discard_changes_cancel":"Keep editing","firewall_policy_editor_shadow_preview_badge":"Preview","firewall_discard_rule_changes_body":"You have unsaved edits in this rule. Closing will lose them.","opens_in_new_tab":"(opens in new tab)","strategy_adaptive_standard_label":"Adaptive Standard","strategy_adaptive_gated_label":"Adaptive Gated","strategy_adaptive_standard_help":"Learns online across every allowed model. Considers your full allowed-models set per request and converges on the best option from real production traffic, weighing quality, cost, latency, and reliability. New routers behave like Balanced for the first ~10 picks per arm while data accumulates.","strategy_adaptive_gated_help":"Requests are first classified as mundane or hard, then drawn from the matching list (weak_pool / strong_pool). It then learns which model wins within the narrowed set. Best when your traffic mixes simple and complex calls. New routers behave like Balanced for the first ~10 picks per arm while data accumulates.","strategy_adaptive_gated_desc":"Difficulty-band learning with mundane / hard model lists","strategy_adaptive_standard_desc":"Online learning across your full allowed-models set","agent_firewall_nav":"Agent Firewall","agent_firewall_subtitle":"Policies enforced on every tool call. Precedence: key attachment → workspace default → observe mode. For prompt + response text, see Guardrails →","firewall_policy_editor_m3_badge":"M3","routing_dsl_insert_btn":"Insert","routing_dsl_insert_model":"Model…","routing_dsl_insert_pool":"Pool…","routing_dsl_insert_router":"Router…","routing_dsl_insert_router_modal_title":"Insert a router reference","routing_dsl_insert_router_empty":"No routers in this workspace yet.","routing_dsl_template_map_title":"Map \"{{name}}\" to your workspace","routing_dsl_template_map_hint":"This template uses tiered placeholders. Pick a real model from your workspace for each tier — the loaded ruleset will reference only these models so it lints clean.","routing_dsl_template_map_confirm":"Insert","routing_dsl_template_map_cancel":"Cancel","routing_dsl_tier_frontier":"Frontier (hard tasks)","routing_dsl_tier_balanced":"Balanced (default)","routing_dsl_tier_cheap":"Cheap / fast","routing_dsl_tier_long_ctx":"Long context","routing_dsl_generate_btn":"Generate with AI","routing_dsl_generate_hide_btn":"Hide AI generator","routing_dsl_generate_card_title":"Generate routing strategy","routing_dsl_generate_prompt_placeholder":"Describe what you want in plain English…","routing_dsl_generate_prompt_aria":"Routing strategy description","routing_dsl_generate_preview_aria":"Generated routing DSL preview","routing_dsl_generate_run_btn":"Generate","routing_dsl_generate_loading":"Generating…","routing_dsl_generate_apply_btn":"Apply","routing_dsl_generate_regenerate_btn":"Regenerate","routing_dsl_generate_discard_btn":"Discard","routing_dsl_generate_needs_save_first":"Save the router once before generating.","routing_dsl_generate_empty_prompt":"Describe the routing you want first.","routing_dsl_generate_error":"Could not generate a valid strategy. Try rephrasing.","routing_dsl_generate_lint_clean":"lint: clean","routing_dsl_generate_via":"via {{model}}","routing_dsl_help_title":"DSL in 60 seconds","routing_dsl_help_precedence":"Rules run top-to-bottom, first match wins. The first rule whose when: is true picks the model; if none match, the default: block decides.","routing_dsl_help_when":"when: is a CEL expression. Common patterns: task_class == \"code\", difficulty > 0.7, request.input_tokens > 100000, model == \"gpt-5\", agent_state.last_test_failed, tool_calls_present_any([\"Edit\",\"Write\"]).","routing_dsl_help_use":"use: picks exactly one effect: model: \"…\" (one model), pool: \"@pool:name\" (a saved list), model: \"orcarouter/name\" (another router), parallel: (ensemble + arbiter), or delegate: balanced (hand off to a preset strategy).","routing_dsl_help_stuck":"Stuck? Click Generate with AI to describe the routing in plain English, or open the ? Variable reference for every CEL identifier and macro.","routing_dsl_help_dismiss":"Dismiss","routing_dsl_explain_cap_source_bytes":"The ruleset source exceeds the size cap. Trim rules or shorten when: expressions — very large rulesets slow every request's evaluation.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_required_keys":"A required key is missing. Every rule needs an id and a use:; on_low_confidence needs signals: and use:. Add the missing key shown in the message.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_syntax":"The YAML could not be parsed. Check indentation (spaces, not tabs), matching quotes, and that list items line up under their key.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_type_check":"A value has the wrong type for its key (e.g. a string where a number is expected). Fix the value to match the key's expected type.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_version":"The version: header is missing or unsupported. Start the ruleset with version: 1.","routing_dsl_explain_cap_rules_count":"Too many rules. The ruleset is over the per-router rule cap — consolidate overlapping rules or move logic into a pool / nested router.","routing_dsl_explain_cap_when_length":"A when: expression is too long. Break the condition into a simpler predicate, or precompute the signal upstream.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_id_format":"Rule ids must match ^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,39}$ — start with a lowercase letter, then lowercase letters / digits / underscores only.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_reserved_id":"This rule id is reserved. \"default\" belongs to the top-level default: block, and ids starting with _ are reserved for system rules. Rename the rule.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_unique_id":"Two rules share the same id. Rule ids must be unique so coverage, traces, and jumps resolve to one rule — rename the duplicate.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_effect_exclusivity":"use: must set exactly one destination: one of model / models / pool / channels / parallel / delegate. Remove the extras so the effect is unambiguous.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_delegate_cycle":"delegate: dsl would route back into this DSL and loop forever. Delegate to a preset strategy instead (e.g. balanced, cheapest).","routing_dsl_explain_schema_delegate_enum":"delegate: must be one of cheapest | quality | balanced | linucb | gated_adaptive. Pick a valid preset.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_parallel_nesting":"parallel: cannot be nested inside another parallel: block. Flatten the ensemble to a single level.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_parallel_leg_count":"A parallel: ensemble needs a valid number of legs (within the min/max shown). Add or remove legs to fit the range.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_parallel_arbiter_required":"A parallel: ensemble needs an arbiter: to pick or combine the legs' answers. Add an arbiter block with a strategy.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_parallel_nil_leg":"A parallel: leg is empty (a null entry in the list). Give every leg a destination (e.g. a model) or remove the blank entry.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_arbiter_strategy":"arbiter.strategy must be best_of_n | majority | first | tests_pass. Pick one of the supported arbitration strategies.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_arbiter_judge_required":"arbiter.best_of_n needs a judge to score the candidates — set exactly one of pool / model / channel on the arbiter.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_arbiter_exclusivity":"The arbiter must set exactly one judge destination (pool / model / channel). Remove the extra ones.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_arbiter_orphan":"arbiter: is only valid alongside parallel:. Either add a parallel: block or remove the arbiter.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_knob_range":"A knob value is out of range (thinking_budget_tokens / samples / temperature / max_latency_ms). Bring it within the documented bounds shown in the message.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_knob_enum":"reasoning_effort must be one of low | medium | high. Pick a valid level.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_reason_tag_format":"reason_tag must match ^[a-z0-9_]+$ — lowercase letters, digits, and underscores only. Used for attribution in coverage / traces.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_signal_enum":"on_low_confidence.signals lists an unknown signal. Valid signals: patch_invalid, self_doubt, next_turn_test_failed, low_logprob.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_pool_prefix":"A pool reference must use the \"@pool:\u003cname>\" prefix. A bare name would be treated as a model — add the @pool: prefix.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_channel_prefix":"A channels entry must use the \"@channel:\u003cname>\" prefix so the lexer can tell it apart from a model name.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_cel_typecheck":"The when: expression failed CEL type-checking — usually an unknown identifier or a type mismatch. Check identifier spelling against the Variable reference (?).","routing_dsl_explain_schema_cel_output_bool":"A when: expression must evaluate to a boolean. e.g. write difficulty > 0.7, not just difficulty — a bare number isn't a condition.","routing_dsl_explain_schema_cel_compile":"The when: expression could not be compiled. Re-check the CEL syntax (operators, parentheses, quotes).","routing_dsl_explain_schema_cel_program":"The when: expression compiled but could not be turned into an executable program. Simplify the expression or check for unsupported constructs.","routing_dsl_explain_internal_cel_env":"An internal error occurred building the CEL environment. This is a server-side issue, not your ruleset — retry, and report it if it persists.","routing_dsl_explain_policy_header_override_denied":"header_override is trying to set a reserved / auth-bearing header. These are blocked so a rule can't subvert authentication. Remove the denied key.","routing_dsl_explain_policy_header_override_invalid":"A header_override key is not a valid HTTP header name (RFC 7230). Use letters, digits, and hyphens only.","routing_dsl_explain_policy_param_override_denied":"param_override is trying to rewrite a protected parameter (identity / routing / tool surface, e.g. model / stream / tools). These are blocked — remove the denied key.","routing_dsl_insert_pool_modal_title":"Insert pool reference","routing_dsl_insert_pool_empty":"No saved pools yet. Create one under Pools to insert it here.","routing_dsl_template_unknown_model":"rule references model \"{{name}}\" which is not in your workspace allow-set — replace via Insert → Model.","routing_dsl_fix_pick_model_btn":"Pick a model","routing_dsl_dryrun_model":"Model","routing_dsl_dryrun_model_auto":"auto (let the rules decide)","routing_dsl_dryrun_agent_state_title":"agent_state overrides","routing_dsl_dryrun_agent_turn":"turn","routing_dsl_dryrun_agent_has_edited":"has_edited","routing_dsl_dryrun_agent_has_run_tests":"has_run_tests","routing_dsl_dryrun_agent_last_test_failed":"last_test_failed","routing_dsl_dryrun_agent_consecutive_errors":"consecutive_errors","routing_dsl_dryrun_agent_tools_used":"tools_used","routing_dsl_dryrun_agent_tools_used_placeholder":"Press Enter to add a tool name (e.g. Read, Edit, Bash)","routing_dsl_dryrun_agent_models_tried":"models_tried","routing_dsl_dryrun_agent_models_tried_placeholder":"Models already invoked this session (for retry-diversity rules)","routing_dsl_explain_policy_parallel_gated":"Parallel rules require workspace opt-in. An admin must enable Workspace Settings → Routing → Allow parallel/ensemble rules before this ruleset can save.","routing_dsl_explain_advisory_parallel_first_leg_only":"Parallel fan-out and arbitration are implemented, but the relay runtime is gated behind the server flag ROUTING_DSL_ENSEMBLE_RUNTIME. With it off, the rule saves and only the first leg serves traffic.","routing_dsl_explain_advisory_cascade_not_yet_wired":"The confidence cascade (signals plus re-dispatch) is implemented, but the relay runtime is gated behind the server flag ROUTING_DSL_ENSEMBLE_RUNTIME. With it off, the spec saves but no re-route happens.","routing_dsl_explain_policy_channels_not_supported":"Channel pinning lands in Phase 4 — the syntax saves but the runtime currently degrades these rules to balanced routing within the candidate model set.","routing_dsl_explain_template_unknown_model":"The loaded template references a model that is not in your workspace allow-set. Click Fix to pick a real model from your workspace.","routing_dsl_insert_needs_caret":"Click in the editor to place the cursor first, then try Insert again.","routing_dsl_tests_btn":"Tests","routing_dsl_tests_needs_save_first":"Save the router once before editing test cases (the suite is stored per-router).","routing_dsl_trace_btn":"Trace","routing_dsl_trace_needs_save_first":"Save the router once before replaying a trace (traces are recorded per-router).","routing_dsl_coverage_title":"Rule coverage","routing_dsl_coverage_shadow_chip":"shadow","routing_dsl_coverage_canary_chip":"canary {{pct}}%","routing_dsl_coverage_refresh_btn":"Refresh","routing_dsl_coverage_fallthrough_chip":"Default fallthrough: {{pct}}% ({{count}})","routing_dsl_coverage_total":"{{count}} requests in window","routing_dsl_coverage_loading":"Loading coverage…","routing_dsl_coverage_empty":"No rule fires recorded yet in this window.","routing_dsl_coverage_load_failed":"Failed to load rule coverage.","routing_dsl_coverage_fires":"{{count}} fires","routing_dsl_coverage_dead_chip":"dead","routing_dsl_coverage_dead_tooltip":"Dead rule — never matched any request in this window. It may be shadowed by an earlier broader rule or have an impossible predicate.","routing_dsl_coverage_live_tooltip":"Active rule — matched at least one request in this window.","routing_dsl_coverage_dead_aria":"Dead rule indicator","routing_dsl_coverage_live_aria":"Active rule indicator","routing_dsl_run_all":"Run all","routing_dsl_tests_drawer_title":"Test cases","routing_dsl_tests_summary":"{{pass}}/{{total}} passed","routing_dsl_tests_hint":"Edit the YAML test suite, then Run all to evaluate each case against the live source.","routing_dsl_tests_editor_aria":"Routing DSL test cases YAML editor","routing_dsl_tests_loading":"Loading test cases…","routing_dsl_tests_save_btn":"Save suite","routing_dsl_tests_close_btn":"Close","routing_dsl_tests_saved":"Test suite saved.","routing_dsl_tests_save_failed":"Failed to save the test suite.","routing_dsl_tests_load_failed":"Failed to load the test suite.","routing_dsl_tests_run_failed":"Failed to run the test suite.","routing_dsl_tests_results_title":"Results","routing_dsl_tests_no_cases":"No cases in the suite yet.","routing_dsl_tests_case_pass":"pass","routing_dsl_tests_case_fail":"fail","routing_dsl_tests_case_error":"error","routing_dsl_tests_case_unnamed":"(unnamed case)","routing_dsl_tests_case_diff":"expected {{expected}}, got {{actual}}","routing_ds