— satisfied by process","compliance_attest_manage":"Manage","compliance_attest_btn":"Attest","compliance_attest_manage_label":"Manage attestation for {{id}}","compliance_attest_label":"Attest {{id}}","compliance_attest_title":"Attest control","compliance_attest_owner":"Owner email","compliance_attest_statement":"How is this control satisfied?","compliance_attest_evidence":"Evidence link or note (optional)","compliance_attest_expires":"Valid until (optional)","compliance_attest_submit":"Attest","compliance_attest_remove":"Remove attestation","compliance_attest_org_hint":"This control can’t be gateway-enforced. Attest that you satisfy it by process and attach evidence — it’s then credited (not a gap) in your report.","compliance_attested_by":"Attested by {{email}}","compliance_attest_success":"Control attested.","compliance_attest_error":"Attestation failed.","compliance_attest_removed":"Attestation removed. The control is a gap again.","compliance_report_include_pii":"Include full member details (PII)","compliance_report_include_pii_hint":"Off by default — member and admin emails are masked in the export. Turn on only if your audit requires full identifiers.","compliance_fw_reviewed":"Reviewed {{date}}","compliance_fw_effective":"Regulation effective {{date}}","compliance_enforcing":"Enforcing","compliance_enforce_label":"Turn on","compliance_enforce_tooltip":"Turn on enforcement — start blocking in production","compliance_enforce_admin":"Admin or owner role required to enforce.","compliance_enforce_aria":"Turn on enforcement for {{name}}","compliance_enforcing_aria":"{{name}} is enforcing","compliance_manage_controls":"Manage controls","compliance_manage_controls_hint":"Edit the Guardrails & Firewall policies these packs create.","compliance_page_title":"Compliance & AI Governance","compliance_page_subtitle":"Coverage = automated runtime controls only — not a certification.","compliance_plan_free":"Free","compliance_plan_paid":"Paid","compliance_plan_observing":"Observing","compliance_window_label":"Time window","compliance_coverage_state_filter":"Filter by coverage state","compliance_fw_all":"All","compliance_fw_switcher_label":"Active frameworks","compliance_viewer_banner":"You have view-only access. Contact your workspace admin to install or configure compliance packs.","compliance_loading":"Loading…","compliance_posture_section":"Posture","compliance_would_block_label":"events would have been BLOCKED","compliance_in_n_requests":"in {{n}} requests","compliance_no_events":"No would-block events in this window","compliance_install_hint":"Install a framework pack to start observing.","compliance_golive_cta":"Go live to block these","compliance_portfolio_label":"Framework coverage","compliance_risk_radar_section":"Top Risks","compliance_top_risks_title":"Top Risks","compliance_ranked_cross_fw":"Ranked · cross-framework deduplicated · {{window}}","compliance_no_risks":"No risks observed in this window.","compliance_view_matches_for":"View matches for {{label}}","compliance_fix_rule_for":"Fix rule for {{label}}","compliance_risk_view":"view","compliance_risk_fix":"fix","compliance_risk_rank":"Rank {{n}}","compliance_coverage_section":"Control Coverage","compliance_coverage_title":"Control Coverage","compliance_gaps_disclosed":"{{n}} gaps disclosed","compliance_coverage_scope_note":"Coverage = automated runtime controls only — not a certification.","compliance_coverage_search":"Search clause or control…","compliance_filter_all_states":"All states","compliance_state_observe":"Observing","compliance_state_covered":"Covered","compliance_state_gap":"Gap","compliance_state_drift":"Drift — rule edited","compliance_no_coverage_match":"No rows match the current filters.","compliance_no_coverage":"No coverage data — install a framework pack to begin.","compliance_col_clause":"Clause","compliance_col_control":"Control","compliance_col_plane":"Plane","compliance_col_mapped_by":"Mapped by","compliance_col_observe_count":"Would-block","compliance_col_state":"State","compliance_edit_rule":"Edit rule for {{id}}","compliance_edit":"Edit →","compliance_gap_badge":"Manual","compliance_gap_manual_title":"Manual or organizational control — not automated","compliance_plane_guardrail":"Guardrail","compliance_plane_firewall":"Firewall","compliance_evidence_section":"Live Evidence","compliance_evidence_title":"Live Evidence","compliance_evidence_admin_full":"Raw (admin)","compliance_evidence_redacted":"Redacted","compliance_evidence_redacted_hint":"Raw content is admin-only","compliance_no_evidence":"No match evidence in this window.","compliance_evidence_events":"events / {{window}}","compliance_evidence_sample_note":"Sample only. Content redacted for privacy.","compliance_open_matches_feed":"Open full matches feed","compliance_evidence_open_matches":"Open full matches feed →","compliance_library_section":"Add Frameworks","compliance_library_title":"Add Frameworks","compliance_library_sub":"Install free to observe. Go live (paid) to enforce.","compliance_library_search":"Search frameworks…","compliance_library_no_results":"No frameworks match your search.","compliance_library_empty":"No frameworks available.","compliance_library_readonly":"Admin or owner role required to install frameworks.","compliance_fw_controls":"{{n}} controls","compliance_mapped_by":"Mapped by: {{name}}","compliance_fw_enforcing":"Enforcing","compliance_fw_observing":"Observing","compliance_fw_install_btn":"Install (observe)","compliance_install_observe":"Install {{name}} in observe mode","compliance_overlap_hint":"Map once · comply many","compliance_overlap_hint_full":"Frameworks share controls — map once, comply many","compliance_install_success":"{{name}} installed in observe mode.","compliance_install_error":"Install failed.","compliance_golive_modal_title":"Go Live: {{name}}","compliance_golive_impact_section":"Impact preview","compliance_golive_impact_title":"What gets protected","compliance_golive_would_block":"events / {{window}} will be blocked","compliance_golive_no_events":"No would-block events observed yet. You can still go live to start enforcing.","compliance_golive_canary_note":"Start with a low-traffic API key to canary this policy before applying account-wide. You can revert by uninstalling the pack at any time.","compliance_golive_set_default":"Set as workspace default guardrail","compliance_golive_replace_warning":"This will replace the current default \"{{name}}\". Existing keys using it will switch to this policy.","compliance_golive_confirm_replace":"I understand and confirm the replacement","compliance_golive_upgrade_title":"Paid plan required","compliance_golive_upgrade_body":"Enforcing policies requires a Team or higher plan. Upgrade to go live.","compliance_golive_upgrade_btn":"Upgrade plan","compliance_golive_confirm_btn":"Go live","compliance_golive_upgrade_required":"Upgrade to go live","compliance_golive_cancel":"Cancel","compliance_golive_confirm_label":"Confirm go live for {{name}}","compliance_golive_success":"{{name}} is now enforcing.","compliance_golive_success_replaced":"{{name}} is now enforcing. Replaced \"{{old}}\".","compliance_golive_error":"Go live failed.","compliance_header_golive":"Go live","compliance_report_section":"Reports","compliance_report_title":"Evidence Reports","compliance_report_free_label":"1 free PDF (watermarked)","compliance_report_generate_btn":"Generate report","compliance_report_refresh":"Refresh","compliance_report_scope_note":"Reports capture a point-in-time snapshot of gateway controls and match evidence. Coverage = automated runtime controls only — not a certification.","compliance_report_no_reports":"No reports yet. Generate one to get an auditor-ready PDF.","compliance_report_col_framework":"Framework","compliance_report_col_period":"Period","compliance_report_col_format":"Format","compliance_report_col_status":"Status","compliance_report_col_created":"Created","compliance_report_all_fw":"All","compliance_report_status_pending":"Pending","compliance_report_status_generating":"Generating","compliance_report_status_ready":"Ready","compliance_report_status_failed":"Failed","compliance_report_polling":"Checking for updates…","compliance_report_download":"Download","compliance_report_download_label":"Download report {{id}}","compliance_report_admin_only":"Admin only","compliance_report_failed":"Failed","compliance_report_hash_note":"Reports include a SHA-256 content hash for tamper-evidence.","compliance_report_gen_modal_title":"Generate Compliance Report","compliance_report_framework_label":"Framework","compliance_report_no_framework":"All frameworks (gap report)","compliance_report_framework_required":"Select a framework to generate a report.","compliance_report_no_packs":"Install a framework pack before generating a report.","compliance_report_format_label":"Format","compliance_paid":"Paid","compliance_free_badge":"Free","compliance_report_queued":"Report generation started.","compliance_report_error":"Failed to start report generation.","compliance_report_gen_submit":"Generate","compliance_report_limit_free":"Free plan allows 1 report. Upgrade for unlimited reports.","compliance_report_format_paid":"CSV and JSON export requires a paid plan.","compliance_report_free_limit_banner":"Free plan allows 1 report. Upgrade for unlimited generation and export.","compliance_report_download_admin_only":"Report download is restricted to admins.","compliance_report_download_failed":"Download failed.","guardrail_source_col":"Source","guardrail_source_custom":"Custom","guardrail_source_pack_hint":"Installed via compliance pack {{key}}","range_max_n_days":"Date range cannot exceed {{n}} days","theme_light":"Light","theme_dark":"Dark","theme_system":"System","theme_switch":"Switch theme","act3_b2_title":"Pay once. Reuse for free.","act3_b2_desc":"Repeated and cached prompt tokens bill at the provider's cache rate — often a fraction of the input price — across 5-minute and 1-hour ephemeral windows. Same answers, less spend, with cached_tokens on every receipt.","act1_b1_paper":"Read the paper · arXiv →","sdk_title":"Works with the tools you already use","model_new_badge":"NEW","blog_strip_tag":"From the blog","blog_strip_title":"Fresh from the engine room.","blog_strip_sub":"What we're building and why — our latest posts.","blog_strip_all":"All posts →","faq_tag":"FAQ","faq_title":"AI routers, LLM gateways, adaptive routing — answered.","faq_sub":"Short, factual answers — the same set search engines see in this page's structured data.","faq_q_ai_router":"What is an AI router?","faq_a_ai_router":"An AI router sits between your app and many models and picks the best model for each request. OrcaRouter grades every prompt in under 1 ms and routes it — frontier for hard reasoning, open-source for routine — across 200+ models at zero token markup.","faq_q_llm_router":"What is an LLM router and how does it work?","faq_a_llm_router":"An LLM router classifies each prompt and matches it to the model most likely to answer well at the lowest cost. OrcaRouter routes on contextual embeddings with online learning from live traffic — 75.5% accuracy on the public RouterArena leaderboard.","faq_q_ai_gateway":"Is OrcaRouter an AI gateway?","faq_a_ai_gateway":"Yes. OrcaRouter is a production AI gateway: one OpenAI-compatible endpoint with adaptive routing, load balancing, automatic failover, guardrails, an agent firewall, prompt caching and per-request observability.","faq_q_ai_cdn":"What is an AI CDN?","faq_a_ai_cdn":"Like a CDN serves content from the best edge, an AI CDN serves inference from the best provider: healthy, fast, cheap capacity, cached repeated prompts, failover on outages. OrcaRouter plays this role across 200+ models.","faq_q_adaptive_routing":"What is adaptive routing?","faq_a_adaptive_routing":"Adaptive routing learns the quality/cost trade-off from your own traffic. Point each workspace at cheapest-that-clears-the-bar, highest quality, or balanced — or let orcarouter/auto keep tuning the choice per request.","faq_q_gateway_vs_router":"Do I need both an AI gateway and an LLM router?","faq_a_gateway_vs_router":"They solve different problems — governance vs model choice — but you don't need two systems: OrcaRouter routes per request and enforces budgets, guardrails and observability on the same hop.","faq_q_latency":"Does routing add latency?","faq_a_latency":"Prompt grading takes under 1 ms and total added latency stays under 50 ms — usually won back many times over by faster providers and cached prompt tokens.","faq_q_markup":"Does OrcaRouter mark up token prices?","faq_a_markup":"No. You pay each provider's published rate; OrcaRouter adds $0 per token and monetizes optional Team and Enterprise features.","faq_q_openai_sdk":"Can I keep my existing OpenAI SDK code?","faq_a_openai_sdk":"Yes — switch base_url to https://api.orcarouter.ai/v1 and your OpenAI, Anthropic or Google SDK code keeps working: Chat Completions, Responses, Embeddings, Images, Audio and streaming.","faq_q_provider_down":"What happens when a provider goes down?","faq_a_provider_down":"OrcaRouter retries against healthy fallback capacity for the same or an equivalent model before the response starts, so upstream outages don't surface to your users.","compliance_strip_desc":"Independently audited, continuously compliant — reports available under NDA.","feat_slide_prev":"Previous feature","feat_slide_next":"Next feature","feat_slide_to":"Go to slide {{n}}","hero_eyebrow_triad":"Zero Markup. Higher Availability. Better Prices.","hero_h1_smarter":"Smarter.","hero_h1_safer":"Safer.","hero_h1_cheaper":"Cost-efficient.","hero_sub_triad":"OrcaRouter grades every prompt and routes it intelligently. Frontier-quality AI at up to 40% lower cost. Adaptive routing, load balancing, guardrails, agent firewall, observability, and governance — all through a single OpenAI-compatible endpoint.","hero_code_caption":"One line. We grade each prompt, route to frontier or OSS, and add $0.","bridge_title":"More than a router.","bridge_sub":"OrcaRouter is the AI gateway for production — adaptive routing, observability, management, and governance behind one OpenAI-compatible endpoint.","bridge_pillar_smarter":"Smarter","bridge_pillar_safer":"Safer","bridge_pillar_cheaper":"Cost-efficient","bridge_pillar_note":"every request, by default — one gateway","act1_label":"Smarter","act1_b1_title":"Routing that's measurably more accurate.","act1_b1_desc":"Every prompt is embedded and routed by a model that keeps learning online from real traffic. On the public RouterArena leaderboard (Jun 2026) it leads on accuracy — ahead of GPT-5, Azure, Martian and NotDiamond — at 75.5%.","act1_b1_link":"Open source · Self-host · Reproduce it →","act1_b2_title":"See everything. Prove anything.","act1_b2_desc":"See exactly what every request cost, which model served it, how long it took, and why it failed — full structured logs you can filter, replay, and copy as a runnable cURL. A route is never a black box.","act1_b3_title":"Change prompts. Not code.","act1_b3_desc":"Version prompts behind named labels with A/B splits and one-click rollback. Move a label and every request picks it up instantly — no redeploy, no code change, no client update.","act2_label":"Safer","act2_b1_title":"A provider goes down. No one notices.","act2_b1_desc":"When a provider rate-limits or 5xxs, OrcaRouter retries the request against a healthy model across 200+ options before the response starts — so transient upstream outages don't surface to your users.","act2_b2_title":"Guardrails that stop things.","act2_b2_desc":"PII Shield and content policies run before the upstream call is billed. A blocked request returns a clean 400 and is never charged — guardrails enforced inline, not logged after the fact.","act2_b3_title":"Safe for your team. And your agents.","act2_b3_desc":"Budgets and roles for people; a risk-scored firewall for agents. Every tool and MCP call is graded ALLOW, REVIEW, or BLOCK before it runs, and anomaly detection flags rate and cost spikes against learned hour-of-week baselines.","act2_b3_note":"Built for the agent era. Before you needed it.","act3_label":"Cost-efficient","act3_b1_title":"Zero markup. Zero black boxes.","act3_b1_desc":"You pay each provider their exact price — we add $0 per token, ever. Every request shows the grade, chosen model, provider, latency, and price, so cost is glass-box, not an opaque blended rate.","act3_pricelist_title":"Every model. One price list.","act3_pricelist_desc":"200+ models with live, side-by-side pricing — what you'd pay the provider directly. We add $0 on top.","cta_title_triad":"Smarter, safer, cost-efficient.","cta_migration":"Swap one line. That's the migration.","cta_sub":"Sign up with GitHub — no credit card required. You're live in under a minute.","billing.payment_history_col_actions":"Actions","billing.invoice_request_btn":"Request invoice","billing.invoice_view_btn":"View invoice","billing.invoice_modal_title":"Issue invoice","billing.invoice_company_label":"Company name","billing.invoice_taxid_label":"VAT / Tax ID","billing.invoice_taxid_type_label":"Tax ID type","billing.invoice_submit":"Issue invoice","billing.invoice_skip_vat":"Issue without VAT","billing.invoice_success":"Invoice issued. Opening it in a new tab…","billing.invoice_error":"Could not issue the invoice. Please try again.","insights_trace_tree_disabled_title":"Trace capture isn’t enabled","insights_trace_tree_disabled_desc":"Trace capture isn’t available for this workspace right now. Ask an admin to enable agent-run tracing.","firewall_mcp_delete_failed":"Delete failed","firewall_mcp_save_failed":"Save failed","firewall_mcp_edit":"Edit","firewall_mcp_delete":"Delete","firewall_mcp_edit_title":"Edit MCP server","firewall_mcp_updated":"MCP server updated","firewall_mcp_deleted":"MCP server deleted","firewall_mcp_delete_title":"Delete MCP server?","firewall_mcp_delete_body":"This removes the registration. Agents can no longer reach its tools through the gateway.","firewall_mcp_endpoint_keep":"Leave blank to keep current","firewall_mcp_auth_keep":"Leave blank to keep stored credentials","firewall_mcp_field_enabled":"Enabled (load this server in the gateway)","firewall_mcp_name_no_dot":"Name cannot contain \".\" — it is the tool namespace separator.","key_firewall_gateway_label":"Firewall gateway (MCP)","key_firewall_gateway_enable":"Enable MCP gateway access","key_firewall_gateway_tip":"Lets this key connect to the MCP gateway (/api/v1/firewall/mcp) and proxy agent tool calls through your firewall. Admin only.","firewall_mcp_col_actions":"Actions","firewall_mcp_probe":"Probe","firewall_mcp_probing":"Probing…","firewall_mcp_tools":"Tools","firewall_mcp_probe_failed":"Couldn’t reach","firewall_mcp_never_checked":"never","firewall_mcp_connect_title":"Connect agents","firewall_mcp_connect_desc":"Point your MCP client at this gateway. Every tool call is checked by your firewall rules before it reaches the upstream server.","firewall_mcp_copy":"Copy","firewall_mcp_copied":"Copied","firewall_mcp_gateway_key":"firewall-gateway API key","firewall_mcp_create_token":"Create a gateway API key →","firewall_activity_run_scope_banner":"Showing events for run {{rid}}","firewall_activity_session_scope_banner":"Showing events for session {{sid}}","firewall_activity_scope_clear":"Back to rollup","firewall_today_guardrails_title":"Guardrails","firewall_today_guardrails_desc":"Content & prompt safety","firewall_skill_delete_confirm_title":"Delete skill?","firewall_skill_delete_confirm_body":"This removes the skill. Its tools are no longer governed by its mode.","firewall_skill_deleted":"Skill deleted","firewall_anomaly_retry_loop":"retry loop: {{tool}} called {{count}}× with identical args from {{token}}","firewall_anomaly_novel_path":"unfamiliar tool path: {{tool}} (seen {{count}}×)","firewall_today_alert_me":"Alert me","firewall_today_alerts_on":"Alerts on","firewall_today_alerts_blocked":"Blocked","firewall_activity_group_help_title":"What do these grouping options mean?","firewall_activity_group_help_source_label":"Source","firewall_activity_group_help_source":"the skill / MCP server / source that owns the call.","firewall_activity_group_help_run_label":"Run","firewall_activity_group_help_run":"one full agent execution (a single task; can span several model steps).","firewall_activity_group_help_session_label":"Session","firewall_activity_group_help_session":"a conversation that can contain multiple runs.","firewall_activity_group_help_none_label":"None","firewall_activity_group_help_none":"the flat event list (one row per call).","insights_trace_tree_legend":"Each row is a step (one model turn); nested rows are the tool calls it made.","firewall_autonomy_seg_custom":"Custom","subscription_credits_never_expire":"credits never expire","hero_h1_gateway":"One Gateway. Every Model.","hero_h1_promise":"Route Smarter. Ship Safer. Spend Less.","hero_paper":"Research Paper","pillar_route":"Route","pillar_observe":"Observe","pillar_manage":"Manage","pillar_govern":"Govern","pillar_route_sub":"Smart routing and automatic failover on every request.","pillar_observe_sub":"See and prove every call — cost, model, latency, and why.","pillar_manage_sub":"Versioned prompts and caching — without a redeploy.","pillar_govern_sub":"Guardrails, budgets, and an agent firewall that enforces.","feat_heading":"AI gateway for production","sdk_eyebrow":"Integrations","sdk_mcp":"OrcaRouter MCP server","act1_b1_note":"* Based on RouterArena leaderboard data, June 2026.","sdk_more":"and more","sdk_sub":"Drop-in OpenAI-compatible, or connect agents over the OrcaRouter MCP server — keep your SDK, framework and editor.","firewall_activity_trace_session":"Session {{key}} · {{runs}} runs · {{calls}} calls","firewall_activity_trace_run":"Run {{key}} · {{calls}} calls","firewall_mcp_copy_config":"Copy config","firewall_mcp_connect_collapsed":"Agents connect to your firewall gateway.","firewall_mcp_flow_agent":"Your agent","firewall_mcp_flow_gateway":"Firewall gateway","firewall_mcp_flow_sources":"Tool servers","firewall_activity_summary_view":"Summary view","request_logs.setting_record_ip":"Record client IP","request_logs.setting_record_ip_hint":"Store the caller's IP address on captured request logs. Off by default.","request_logs.setting_readonly_notice":"Only workspace owners and admins can change these settings. You have read-only access.","routing_dsl_mechanic_stage_specialization":"stage specialization","routing_dsl_mechanic_ensemble_gating":"ensemble gating","routing_dsl_mechanic_task_classification":"task classification","routing_dsl_mechanic_long_context_routing":"long-context routing","routing_dsl_mechanic_agent_gating":"agent gating","routing_dsl_mechanic_policy_guards":"policy guards","routing_dsl_mechanic_size_shape_gates":"size/shape gates","routing_dsl_mechanic_mechanic_4_5_diversity_retry":"Mechanic 4/5 — diversity & retry","routing_dsl_mechanic_tenant_gating":"tenant gating","routing_dsl_mechanic_time_of_day_routing":"time-of-day routing","routing_dsl_mechanic_mechanic_2_planning_detection":"Mechanic 2 — planning detection","routing_dsl_mechanic_mechanic_2_task_tool_detection":"Mechanic 2 — Task-tool detection","routing_dsl_mechanic_mechanic_1_3_localize_patch_detection":"Mechanic 1/3 — localize / patch detection","routing_dsl_mechanic_verification_step_detection":"verification step detection","routing_dsl_mechanic_client_version_gating":"client/version gating","routing_dsl_mechanic_schema":"schema","routing_dsl_mechanic_destination":"destination","routing_dsl_mechanic_phase_4_ensembles":"Phase 4 — ensembles","routing_dsl_mechanic_fallback":"fallback","routing_dsl_mechanic_observability":"observability","routing_dsl_mechanic_knob_override":"knob override","routing_dsl_mechanic_request_shaping":"request shaping","routing_dsl_mechanic_mechanic_3_cascade":"Mechanic 3 — cascade","routing_dsl_var_task_class_desc":"Classified task shape: chat | code | agent | vision | audio | rag | creative","routing_dsl_var_difficulty_desc":"Heuristic difficulty score from FeatureVector","routing_dsl_var_code_keyword_density_desc":"Fraction of code-like tokens (identifiers, brackets, keywords) in the prompt","routing_dsl_var_reasoning_cue_count_desc":"Count of reasoning cue tokens (\"think\", \"step by step\", \"plan\", etc.)","routing_dsl_var_log_prompt_tokens_desc":"Natural log of prompt token count — useful for size-tiered gates","routing_dsl_var_has_tools_desc":"True if the request declares any tools/functions","routing_dsl_var_tool_count_desc":"Number of tool definitions in the request","routing_dsl_var_model_desc":"Originally-requested model id (before routing)","routing_dsl_var_request_desc":"Request envelope: input_tokens, stream, max_tokens, etc.","routing_dsl_var_agent_state_desc":"Per-conversation memory: turn, has_edited, models_tried, last_test_failed, etc.","routing_dsl_var_headers_desc":"HTTP request headers (read-only)","routing_dsl_var_user_desc":"Authenticated user metadata: id, role, group","routing_dsl_var_token_desc":"API token metadata: id, name, group","routing_dsl_var_time_desc":"Time context: hour (0-23), weekday (0-6), unix","routing_dsl_var_workspace_desc":"Workspace context: id, plan_tier","routing_dsl_var_system_prompt_matches_desc":"True when the system prompt matches the given regex","routing_dsl_var_user_message_matches_desc":"True when the latest user message matches the given regex","routing_dsl_var_tool_definitions_include_desc":"True when the request declares a tool with the given name","routing_dsl_var_tool_calls_present_any_desc":"True when ANY of the named tools was called in this turn","routing_dsl_var_tool_results_from_any_desc":"True when a tool RESULT message from any of the named tools is present","routing_dsl_var_header_matches_desc":"True when the named header value matches the regex","routing_dsl_var_id_desc":"Rule identifier (^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,39}$). Must be unique in the ruleset.","routing_dsl_var_when_desc":"Boolean CEL expression. Rule fires when the result is true.","routing_dsl_var_use_desc":"Effect block. Exactly one of: pool / model / models / channels / parallel / delegate.","routing_dsl_var_pool_desc":"Reference to a workspace saved list. Must use the @pool: prefix.","routing_dsl_var_models_desc":"Explicit candidate set passed to the upstream picker.","routing_dsl_var_channels_desc":"Pin the request to specific channel deployments. Each @channel:\u003cname> must resolve to exactly ONE enabled channel of that name in the workspace group; an ambiguous (non-unique name) or missing ref degrades the route to balanced. Channel selection AND retry failover are constrained to the resolved set.","routing_dsl_var_parallel_desc":"Fan-out: 2..5 legs. Requires arbiter:. Workspace flag RoutingDSLAllowParallel must be on.","routing_dsl_var_arbiter_desc":"Judge/aggregator for parallel legs. strategy: best_of_n|majority|first|tests_pass|synthesize.","routing_dsl_var_delegate_desc":"Hand off to a built-in strategy: cheapest|quality|balanced|linucb|gated_adaptive.","routing_dsl_var_reason_tag_desc":"Audit tag attached to the routing decision. Surfaces in analytics.","routing_dsl_var_reasoning_effort_desc":"Override reasoning effort: low|medium|high. Maps to provider-specific knobs.","routing_dsl_var_thinking_budget_tokens_desc":"Override extended-thinking budget (Anthropic / Gemini). 1024..64000.","routing_dsl_var_samples_desc":"Override n (sample count). 1..16.","routing_dsl_var_model_rewrite_desc":"Send the request to the upstream under a different model name. Gated against the rule's resolved candidate set, so it can't escalate to an unauthorized model.","routing_dsl_var_affinity_ttl_desc":"Channel stickiness: pin the session to the channel that first served it for this window, e.g. \"30s\", \"5m\" (1s..6h). Keyed by the DSL session id (X-OrcaRouter-Session-Id) — without that header it no-ops.","routing_dsl_var_temperature_desc":"Override sampling temperature. 0..2.","routing_dsl_var_max_latency_ms_desc":"Soft deadline for the rule. parallel: races legs against this budget.","routing_dsl_var_on_low_confidence_desc":"Cascade: re-route when one of the listed signals fires after the primary use.","routing_dsl_var_on_disagreement_desc":"Parallel escalation: when a majority arbiter finds no strict majority among the legs, re-dispatch this higher-effort use and serve it instead. Direct model:/models: only (depth 1). Runtime gated behind ROUTING_DSL_ENSEMBLE_RUNTIME.","routing_dsl_var_signals_desc":"Cascade triggers: patch_invalid|self_doubt|next_turn_test_failed|low_logprob.","routing_dsl_var_threshold_desc":"Per-signal cascade thresholds inside on_low_confidence, e.g. { low_logprob: -1.5, self_doubt: 2 }. Read by the post-response signal evaluator.","routing_dsl_var_strategy_desc":"Arbiter strategy: best_of_n (judge picks one leg) | majority (vote) | first (race) | tests_pass (tests decide) | synthesize (aggregator fuses legs into a new answer; OpenAI-format clients only, charges N+1).","routing_dsl_var_template_desc":"Named judge/aggregator prompt template (best_of_n: swe_patch_judge_v1 | localize_file_vote_v1; synthesize: synthesize_v1).","routing_dsl_var_version_desc":"DSL schema version. Currently 1.","routing_dsl_var_rules_desc":"Ordered ruleset. First match (by id) wins.","routing_dsl_var_default_desc":"Fallback when no rule matches. Typical: { delegate: balanced }.","routing_dsl_var_header_override_desc":"Inject/replace request headers. Auth-bearing names are denied at lint AND runtime.","routing_dsl_var_param_override_desc":"Inject/replace request body keys. Identity/routing/tool keys are denied.","usage_tab_label":"Usage & ROI","usage_no_data":"No data","usage_loading":"Loading…","usage_empty_title":"No usage tracked yet","usage_empty_desc":"Once your API keys make requests, this tab breaks down where the spend goes, when, and the return on it.","usage_exec_loading":"Summarizing your usage…","usage_exec_spend_line":"Spent {{spend}} across {{count}} use cases","usage_exec_saved_line":"saved {{pct}} vs list","usage_exec_forecast_under":"forecast {{forecast}} ({{pct}} under budget)","usage_exec_forecast_over":"forecast {{forecast}} ({{pct}} over budget)","usage_exec_top_return":"Top return \"{{name}}\" {{roi}} ROI","usage_exec_success":"{{pct}} success","usage_exec_flag_near_cap":"{{n}} key near cap","usage_exec_flag_idle":"{{n}} idle","usage_exec_flag_spike":"{{n}} spend spike","usage_kpi_roi":"Blended ROI","usage_kpi_forecast":"Forecast vs budget","usage_reliability_label":"Reliability","usage_reliability_aria":"Production reliability","usage_reliability_success":"Success {{pct}}","usage_reliability_errors":"Errors {{n}} ({{spend}} charged)","usage_reliability_p95":"p95 {{ms}}","usage_reliability_retries":"retries {{n}}","usage_savings_title":"How OrcaRouter pays for itself","usage_savings_summary":"List {{list}} = Paid + Saved {{saved}} ({{pct}})","usage_savings_paid":"Paid","usage_savings_cache":"cache","usage_savings_routing":"routing","usage_savings_aria":"Spend breakdown: paid {{paid}}, cache savings {{cache}}, routing savings {{routing}}","usage_burndown_title":"Budget pacing (burn-down)","usage_burndown_actual":"Cumulative spend","usage_burndown_budget":"Budget","usage_burndown_aria":"Cumulative spend versus budget over the period","usage_burndown_pace":"day {{day}}/{{total}} · {{pct}} spent","usage_burndown_on_track":"on track","usage_burndown_over_pace":"over pace","usage_trend_title":"Monthly spend (last 6 months)","usage_trend_spend":"Spend","usage_trend_save_rate":"save-rate","usage_trend_aria":"Monthly spend over the last six months","usage_dimension_aria":"Break down usage by","usage_dim_key":"API key","usage_dim_member":"Member","usage_dim_task":"Task","usage_dim_environment":"Environment","usage_dim_app":"App","usage_dim_app_hint":"Source application self-reported by the client — informational only, not used for billing.","usage_metric_aria":"Heatmap metric","usage_metric_spend":"Spend","usage_metric_reqs":"Reqs","usage_metric_tokens":"Tokens","usage_heatmap_empty_title":"No usage yet","usage_heatmap_empty_desc":"Once your keys start making requests, a per-use-case heatmap appears here.","usage_heatmap_aria":"Usage heatmap of top use cases by day","usage_breakdown_title":"Breakdown","usage_col_use_case":"Use case / API key","usage_col_app":"App","usage_col_reqs":"Requests","usage_col_cost_per_req":"$/req","usage_col_spend":"Spend","usage_col_pct":"% of spend","usage_col_cache":"Cache saved","usage_col_value":"Value/mo","usage_col_roi":"ROI","usage_col_budget":"Budget used","usage_provider_title":"Provider mix & concentration","usage_provider_unknown":"unknown","usage_provider_concentration":"{{pct}} on a single provider — routing keeps several warm for resilience.","usage_activity_title":"When inference happens (UTC)","usage_activity_aria":"Activity by hour and weekday (UTC)","usage_activity_aria_peak":"Activity by hour and weekday (UTC); peak {{dow}} {{hour}}:00","usage_donut_title":"Spend split","usage_donut_others":"others","usage_donut_aria":"Spend split by use case","usage_attention_title":"Attention","usage_attention_active_keys":"Active keys {{active}}/{{total}}","usage_attention_idle":"{{n}} idle 30d+","usage_attention_near_cap":"Near cap \"{{name}}\" {{pct}}%","usage_attention_spike":"Spike {{date}} ~{{mult}}× baseline (est.){{driver}}","usage_attention_errors":"{{n}} failed requests","usage_attention_all_clear":"Nothing needs attention right now.","usage_opp_title":"Opportunities","usage_opp_total":"est. up to {{amt}}/mo","usage_opp_empty":"No optimisation opportunities detected.","usage_opp_est":"(est. {{low}}–{{high}}/mo)","usage_opp_disclaimer":"est. = heuristic; verify before acting.","usage_opp_idle":"\"{{label}}\" idle / no tagged value — review or decommission","usage_opp_cache":"\"{{label}}\" cache underused vs median — raise caching","usage_opp_model":"\"{{label}}\" high $/req for its task — try a cheaper model","usage_charged_disclaimer":"Spend is charged usage (sum of metered quota), not your invoice — promos, credits and rounding differ. Amount owed is in Billing.","usage_tag_section_title":"Usage & ROI","usage_tag_section_desc":"Tag this key with a use case and a monthly value/budget so the Usage & ROI tab can attribute spend and compute ROI.","usage_tag_use_case_label":"Use-case label","usage_tag_use_case_placeholder":"e.g. Support Copilot","usage_tag_value_label":"Monthly value","usage_tag_value_placeholder":"Monthly business value of this use case","usage_tag_value_extra":"Used to compute this key’s ROI (value ÷ spend).","usage_tag_budget_label":"Monthly budget","usage_tag_budget_placeholder":"Monthly spend target for this key","usage_tag_budget_extra":"Powers the budget burn-down and pacing.","usage_delta_vs_prior":"{{pct}}% vs prior","usage_delta_over":"{{pct}} over","usage_delta_under":"{{pct}} under","firewall_template_gallery_title":"Start from a template","firewall_template_gallery_subtitle":"Pick the agent's job — we preload rules tuned to its risks. You can edit everything before it goes live.","firewall_template_gallery_search_ph":"Search templates…","firewall_template_recommended":"Recommended","firewall_template_rules_count":"{{count}} rules","firewall_template_preview_btn":"Preview","firewall_template_covers":"Covers","firewall_template_preview_name":"Policy name","firewall_template_rule_col":"Rule","firewall_template_action_col":"Action","firewall_template_default_when_unmatched":"Default when nothing matches","firewall_template_apply_enforce":"Enforce now","firewall_template_apply_shadow":"Shadow mode — watch, don't block","firewall_template_apply_default":"Make this the workspace default","firewall_template_preview_back":"Back","firewall_template_preview_apply":"Apply","firewall_template_start_blank":"Start blank instead","firewall_template_empty":"No templates match your search.","firewall_template_apply_failed":"Could not apply template","firewall_template_applied_toast":"Applied \"{{name}}\" — {{count}} rules created","firewall_template_loading":"Loading…","firewall_template_apply_mode_label":"How to apply","firewall_template_caveat":"Heads up: argument rules assume common arg names (command/path/query/amount); egress & sequence rules enforce only when your gateway/SDK reports tool egress. Review and tune the rules for your tools before relying on them.","dashboard_tab_label":"Dashboard","dashboard_apps_spend_title":"Spend by app","dashboard_apps_spend_unknown":"Unknown","dashboard_apps_spend_other":"Other","dashboard_apps_spend_view_usage":"View in Usage","dashboard_apps_spend_empty":"No app data for this window","costs_tab_label":"Costs","costs_keys_help":"Your API keys ranked by spend this window.","costs_trend_granularity_aria":"Time granularity","costs_trend_unit_aria":"Metric","costs_trend_title":"Spend over time","costs_help_trend":"Spend, tokens or requests over time, split into cache vs non-cache. USD shows a single total (per-token $ split isn’t stored).","costs_gran_daily":"Daily","costs_gran_weekly":"Weekly","costs_gran_monthly":"Monthly","costs_unit_usd":"USD","costs_unit_tokens":"Tokens","costs_unit_requests":"Requests","costs_legend_cache":"Cache","costs_legend_noncache":"Non-cache","costs_avg_per_req":"Avg / req","costs_delta_pp":"{{pp}}pp vs prior","costs_metered_note":"Spend is charged (metered) usage — not your invoice. Promos, credits and rounding differ.","costs_see_billing":"See Billing →","costs_help_spend":"What you paid upstream providers at their published rates over the window — no markup.","costs_help_avg":"Average cost per API request: total spend ÷ requests.","costs_help_tokens":"All tokens processed over the window: input + output, including cached.","costs_help_projected":"Estimated spend for the full month at your current run-rate (month-to-date ÷ active days × days in month).","costs_help_cache_hit":"Share of input tokens served from cache (cache reads ÷ total input). Higher means lower cost.","costs_help_cache_saved":"Quota the cache-read discount saved versus paying full input price.","usage_opp_help":"Heuristic suggestions to cut spend without losing value — each shows an estimated monthly saving range. Verify before acting.","usage_savings_cache_help":"Saved by serving cached responses instead of re-calling the model.","usage_savings_routing_help":"Saved by routing to cheaper providers/models at zero markup.","usage_savings_help":"List price is the undiscounted upstream rate. You pay less via two separate savings — cache and routing — which together with Paid add up to List.","usage_breakdown_help":"Spend, efficiency and ROI for each row of the selected breakdown. Click an API-key row to drill into its usage.","usage_col_cost_per_req_help":"Average cost per request (spend ÷ requests).","usage_col_spend_help":"Charged usage (metered quota) for this row this period — not your invoice.","usage_col_cache_help":"Amount saved by serving cached responses instead of re-calling the model.","usage_col_value_help":"Monthly business value you tagged on this key — edit it in the key’s drawer. Drives ROI.","usage_col_roi_help":"Return on spend: tagged value ÷ spend.","usage_col_budget_help":"Share of this key’s monthly budget consumed. Amber ≥ 80%, red ≥ 100%.","usage_heatmap_title":"Top use cases by day","usage_heatmap_help":"Each row is a use case / key, each column a UTC day. Darker means more of the selected metric (spend, requests or tokens).","usage_reliability_help":"Production health this period — request success rate, latency, and retries. Operational (not financial), so it shows for everyone.","usage_reliability_errors_help":"Failed requests and what they cost — some providers still bill for errors.","usage_reliability_p95_help":"95th-percentile latency: 95% of requests responded faster than this.","usage_reliability_retries_help":"Automatic re-attempts after a failed upstream call. Lots of retries can signal an unstable provider.","usage_kpi_roi_help":"Return on AI spend: the business value you tagged on your API keys divided by what you paid this period. Set a key’s value in its settings.","usage_kpi_roi_basis":"value ÷ spend","usage_kpi_value":"Tagged value / mo","usage_kpi_value_help":"Total monthly business value you’ve assigned to API keys. It’s the numerator of ROI — set it per key in the key’s settings.","usage_kpi_value_basis":"assigned business value, per month","usage_kpi_forecast_help":"Spend projected to the end of this period at the current run-rate, shown against the monthly budget you set on your keys.","usage_kpi_forecast_basis":"projected spend vs budget","usage_heatmap_legend_less":"less","usage_heatmap_legend_more":"more","usage_provider_help":"Share of spend by upstream provider. Heavy reliance on one vendor is a resilience and pricing risk — routing keeps several warm.","usage_provider_subtitle":"share of spend by provider","usage_burndown_help":"Cumulative spend so far against your budget line. “On track” means you’re spending no faster than the budget allows for this point in the period.","usage_activity_help":"When requests happen. Rows are weekdays, columns are hours of the day (UTC). Darker means more requests.","usage_activity_insights_title":"When it’s busy","usage_activity_insights_help":"Derived from the grid — handy for scheduling batch jobs or shifting load into cheaper off-peak windows.","usage_activity_peak_label":"Busiest hour","usage_activity_busiest_day":"Busiest day","usage_activity_offhours":"Off-hours","usage_activity_offhours_sub":"outside 08:00–20:00 UTC","usage_activity_weekend":"Weekend","usage_exec_help":"ROI = tagged business value ÷ spend. Forecast is a run-rate projection of this period’s spend versus your budget. All figures are charged usage, not your invoice.","usage_intro_title":"The return on your AI spend","usage_intro_desc":"ROI, budget pacing, reliability and where to optimize. Raw spend, latency and per-key / per-model detail live on the Dashboard tab.","usage_trend_help":"Total spend per calendar month over the last six months — the long-term trend. The footer shows whether the latest month rose or fell versus the previous one.","usage_trend_mom":"Spend vs last month","usage_trend_save_rate_help":"Share of list price you saved that month.","usage_attention_help":"Things worth a look this period — idle keys, keys near their cap, spend spikes and errors.","usage_attention_idle_help":"Keys with no usage in 30+ days — review or revoke.","usage_attention_near_cap_help":"This key is close to its spending cap; raise the limit or it will start returning 402s.","usage_attention_spike_help":"A day whose spend was far above the period’s typical (baseline) daily spend. Heuristic — verify before acting.","usage_unit_aria":"Show usage in","usage_burndown_title_unit":"Usage pacing — {{unit}}","usage_burndown_pace_volume":"day {{day}}/{{total}} · {{amount}} so far","usage_trend_title_unit":"Monthly {{unit}} (last 6 months)","usage_trend_mom_unit":"{{unit}} vs last month","usage_burndown_help_unit":"Cumulative {{unit}} used so far over the selected period.","usage_burndown_aria_unit":"Cumulative {{unit}} over the period","usage_tag_save":"Save value & budget","usage_tag_saving":"Saving…","usage_tag_saved":"Value & budget updated","usage_tag_save_failed":"Could not save","firewall_template_baseline_all_agents_name":"Baseline (all agents)","firewall_template_coding_agent_name":"Coding / dev agent","firewall_template_customer_support_agent_name":"Customer-support agent","firewall_template_rag_research_agent_name":"RAG / research assistant","firewall_template_data_analytics_agent_name":"Data-analytics agent","firewall_template_devops_ops_agent_name":"DevOps / ops agent","firewall_template_browser_computer_use_agent_name":"Browser / computer-use agent","firewall_template_baseline_all_agents_desc":"Universal safety floor every agent should have: SSRF/metadata egress denylist, destructive-shell deny, secret-file deny, a lethal-trifecta exfil breaker, and a per-run cost cap.","firewall_template_coding_agent_desc":"For agents with shell, git, filesystem and CI tools. Blocks rm -rf, secret-file reads and web|sh pipes; gates force-push; breaks the GitHub issue→private-read→public-PR exfil flow; caps runaway loops.","firewall_template_customer_support_agent_desc":"For agents with refund, CRM, ticketing and email tools. Caps and gates refunds, masks PII (email/SSN/card) in tool traffic, gates bulk export and account-takeover actions, and breaks refund loops.","firewall_template_rag_research_agent_desc":"For agents with web-fetch, search and document-retrieval tools. Denies SSRF/metadata egress and non-http schemes, breaks retrieve→egress chains, and caps research loops.","firewall_template_data_analytics_agent_desc":"For agents with SQL, warehouse and export tools. Blocks destructive DDL and secret-table reads, gates DELETE/UPDATE and large exports, and breaks the inject→query→export→egress exfil chain.","firewall_template_devops_ops_agent_desc":"For agents with cloud CLI, Kubernetes, Terraform and secrets-manager tools. Blocks infra-destroy and recursive cloud/k8s deletes, gates terraform apply, IAM escalation and secret reads, and caps cost.","firewall_template_browser_computer_use_agent_desc":"For agents that drive a browser or desktop (click, type, navigate). Gates financial/irreversible clicks, blocks typing credentials and reading cookies/storage, denies SSRF navigation, and breaks page-read→egress chains.","firewall_template_baseline_all_agents_rule_10":"SSRF / cloud-metadata egress deny","firewall_template_baseline_all_agents_rule_20":"Destructive shell/command deny","firewall_template_baseline_all_agents_rule_30":"Secret-file read deny","firewall_template_baseline_all_agents_rule_40":"Lethal-trifecta exfil breaker","firewall_template_baseline_all_agents_rule_50":"Per-run cost cap ($10)","firewall_template_coding_agent_rule_10":"Block recursive delete (rm -rf)","firewall_template_coding_agent_rule_20":"Block web-pipe-to-shell","firewall_template_coding_agent_rule_30":"Deny secret-file reads","firewall_template_coding_agent_rule_40":"Gate force-push / reset --hard","firewall_template_coding_agent_rule_50":"GitHub toxic-flow breaker","firewall_template_coding_agent_rule_60":"Runaway-loop cost cap ($5)","firewall_template_customer_support_agent_rule_5":"Refund-loop circuit breaker","firewall_template_customer_support_agent_rule_10":"Hard-cap unattended refund (> $50)","firewall_template_customer_support_agent_rule_20":"Gate refunds for approval","firewall_template_customer_support_agent_rule_30":"Gate generic refunds for approval","firewall_template_customer_support_agent_rule_40":"Gate bulk reads/exports (> 100 rows)","firewall_template_customer_support_agent_rule_50":"Gate password reset","firewall_template_customer_support_agent_rule_60":"Gate 2FA disable","firewall_template_customer_support_agent_rule_80":"Mask PII in tool args & results","firewall_template_rag_research_agent_rule_10":"SSRF / cloud-metadata egress deny","firewall_template_rag_research_agent_rule_20":"Block non-http fetch schemes","firewall_template_rag_research_agent_rule_30":"Retrieve→egress exfil breaker","firewall_template_rag_research_agent_rule_40":"Research-loop cost cap ($2)","firewall_template_data_analytics_agent_rule_10":"Block destructive DDL","firewall_template_data_analytics_agent_rule_20":"Deny secret-table reads","firewall_template_data_analytics_agent_rule_30":"Gate DELETE / UPDATE","firewall_template_data_analytics_agent_rule_40":"Gate large exports (> 10k rows)","firewall_template_data_analytics_agent_rule_50":"Query→export→egress exfil breaker","firewall_template_data_analytics_agent_rule_60":"Analytics cost cap ($3)","firewall_template_devops_ops_agent_rule_10":"Block infrastructure destroy","firewall_template_devops_ops_agent_rule_20":"Block recursive cloud deletes","firewall_template_devops_ops_agent_rule_30":"Block destructive Kubernetes ops","firewall_template_devops_ops_agent_rule_40":"Gate terraform apply","firewall_template_devops_ops_agent_rule_50":"Gate IAM privilege escalation","firewall_template_devops_ops_agent_rule_60":"Gate secret-manager reads","firewall_template_devops_ops_agent_rule_70":"Ops cost cap ($10)","firewall_template_browser_computer_use_agent_rule_10":"Gate financial / irreversible clicks","firewall_template_browser_computer_use_agent_rule_20":"Block typing into credential fields","firewall_template_browser_computer_use_agent_rule_30":"Block cookie reads","firewall_template_browser_computer_use_agent_rule_40":"Block local-storage reads","firewall_template_browser_computer_use_agent_rule_50":"SSRF navigation egress deny","firewall_template_browser_computer_use_agent_rule_60":"Page-read→egress exfil breaker","firewall_template_browser_computer_use_agent_rule_70":"Browse cost cap ($3)","hero_cta_microcopy":"No credit card · live in 60 secs","hero_trust_accuracy":"Beats GPT-5 & Azure on RouterArena","hero_trust_research":"Backed by published research","route_mode_cheapest":"Cheapest","route_mode_cheapest_sub":"lowest cost","route_mode_balanced":"Balanced","route_mode_balanced_sub":"cheapest that clears the bar","route_mode_quality":"Quality","route_mode_quality_sub":"highest score","route_mode_adaptive":"Adaptive","route_mode_adaptive_sub":"learns from your traffic","route_modes_title":"Route on your terms.","route_modes_desc":"orcarouter/auto is a smart default, not a black box. Point each workspace at the objective you want — the cheapest model that clears your quality bar, the highest quality, or a balance of both — or let it learn the trade-off from your own traffic. You're never locked into one behavior.","routing_dsl_title":"Need more than a mode? Write the rule.","routing_dsl_desc":"When the default isn't enough, express routing as code — version-controlled, reviewable, and live in seconds. No redeploy, no client change.","routing_dsl_docs":"Explore routing docs","landing_seo_description":"One OpenAI-compatible AI gateway for production AI — adaptive routing, load balancing, guardrails, agent firewall, observability and governance across 200+ models.","pricing_seo_description":"Transparent pricing for OrcaRouter. $0 markup on every OpenAI, Anthropic and Gemini call. Free Hacker tier, ${{price}}{{interval}} Team plan, custom Enterprise. Pay only what providers charge.","rewards_seo_description":"Stack OrcaRouter Points on every API call. Climb Ripple → Wave → Surge → Tide → Storm tiers for 1.5×–3× rate limits, priority routing, dedicated support and revenue share.","ig_seo_desc_not_found":"The integration you requested does not exist on OrcaRouter. Browse our integration hub for Cursor, Cline, Continue, Aider, Vercel AI SDK and more.","ig_seo_desc_detail":"Connect {{name}} to OrcaRouter in 5 steps. {{tagline}} Route prompts to GPT-4o, Claude, Gemini and 200+ models with no markup.","ig_seo_desc_hub":"Drop-in OrcaRouter setup for {{count}}+ AI tools. Plug Cursor, Cline, Continue, Aider, Vercel AI SDK and your own OpenAI-compatible client into 200+ models with one API key.","nav_blog":"Blog","nav_ai_security":"AI Security","blog_eyebrow":"OrcaRouter Blog","blog_featured":"Featured","blog_view":"View","blog_view_list":"List view","blog_view_table":"Table view","blog_count":"Total · {{n}}","blog_col_title":"Title","blog_col_category":"Category","blog_col_author":"Author","blog_col_date":"Date","blog_date_published":"Date Published","blog_hero_title":"Blog","blog_hero_sub":"Engineering deep-dives, product updates and AI infrastructure notes from the OrcaRouter team.","blog_loading":"Loading…","blog_load_error":"Could not load posts. Please try again later.","blog_empty":"No posts yet.","blog_prev":"Previous","blog_next":"Next","blog_page_of":"Page {{page}} of {{total}}","blog_post_not_found":"This post could not be found.","blog_back_to_list":"Back to all posts","blog_seo_title_list":"Blog · OrcaRouter","blog_seo_desc_list":"Engineering deep-dives, product updates and AI infrastructure notes from the OrcaRouter team.","retention_tab_label":"Retention & Churn","retention_basis_label":"Paying definition","retention_basis_consumption":"Usage-based","retention_basis_payment":"Payment-based","retention_fetch_failed":"Failed to load retention data","retention_days_suffix":"d","retention_kpi_active_payers":"Active payers","retention_kpi_active_payers_hint":"Distinct paying customers in the window","retention_kpi_retention_rate":"Retention rate","retention_kpi_retention_rate_hint":"Prior-period payers still active","retention_kpi_gross_churn":"Gross churn","retention_kpi_gross_churn_hint":"Prior-period payers who went silent","retention_kpi_nrr":"Net revenue retention","retention_kpi_nrr_hint":"Current revenue from prior payers vs their prior revenue","retention_kpi_churned":"Churned","retention_kpi_churned_hint":"Paid before, silent now","retention_kpi_revenue_churned":"Revenue churned","retention_kpi_revenue_churned_hint":"Spend lost to churn this period","retention_kpi_reactivated":"Reactivated","retention_kpi_reactivated_hint":"Returned after a gap","retention_kpi_new_payers":"New payers","retention_kpi_new_payers_hint":"First-time payers this period","retention_kpi_avg_lifespan":"Avg lifespan","retention_kpi_avg_lifespan_hint":"Days from first to last activity","retention_kpi_avg_ltv":"Avg LTV","retention_kpi_median_ltv":"Median LTV","retention_curve_title":"Retention curve (cohort survival)","retention_curve_empty":"Not enough cohort history yet","retention_curve_x":"Months since signup","retention_engagement_title":"Active payers over time","retention_engagement_empty":"No activity in this range","retention_engagement_active":"Active workspaces","retention_engagement_ma":"7-day average","retention_engagement_avg":"Avg/day","retention_engagement_peak":"Peak","retention_churn_reasons_title":"Why customers churn","retention_churn_reasons_empty":"No churned customers in this period","retention_churn_reasons