_developer":"Developer","member_report_role_owner":"Owner","member_report_role_viewer":"Viewer","member_report_search_aria":"Search members","member_report_sort_aria":"Sort by","member_report_sort_last_active":"Sort: Last active","member_report_sort_requests":"Sort: Requests","member_report_sort_spend":"Sort: Spend","member_report_spend_basis_note":"Charged usage incl. BYOK platform fees; BYOK provider costs are billed by your provider — not your invoice.","member_report_team_col_byok":"BYOK reqs","member_report_team_col_group":"Team","member_report_team_col_members":"Members","member_report_team_empty":"No team usage in this period.","member_report_team_multi_note":"Members in several teams count toward each — the member view is the accounting identity.","member_report_traffic_all":"All traffic","member_report_traffic_byok":"BYOK","member_report_traffic_platform":"Platform-billed","member_usage_by_app":"By app","member_usage_sparkline_label":"Last {{n}} days","member_usage_sparkline_aria":"Daily spend trend, {{n}} days — peak {{peak}}, latest {{latest}}","member_usage_view_requests":"View requests →","members_role_popover_subtitle":"Granted by role: {{role}}","members_tab_adoption":"Adoption","members_tab_usage_report":"Usage report","requests_member_filter_chip":"Member #{{id}}","requests_member_filter_clear":"Clear member filter","usage_member_full_report_link":"View full member report →","usage_member_top50_note":"Showing top members by spend.","adoption_stage_agentic":"Agentic","adoption_stage_agentic_hint":"agent sessions + tools","adoption_stage_copilot":"Copilot","adoption_stage_copilot_hint":"IDE / copilot apps, regular use","adoption_stage_casual":"Casual","adoption_stage_casual_hint":"chat-tier, occasional","adoption_stage_none":"None","adoption_stage_none_hint":"no usage this window","adoption_funnel_seats":"Seats","adoption_funnel_active":"Active (12 wks)","adoption_funnel_multi_week":"Active in 2+ weeks","adoption_funnel_habitual":"Habitual (3+ days/wk)","adoption_task_class_chat":"Chat","adoption_task_class_code":"Code","adoption_task_class_agent":"Agent","adoption_task_class_vision":"Vision","adoption_task_class_audio":"Audio","adoption_task_class_rag":"RAG","adoption_task_class_creative":"Creative","adoption_task_class_other":"Other","member_group_ungrouped":"Ungrouped","member_group_small_fold":"Other (small groups)","adoption_wau_bar_label":"Week of {{week}}: {{n}} active","member_usage_all_traffic_note":"Detail below covers ALL traffic; the report App/Traffic filters do not narrow this view.","byok_settings_eligibility_banner":"Channel eligibility is configured per channel on the channel edit page ('byok_eligible'). Adoption and fee-revenue stats land together with the reporting split.","discord_guild_id_label":"Discord Guild ID (server ID)","discord_guild_id_ph":"Used to verify the user has joined the server","discord_bot_token_label":"Discord Bot Token","discord_bot_verify_help":"Below powers the free-package “join Discord” task: a bot in your server verifies membership at claim time. Free to set up — no paid Discord plan needed.","billing.free_history_title":"Free plan activity","billing.free_history_type_claim":"Free plan claimed","billing.free_history_type_task":"Task: {{name}}","billing.free_history_col_reward":"Reward","billing.free_history_reward_free":"Free","billing.free_history_reward_calls":"+{{count}} calls","billing.free_history_status_claimed":"Claimed","billing.free_history_status_done":"Completed","billing.free_history_invited":"Invited: {{names}}","profile_section_bindings_title":"Account bindings","profile_section_bindings_desc":"Link third-party accounts to unlock related perks","profile_binding_discord_bound_desc":"Your Discord account is linked","profile_binding_discord_unbound_desc":"Link it to verify you joined the Discord server","profile_binding_bound":"Bound","profile_binding_bind_discord":"Bind Discord","free_package_alias_copied":"Model name copied: {{m}}","free_package_alias_copy_failed":"Copy failed","free_package_header_btn":"Free plan","free_package_modal_title":"Free plan","free_package_banner_cta":"Claim now","free_package_banner_msg":"Free plan available: try {{count}} models for free","free_package_claim_btn":"Claim now","free_package_claim_failed":"Could not claim the free plan.","free_package_claim_success":"Free plan claimed — enjoy!","free_package_claiming":"Claiming…","free_package_copy_alias":"Copy model name","free_package_copied":"Copied","free_package_daily_limit":"{{n}}/day","free_package_expired_topup_btn":"Add credits","free_package_expires_in_days":"{{d}}d {{h}}h left","free_package_expires_in_hours":"{{h}}h {{m}}m left","free_package_expires_in_minutes":"{{m}}m left","free_package_expires_in_seconds":"{{s}}s left","free_package_expiry_date_line":"Free plan expires on {{date}}","free_package_expiry_line":"Free plan expires {{when}} ({{date}})","free_package_minute_limit":"{{n}}/min","free_package_model_calls":"{{n}} calls","free_package_not_claimable":"The free plan is not claimable right now.","free_package_rate_limit_prefix":"Rate limit","free_package_remaining":"{{r}} / {{total}} calls left","free_package_section_title":"Free plan","free_package_tab_title":"Free Credits","free_pkg_add_btn":"New package","free_pkg_reset_claim_btn":"Reset a user’s claim","free_pkg_reset_claim_ok":"Reset","free_pkg_reset_claim_help":"Reverts the user to un-claimed and clears their completed tasks so they can claim again — for testing. Deleting the claim also zeroes the workspace balance it created.","free_pkg_reset_email_label":"User email","free_pkg_reset_email_required":"Enter a user email","free_pkg_reset_done":"Claim reset","free_pkg_reset_result":"Done: {{grants}} claim(s), {{balances}} balance row(s), {{tasks}} task(s) cleared.","free_pkg_add_title":"New package","free_pkg_claim_window":"Claim window","free_pkg_claim_window_open":"always open","free_pkg_col_actions":"Actions","free_pkg_col_enabled":"Enabled","free_pkg_created":"Package created","free_pkg_delete_title":"Delete package?","free_pkg_deleted":"Package deleted","free_pkg_edit_title":"Edit package","free_pkg_empty":"No free package yet","free_pkg_enabled_off":"Off","free_pkg_enabled_on":"On","free_pkg_field_description":"Description","free_pkg_field_name":"Name","free_pkg_field_name_ph":"Starter free plan","free_pkg_field_validity":"Validity (days after claim)","free_pkg_field_window":"Claim window","free_pkg_limit_zero_help":"0 = no limit","free_pkg_load_error":"Could not load free-package config: {{e}}","free_pkg_model_add_btn":"Add model","free_pkg_model_add_title":"Add model","free_pkg_model_alias_conflict":"This free alias is already in use","free_pkg_model_base_required":"Base model is required","free_pkg_model_col_alias":"Free alias","free_pkg_model_col_base":"Base model","free_pkg_model_col_daily":"Daily limit","free_pkg_model_col_initial":"Total quota","free_pkg_model_col_minute":"Per-minute limit","free_pkg_model_created":"Model added","free_pkg_model_delete_title":"Remove model from the free pool?","free_pkg_model_deleted":"Model removed","free_pkg_model_edit_title":"Edit model","free_pkg_model_saved":"Model updated","free_pkg_models_empty":"No models in the pool","free_pkg_name_required":"Package name is required","free_pkg_saved":"Package updated","free_pkg_section_models":"Free model pool","free_pkg_section_package":"Package","free_pkg_label_fallback":"Package #{{id}}","free_pkg_section_tasks":"Growth tasks","free_pkg_task_add_btn":"Add task","free_pkg_task_add_title":"Add task","free_pkg_task_alias_required":"Reward model alias is required","free_pkg_task_col_delay":"Delay (s)","free_pkg_task_col_key":"Task key","free_pkg_task_col_reward":"Reward","free_pkg_task_col_url":"Target URL","free_pkg_task_col_verify":"Verify mode","free_pkg_task_created":"Task created","free_pkg_task_delete_title":"Delete task?","free_pkg_task_deleted":"Task deleted","free_pkg_task_edit_title":"Edit task","free_pkg_task_field_alias":"Reward model alias","free_pkg_task_field_calls":"Reward calls","free_pkg_task_field_rewards":"Reward models","free_pkg_task_reward_add":"Add reward model","free_pkg_task_reward_remove":"Remove reward model","free_pkg_task_reward_calls_suffix":"calls","free_pkg_task_reward_calls_positive":"Reward calls must be greater than 0","free_pkg_task_reward_dup":"The same model can only be rewarded once per task","free_pkg_task_field_delay":"Delay (seconds)","free_pkg_task_field_referral_target":"Referrals required","free_pkg_task_key_required":"Task key is required","free_pkg_task_saved":"Task updated","free_pkg_tasks_empty":"No tasks yet","free_pkg_validity_label":"Valid {{d}} days","free_task_claim_btn":"Claim reward","free_task_claim_success":"+{{n}} calls added to {{model}}","free_task_claim_success_generic":"Reward added to your free plan","free_task_claiming":"Claiming…","free_task_discord_join":"Join our Discord","free_task_done":"Done","free_task_fail_already_claimed":"Reward already claimed.","free_task_fail_generic":"Could not claim the reward.","free_task_go_btn":"Go","free_task_locked_btn":"Locked","free_task_locked_hint":"Claim the free plan first","free_task_referral_share":"Share with a friend","free_task_reward_line":"+{{n}} calls → {{model}}","free_task_referral_progress":"Invited {{x}}/{{n}}","free_task_copy_invite":"Copy invite link","free_task_start_referral_btn":"Get invite link","free_task_invite_copied":"Invite link copied","free_task_section_title":"Earn more free calls","free_task_twitter_follow":"Follow us on X","free_task_wait_countdown":"Verifying… {{s}}s","free_package_expired_notice":"Your free plan has expired. Add credits to keep using these models.","free_package_reason_already_claimed":"This workspace has already claimed the free plan.","free_package_reason_user_claimed_elsewhere":"You have already claimed this free plan in another workspace.","free_package_reason_window_closed":"The claim window for this free plan has closed.","free_package_validity_note":"Valid for {{d}} days after claiming.","free_package_free_badge":"FREE","free_package_section_models":"Free models","free_package_price_free":"Free","free_package_validity_never":"Never expires once claimed.","free_pkg_delete_help":"The package, its model pool, and its claim window are permanently removed.","free_pkg_delete_claimed_warn":"This package has been claimed by {{count}} workspace(s). Deleting it immediately zeroes their remaining free calls and erases the claim history — this cannot be undone.","free_pkg_delete_confirm_hint":"Type {{handle}} to confirm.","free_pkg_empty_help":"Create a package to offer a claimable pool of free models on the billing page.","free_pkg_field_description_ph":"Shown to users on the billing page","free_pkg_field_window_help":"Leave empty for an always-open claim window.","free_pkg_model_alias_ph":"Leave blank for \"\u003cbase model>-free\"","free_pkg_models_empty_help":"Add a base model to expose it under a free alias with a call allowance.","free_pkg_task_delay_help":"Only used by click + delay verification.","free_pkg_task_referral_help":"The invite link is generated automatically from each user’s referral code. The reward unlocks once an invited friend actually registers — no target URL or delay needed.","free_pkg_task_field_alias_ph":"Pick a free alias from the pool","free_pkg_task_key_immutable":"Task key cannot be changed after creation.","free_pkg_task_key_ph":"discord_join / twitter_follow / custom key","free_pkg_tasks_empty_help":"Tasks reward extra free calls for social actions (join Discord, follow on X, refer a friend).","free_task_bind_discord_hint":"Link your Discord account in Settings first, then come back to claim.","free_task_fail_not_bound":"Please link your Discord account in Settings first.","free_task_fail_not_member":"Please join our Discord server first, then claim again.","free_task_fail_too_early":"Not ready yet — please wait a moment and try again.","free_pkg_verify_discord_guild":"Discord guild membership","free_pkg_verify_click_delay":"Click + delay","free_pkg_verify_referral_count":"Referral registration","marketing_tab_free_package":"Free package","marketing_tab_free_package_help":"Claimable free-model package on the billing page: model pool with per-model call allowances and rate limits, claim window, and growth tasks (Discord / X / referral) that reward extra calls.","free_task_fail_not_clicked":"Start the task first, then come back to claim.","free_task_fail_no_grant":"Claim the free plan first — rewards are credited into it.","free_task_fail_provider_taken":"This Discord account already claimed the reward on another account.","free_task_fail_verify_unavailable":"Discord verification is not configured yet. Please try again later.","free_task_fail_verify_failed":"Could not verify your Discord membership right now — please try again shortly.","models_free_desc":"Free tier of {{base}} — claim in billing","models_free_badge":"FREE","models_free_remaining":"{{r}}/{{t}} calls left","models_free_calls":"{{n}} free calls","models_free_daily":"{{n}}/day","models_free_minute":"{{n}}/min","models_free_claim_cta":"Claim in billing →","free_router_badge":"Free","free_router_card_desc":"One endpoint that routes each request by difficulty across the free models you claimed. Spends free calls, never your wallet — and when one tier runs out it falls back to another you still have.","models_free_router_meta":"Free models router","models_free_router_routes_to":"Routes to","models_free_router_meta_sub":"· by difficulty","free_router_hero_tagline":"One endpoint for the free tier — routed by difficulty across the free models you claimed.","free_router_seo_desc":"OrcaRouter Free is one endpoint that routes each request by difficulty across the free models you claimed — simple prompts to the light tier, hard ones to the stronger tier. It spends free calls, never your wallet. Call it as orcarouter/free.","free_router_overview":"One endpoint for the free tier. Instead of picking a specific -free alias yourself, call orcarouter/free and it routes each request by difficulty across the free models you claimed — spending free calls, never your wallet.","free_router_how_title":"How it works","free_router_how_s1_title":"Classify by difficulty","free_router_how_s1_body":"Each request is scored on prompt length, code density, tools and reasoning cues — the same signal our adaptive router uses.","free_router_how_s2_title":"Route to a free model","free_router_how_s2_body":"Mundane prompts go to the light free tier; hard ones to the stronger free tier — drawn only from the free models you claimed.","free_router_how_s3_title":"Spend a free call","free_router_how_s3_body":"One free call is deducted from that model's allowance. Your wallet is never touched. Out of one tier? It falls back to another you still have.","free_router_models_title":"Free models it routes to","free_router_models_empty":"Claim a free package in billing to unlock the free models this router draws from.","free_router_faq_q1":"What is orcarouter/free?","free_router_faq_a1":"A curated router over the free-tier models you claimed. It classifies each request by difficulty and sends easy prompts to the light free model, hard ones to the stronger free model — one endpoint instead of picking an alias yourself.","free_router_faq_q2":"How is it billed?","free_router_faq_a2":"It consumes a free call from the selected model's claimed allowance — never your wallet balance. When a tier runs out it falls back to another free model you still have calls for.","free_router_faq_q3":"What if I have no free models?","free_router_faq_a3":"Claim a free package in the billing page first. With no claimed free model (or all of them used up), orcarouter/free returns a \"free allowance used up\" error rather than charging you.","tiered_pricing_cache_write_price":"Cache Write Price (Optional)","tiered_pricing_cache_write_price_placeholder":"Empty = inherit global","tiered_pricing_error_cache_write_price_nonneg":"Tier {{idx}}: cache write price must be >= 0","tiered_pricing_tier_cache_write_suffix":"write $ {{cacheWrite}}/1M","usage_cache_creation_tokens_line":"Cache creation {{tokens}} tokens / 1M tokens * {{symbol}}{{price}}","usage_cache_creation_ratio_breakdown":"Cache creation: {{tokens}} / 1M * model ratio {{modelRatio}} * cache creation ratio {{cacheCreationRatio}} * {{ratioType}} {{ratio}} = {{amount}}","usage_cache_creation_ratio_label":"Cache creation ratio {{cacheCreationRatio}}","usage_cache_creation_price":"Cache creation price {{symbol}}{{price}} / 1M tokens","usage_cache_creation_price_colon":"Cache creation price: {{symbol}}{{price}} / 1M tokens","usage_ratio_summary_with_cache_creation":"Model ratio {{modelRatio}}, completion ratio {{completionRatio}}, cache ratio {{cacheRatio}}, cache creation ratio {{cacheCreationRatio}}, {{ratioType}} {{ratio}}","boost_meter_title":"Boost your reward","boost_meter_total_line":"{{amount}} — caps at {{cap}}","boost_meter_progress_aria":"Boost progress toward the cap","boost_meter_ends_in":"Boost ends in {{time}}","boost_meter_window_over":"Boost window ended — collect what you earned","boost_meter_deadline_static":"Boost ends {{date}}","boost_share_label":"Your boost link","boost_share_copy":"Copy","boost_share_copy_aria":"Copy boost link","squad_copy_link_aria":"Copy invite link","squad_share_opening":"Opening your squad invite…","squad_join_aria":"Join {{name}}'s squad ({{count}}/{{size}} members)","boost_share_copied":"Link copied","boost_rung_unique_visit":"Friend taps your link","boost_rung_signup":"Friend signs up","boost_rung_first_call":"Friend makes their first API call","boost_rung_amount":"+{{amount}} each","boost_rung_used":"{{used}}/{{max}}","boost_collect_cta":"Collect {{amount}} now →","billing.boost_earn_sub":"Share your link — every friend who joins grows the reward you collect.","billing.boost_earn_unnamed":"Boost meter","billing.boost_earn_ends":"Ends {{date}}","billing.boost_earn_copy":"Copy link","billing.boost_earn_copied":"Copied","billing.boost_earn_collect":"View & collect →","boost_setting_no_changes":"No changes to save","boost_setting_save_failed":"Save failed, please retry","boost_setting_save_success":"Saved","boost_setting_section":"Boost & Referral","boost_setting_desc":"Enable boost meters on vouchers: a claimant opens a meter, shares a link, and every friend who joins grows the reward they collect. Requires model-scoped promo credit to be enabled (the parent switch). Per-voucher programs are configured in the voucher editor and override these defaults.","boost_setting_enable_label":"Enable boost meters","boost_setting_supersede_label":"Boost replaces classic invite rewards","boost_setting_supersede_extra":"A boost-attributed signup pays the boost rails instead of the global invite bonus — never both.","boost_setting_tap_label":"Count anonymous link taps","boost_setting_tap_extra":"Off by default: taps are the most farmable rung. Signups and first API calls always count.","boost_setting_window_label":"Default meter window (hours)","boost_setting_max_open_label":"Max open meters per user","boost_setting_tap_cap_label":"Tap budget per IP per hour","boost_setting_helper_reward_label":"Default friend-side reward (quota)","boost_setting_helper_reward_extra":"Credit a referred friend receives on signup. 0 = none; a voucher program can override per voucher.","boost_setting_save":"Save Boost & Referral settings","redemption_boost_label":"Boost program (share-to-grow meter)","redemption_boost_hint":"The claimer opens a meter instead of a flat grant: an endowed start, a share link, and typed contribution rungs that grow the reward toward a cap. Needs Boost & Referral enabled in Settings → Operation to run; the flat amount above stays the fallback while it is off.","redemption_boost_config_label":"Boost program JSON (unlock_tasks)","redemption_boost_config_hint":"Validated on save — quotas are raw quota units (500,000 ≈ $1). endowed + entry bonus must fit under cap_quota; helpers: unique_visit / signup / first_call / first_topup.","redemption_boost_template_btn":"Insert example program","redemption_boost_config_required":"Enter the boost program JSON or turn the boost section off","redemption_boost_config_not_json":"The boost program must be valid JSON","boost_landing_someone":"A friend","boost_landing_title_reward":"{{name}} sent you {{amount}} in free AI credit","boost_landing_title_plain":"{{name}} invited you to OrcaRouter","boost_landing_sub":"Sign up and it lands on your account — and your signup grows their reward too.","boost_landing_sub_closed":"This boost window has ended, but a free account still takes 30 seconds.","boost_landing_progress":"They're at {{total}} of {{cap}} — help them max it out","boost_landing_cta_reward":"Claim my {{amount}} →","boost_landing_cta_plain":"Join & boost them →","boost_landing_cta_closed":"Create a free account →","boost_landing_fineprint":"Takes 30 seconds. No credit card required.","boost_register_banner_reward":"You've been invited — \u003camount> in free credit lands on this account after signup.","boost_register_banner_plain":"You've been invited — signing up boosts your friend's reward.","boost_register_banner_reward_named":"{{name}} invited you — \u003camount> in free credit lands on this account after signup.","boost_register_banner_plain_named":"{{name}} invited you — signing up boosts their reward.","boost_meter_delta":"+{{amount}}","boost_next_cap_reached":"Cap reached — collect your {{amount}} now","boost_next_rung":"Next: {{action}} adds {{amount}}","boost_next_all_used":"Every boost is in — collect before the window closes","boost_share_message":"I'm unlocking {{total}} in free AI credit — tap my link and help me grow it to {{cap}}: {{url}}","boost_share_msg_copy":"Copy invite message","boost_share_msg_copied":"Message copied","boost_share_native":"Share…","boost_preclaim_line":"Boost drop: claiming starts a {{hours}}-hour window — share your link to grow it up to {{cap}}, then collect once.","redeem_cta_boost":"Claim {{amount}} — boost it up to {{cap}} →","billing.boost_earn_stranded":"This drop has closed — the meter can no longer be collected","billing.boost_earn_ended":"Window ended — collect what you earned","billing.ws_rail_armed_title":"+{{pct}}% team match armed","billing.ws_rail_armed_line":"Top-ups earn +{{pct}}% bonus credit — {{matched}} of {{cap}} matched · through {{date}}","billing.ws_rail_capped_title":"Team match maxed out","billing.ws_rail_capped_line":"You earned the full {{cap}} match this window — it runs through {{date}}.","billing.ws_rail_budget_title":"Team match paused","billing.ws_rail_budget_line":"This month's match pool is fully claimed — top-ups won't earn the bonus until it refills. Your window runs through {{date}}.","billing.ws_rail_prompt_title":"Earn a +{{pct}}% team match","billing.ws_rail_prompt_line":"Add a teammate who ships a call — your workspace earns +{{pct}}% bonus credit on top-ups for the rest of the month.","billing.ws_rail_prompt_cta":"Invite a teammate →","boost_setting_ws_rail_label":"Enable workspace teammate rail","boost_setting_ws_rail_extra":"Add a teammate who ships a call → the workspace earns a top-up match for the rest of the month. Independent of the meter switch; needs the promo-credit parent.","boost_setting_ws_rail_pct_label":"Teammate match percent","boost_setting_ws_rail_cap_label":"Match cap per teammate (quota)","boost_setting_ws_rail_min_topup_label":"Min top-up to match (USD)","boost_setting_ws_rail_budget_label":"Rail budget pool (quota)","boost_setting_ws_rail_budget_extra":"Global pool across all teammate matches. 0 = unlimited; read live, so growing it resumes matching immediately.","boost_next_window_over":"Window ended — collect your {{amount}} now","boost_rung_first_topup":"Friend makes their first top-up","boost_rung_amount_percent":"+{{percent}}% of their top-up (up to {{cap}})","boost_next_amount_percent":"{{percent}}% of their top-up","squad_request_failed":"Squad request failed — try again.","squad_not_available_note":"Squads aren't available right now.","squad_card_title":"Team up to unlock this drop","squad_create_btn":"Start a squad","squad_open_pool_label":"List it publicly so others can join","squad_join_token_ph":"Paste an invite token","squad_join_btn":"Join","squad_pool_title":"Open squads looking for members","squad_member_count":"{{count}}/{{size}} members","squad_forming_title":"Your squad is forming","squad_fill_deadline":"— fills by {{date}}","squad_tier_note":"{{member}} each if it fills, {{solo}} solo if it doesn't.","squad_filled_note":"Squad filled — member tier {{amount}} unlocked","squad_solo_note":"Deadline passed — solo tier {{amount}}","squad_granted_note":"{{amount}} credited to your workspace","squad_invite_label":"Your invite token","squad_invite_link_label":"Your invite link","squad_qualified_waiting":"You're qualified — credit releases when the squad resolves","squad_qualify_note":"Make your first API call to release your credit","squad_qualify_spend_note":"Spend {{amount}} to release your credit","squad_time_left":"{{time}} left","squad_seats_filled":"{{count}} of {{size}} seats filled","squad_seat_you":"You","squad_unlock_more":"{{count}} more to unlock {{amount}} each","squad_solo_fallback":"or {{solo}} solo if it doesn't fill","squad_share_cta":"Share your invite","squad_share_title":"Join my squad","squad_share_text":"Join my squad and we both unlock more credit","squad_first_request_title":"Your first request","squad_first_request_sub":"One API call releases your squad credit.","squad_celebrate_title":"Squad complete!","squad_celebrate_sub":"{{amount}} unlocked for everyone — credited once you've each made a call.","drop_banner_cta":"Claim it →","drop_banner_dismiss":"Dismiss","redeem_waitlist_ref_line":"Each friend who joins through your link moves you up the line.","redemption_duplicate_action":"Duplicate","redemption_waitlist_col_priority":"Priority","drop_setting_enabled_label":"Model-drop banner","drop_setting_enabled_extra":"Sells the current drop voucher on the Models / Leaderboard pages and in launch notify emails. Live only while text is set and the window is open.","drop_setting_text_label":"Banner text","drop_setting_text_ph":"Kimi K3 is live — claim $25 free credit","drop_setting_key_label":"Drop voucher key","drop_setting_key_extra":"The banner links to /redeem/{key}. Never exposed while the banner is dark.","drop_setting_ends_label":"Banner ends at (unix)","drop_setting_ends_extra":"Unix seconds after which the banner goes dark automatically. 0 = no scheduled end.","boost_growth_x_follow":"Follow @{{handle}} on X — release-day drops land there first","boost_growth_discord_link":"Link your Discord account in settings to claim {{amount}}","boost_growth_discord_verify":"Verify Discord join — claim {{amount}}","boost_growth_discord_claimed":"Discord reward claimed","boost_growth_discord_failed":"Could not verify — try again.","boost_growth_graduation":"You've referred {{count}} activated devs — apply to the Partner program →","boost_setting_discord_guild_label":"Discord guild id","boost_setting_discord_guild_extra":"The P6 rewarded join task: guild id + bot token + reward > 0 arm it. One credit per Discord identity.","boost_setting_discord_token_label":"Discord bot token","boost_setting_discord_token_clear":"Clear stored token","boost_setting_discord_token_cleared":"Stored Discord bot token cleared","boost_setting_discord_reward_label":"Discord join reward (quota)","boost_setting_graduation_label":"Partner graduation threshold","boost_setting_graduation_extra":"Activated referrals at which the Earn hub pitches the Partner program. 0 = tile off.","compare_page_h1":"{{a}} vs {{b}} Comparison: Benchmarks, Pricing & Speed ({{date}})","compare_intro":"A head-to-head comparison of {{a}} ({{ap}}) and {{b}} ({{bp}}) on OrcaRouter — pricing, context window, latency, throughput and benchmark quality, side by side, so you can pick the right model for your workload.","compare_seo_title_full":"{{a}} vs {{b}} Comparison: Benchmarks, Pricing & Speed ({{date}}) · OrcaRouter","compare_seo_title_mid":"{{a}} vs {{b}} Comparison: Pricing & Benchmarks ({{date}}) · OrcaRouter","compare_seo_title_short":"{{a}} vs {{b}} Comparison ({{date}}) · OrcaRouter","compare_seo_title_min":"{{a}} vs {{b}} Comparison · OrcaRouter","compare_meta_tail":"Full {{date}} pricing & benchmark comparison on OrcaRouter.","compare_meta_price":"{{x}} vs {{y}} per 1M input.","compare_meta_context":"{{x}} vs {{y}} context.","compare_meta_latency":"{{x}}ms vs {{y}}ms p50 latency.","compare_h2_speed":"Speed & latency","compare_h2_benchmarks":"Benchmarks & quality","compare_h2_choose":"Which should you choose?","compare_h2_battle":"Hands-on test: {{a}} vs {{b}} in Battle Mode","compare_toc_title":"On this page","compare_toc_battle":"Battle test","compare_toc_faq":"FAQ","compare_glance_title":"At a glance","compare_rates_title":"Token rates side by side","compare_best_for_title":"Best for","compare_best_for_cost":"Cost-sensitive, high volume","compare_best_for_speed":"Latency-critical chat & agents","compare_best_for_quality":"Hardest reasoning & coding","compare_best_for_context":"Longest inputs","compare_hub_seo_title":"Compare AI Models — Benchmarks, Pricing & Speed · OrcaRouter","compare_hub_meta":"Compare AI models side by side — pricing, benchmarks, context window and latency for every major LLM, with a live head-to-head Battle Mode.","compare_hub_breadcrumb":"Compare","breadcrumb":"Breadcrumb","compare_hub_h1":"Compare AI models","compare_hub_intro":"Head-to-head comparisons of the models available on OrcaRouter — pricing per million tokens, context window, p50 latency, throughput and benchmark quality, side by side. Every comparison ends with a live Battle Mode you can run yourself and vote on.","compare_hub_h2_cross":"Compare models across providers","compare_hub_h2_same":"Compare models from the same provider","compare_hub_outro":"Looking for a single model rather than a matchup? The full catalog lists every model with its pricing, capabilities and benchmarks.","compare_hub_link_from_model":"Browse AI model comparisons →","compare_meta_lead":"{{a}} vs {{b}} compared.","compare_h2_table":"Model comparison","compare_h2_performance":"Performance comparison","compare_h2_faq":"{{a}} vs {{b}} FAQ","compare_table_caption":"Pricing, context, latency, throughput and quality for {{a}} and {{b}}.","compare_col_metric":"Metric","compare_col_takeaway":"Takeaway","compare_row_latency":"p50 latency","compare_row_throughput":"Throughput","compare_unit_per_m":"per 1M tokens","compare_expl_input":"{{winner}} is {{pct}}% cheaper than {{loser}} on input tokens.","compare_expl_input_nopct":"{{winner}} has cheaper input pricing than {{loser}}.","compare_expl_input_tie":"{{a}} and {{b}} charge the same for input tokens.","compare_expl_output":"{{winner}} is {{pct}}% cheaper than {{loser}} on output tokens.","compare_expl_output_nopct":"{{winner}} has cheaper output pricing than {{loser}}.","compare_expl_output_tie":"{{a}} and {{b}} charge the same for output tokens.","compare_expl_context":"{{winner}} accepts a {{pct}}% larger context window than {{loser}}.","compare_expl_context_nopct":"{{winner}} accepts a larger context window than {{loser}}.","compare_expl_context_tie":"{{a}} and {{b}} share the same context window.","compare_expl_latency":"{{winner}} responds {{pct}}% faster than {{loser}} at the median.","compare_expl_latency_nopct":"{{winner}} has lower median latency than {{loser}}.","compare_expl_latency_tie":"{{a}} and {{b}} have comparable median latency.","compare_expl_throughput":"{{winner}} streams tokens {{pct}}% faster than {{loser}}.","compare_expl_throughput_nopct":"{{winner}} has higher throughput than {{loser}}.","compare_expl_throughput_tie":"{{a}} and {{b}} stream at a similar rate.","compare_expl_quality":"{{winner}} scores {{pct}}% higher than {{loser}} on the composite quality index.","compare_expl_quality_nopct":"{{winner}} has a higher composite quality score than {{loser}}.","compare_expl_quality_tie":"{{a}} and {{b}} have matching composite quality scores.","compare_verdict_price":"On price, {{winner}} is the cheaper option — about {{pct}}% below {{loser}} on input tokens.","compare_verdict_price_nopct":"On price, {{winner}} is the cheaper option versus {{loser}}.","compare_verdict_speed":"For latency-sensitive workloads, {{winner}} returns the first token sooner.","compare_verdict_quality":"On benchmark quality, {{winner}} leads the composite index.","compare_verdict_pick":"Pick {{cheap}} to minimise cost, or {{fast}} when response speed matters most.","compare_perf_conclusion":"Across the last 7 days, {{winner}} holds the lower median response latency.","compare_perf_conclusion_tie":"Median response latency is comparable between the two models over the last 7 days.","compare_arena_title":"Community head-to-head (Design Arena)","compare_arena_source":"Source: Design Arena Elo","compare_arena_elo_unit":"Elo rating","compare_arena_win_rate":"{{pct}}% win rate","compare_arena_conclusion":"In head-to-head community tournaments, {{winner}} holds the higher Elo rating ({{win_elo}} versus {{lose_elo}}), meaning it wins more direct match-ups against comparable models.","compare_arena_conclusion_tie":"Both models hold a comparable community Elo rating (around {{elo}}) in head-to-head tournaments, so neither has a clear edge in blind preference tests.","compare_faq_arena_q":"Which wins more head-to-head match-ups, {{a}} or {{b}}?","compare_faq_arena_a":"{{winner}} holds the higher Design Arena Elo rating ({{win_elo}} versus {{lose_elo}}), so it wins more blind head-to-head comparisons against comparable models.","compare_faq_cheaper_q":"Is {{a}} or {{b}} cheaper?","compare_faq_cheaper_a":"{{winner}} is cheaper on input tokens at {{win_price}} per 1M versus {{lose_price}} per 1M.","compare_faq_context_q":"Which has the larger context window, {{a}} or {{b}}?","compare_faq_context_a":"{{winner}} accepts the larger context window, so it fits longer documents and conversations in a single request.","compare_faq_faster_q":"Which is faster, {{a}} or {{b}}?","compare_faq_faster_a":"{{winner}} has the lower median (p50) response latency in OrcaRouter's live measurements.","compare_faq_which_q":"Should I use {{a}} or {{b}}?","compare_faq_which_a":"Choose {{a}} or {{b}} based on your priority: cost, context window, latency, or benchmark quality. The table above shows which model wins on each, so match the winner to the dimension that matters most for your workload.","compare_faq_switch_q":"How do I switch between {{a}} and {{b}}?","compare_faq_switch_a":"Both models are available through the same OrcaRouter API endpoint — change the model name in your request to route to either one, with no other code changes.","compare_h2_pricing":"Pricing & cost analysis","compare_narrative_intro2":"Both {{a}} and {{b}} are available through the same OrcaRouter endpoint at provider cost with zero token markup, so switching between them is a one-line change and the numbers below are what you actually pay. This comparison pulls live pricing, the published context window, and OrcaRouter's own latency and throughput measurements so you can weigh cost against performance for your specific workload rather than relying on a vendor's headline benchmark. The right choice almost always depends on the shape of your traffic — prompt length, how much text you generate, how latency-sensitive your users are, and how hard the reasoning is — so the sections below break the decision down one dimension at a time and end with a concrete recommendation. Wherever a metric is missing for one of the two models, that row is left out rather than guessed, so every claim here is backed by a real number.","compare_narrative_pricing":"On input tokens {{a}} costs {{a_in}} per 1M versus {{b_in}} for {{b}}, and on output {{a_out}} versus {{b_out}} per 1M. Output tokens are usually where the bill is decided: a chat or agent workload that generates long completions is dominated by the output rate, so the model that looks cheaper on input can still be the more expensive choice end to end. Estimate your real input-to-output ratio before picking on price alone — a retrieval-heavy prompt with a short answer and a short prompt with a long generation land on opposite sides of this table. A practical way to size this is to take a representative sample of your prompts, count the average input and output tokens, and multiply each by the two models' respective rates; the model with the lower blended cost on your actual mix is the one to beat. Remember that both prices here are the raw provider rate — OrcaRouter adds no markup — so the comparison is apples-to-apples and the savings you compute are the savings you keep.","compare_narrative_pricing_free":"One or both of these models does not expose per-token pricing here (it may be a free-tier, per-call, or not-yet-priced model), so treat the cost columns as indicative and confirm the live rate on each model's own page before you budget against it.","compare_narrative_context":"{{a}} accepts up to {{a_ctx}} tokens of context and {{b}} accepts {{b_ctx}}. The context window caps how much source material — documents, code, prior conversation — you can send in a single request. A larger window lets you skip chunking and retrieval plumbing for long inputs, but you still pay input-token rates for everything you send, so a bigger window is a capability, not a discount. Match the window to the longest single request your workload realistically produces rather than the largest number on the page. Also keep in mind that quality can degrade toward the end of a very long context on any model, so a large window is best treated as headroom for occasional long inputs rather than a licence to stuff every request to the limit.","compare_narrative_performance":"Latency and throughput decide how the model feels in production. Median (p50) response latency is how long a typical request waits before the first token; throughput (tokens per second) sets how fast the answer streams once it starts. For interactive chat and agent loops, low p50 latency matters most because the user is waiting on the first token; for batch generation and long-form output, throughput dominates the wall-clock time because the answer is long. The 7-day trend charts above show whether each model's latency is stable or drifting, which a single headline number hides — a model with a great average but a noisy tail can still miss a strict p95 SLA. If your product has a latency budget, read both the median and the shape of the curve, and remember that end-to-end latency also includes your network hop and any retrieval or tool calls you make around the model.","compare_narrative_quality":"Benchmark scores approximate capability but are not a substitute for testing on your own prompts. The composite indices shown here aggregate multiple public evaluations, and the percentile marks where each model lands against every comparable model in the catalog — a useful shortlist signal, not a guarantee for your task. A model that leads on a general intelligence index can still trail on your domain (coding, extraction, multilingual, long-context reasoning), so use the benchmarks to narrow the field, then run both models on a representative slice of your traffic. Pay attention to the specific index that matches your use case rather than the top-line number: a coding-heavy product should weight the coding index, a research assistant the reasoning index. Benchmarks also age as models are updated, so treat them as a starting hypothesis you confirm with your own evaluation set.","compare_narrative_choosing":"If cost is the binding constraint, start with the cheaper model on your actual input-to-output mix and only move up if quality misses. If responsiveness is the priority — user-facing chat, agents, anything where someone is waiting — weight p50 latency and throughput over a small price gap. If you are pushing the hardest reasoning, coding, or long-context work, let the benchmark and context-window winner lead and accept the higher rate where it pays for itself. Because both models sit behind the same API, the low-risk move is to route a fraction of real traffic to each and compare cost, latency, and answer quality on your own prompts before committing. A common pattern is to tier: send the bulk of easy, high-volume requests to the cheaper or faster model and reserve the stronger model for the requests that actually need it, which captures most of the quality upside at a fraction of the cost. Whichever you choose, keep the switch reversible — with a one-line model-name change you can move traffic back the moment the numbers or your requirements shift.","compare_faq_output_q":"Which is cheaper on output tokens, {{a}} or {{b}}?","compare_faq_output_a":"{{winner}} has the lower output price at {{win_price}} per 1M versus {{lose_price}} per 1M. Output pricing usually matters more than input for generation-heavy workloads, so weight it accordingly.","compare_faq_throughput_q":"Which streams faster, {{a}} or {{b}}?","compare_faq_throughput_a":"{{winner}} has the higher measured throughput (tokens per second), so long completions finish sooner once generation starts.","compare_faq_quality_q":"Which scores higher on benchmarks, {{a}} or {{b}}?","compare_faq_quality_a":"{{winner}} leads on the composite quality index shown above, but benchmark leads don't always transfer to a specific domain — validate on your own prompts before standardizing.","compare_faq_pricing_model_q":"How are {{a}} and {{b}} billed on OrcaRouter?","compare_faq_pricing_model_a":"Both are billed at the upstream provider's rate with zero token markup — you pay the same per-token price you would pay the provider directly, through one OrcaRouter API key and endpoint.","compare_faq_same_api_q":"Can I call both {{a}} and {{b}} with the same code?","compare_faq_same_api_a":"Yes. Both are exposed through OrcaRouter's OpenAI-compatible API, so you change only the model name to route between them — no SDK swap, no separate credentials.","boost_setting_parent_off_warning":"Boost meters are enabled, but the promo-credit parent switch is off — claim pages hide all boosters and claims pay flat until it is turned on.","redemption_boost_dark_warning":"Boost is currently off globally (master switch and/or promo-credit parent) — this program saves, but the public claim page shows a plain voucher until both are on.","growth_builder_boost_helper_reward_custom":"Custom friend-side reward","growth_builder_boost_helper_reward_custom_extra":"Unchecked: the platform's default friend reward still applies. To give the friend nothing, check this and set $0.","growth_builder_preview_boost_helper_reward_default":"Friend reward: platform default","growth_builder_rung_unique_visit_caveat":"Counts only while 'Count anonymous link taps' is on in Boost settings (ships off)","growth_builder_preview_boost_window_default":"Meter window: platform default","boost_landing_sub_full":"Their boost is maxed out — but a free account still takes 30 seconds.","squad_headline":"Team up for {{amount}} each","squad_offer_line":"A team of {{size}} unlocks {{amount}} each — fill it within {{hours}}h.","squad_offer_line_solo":"A team of {{size}} unlocks {{amount}} each within {{hours}}h — if it doesn't fill, everyone still gets {{solo}}.","squad_register_cta":"Create free account & team up","squad_cta_ready":"Team up to unlock {{amount}} each →","squad_invite_banner":"{{name}} invited you to join their squad","squad_join_named_cta":"Join {{name}}'s squad →","squad_register_named_cta":"Create free account & join {{name}}'s squad","squad_register_banner":"{{name}} invited you to join their squad — sign up to claim your spot.","squad_start_own_alt":"or start your own squad","how_it_works_toggle":"How does it work?","squad_hiw_s1":"Grab a seat — or start a new squad.","squad_hiw_s2":"Share your link; each friend who joins fills a seat.","squad_hiw_s3":"Fill the squad before the timer runs out.","squad_hiw_s4":"Fill it and everyone gets the bigger reward — if it does not fill, you still get the solo amount.","boost_hiw_s1":"Claim to unlock your personal share link.","boost_hiw_s2":"Friends tap your link and sign up.","boost_hiw_s3":"Every signup pushes your meter higher.","boost_hiw_s4":"Cross each tier for a bigger reward, up to the cap.","growth_builder_usd_note":"Boost amounts are entered in US dollars — the voucher amount above uses your display currency.","boost_landing_sub_signup_full":"You can still help their boost grow — sign up free, it takes 30 seconds.","onb_auto_catalog_link":"Discover all models in the catalog","onb_auto_desc":"One model name. Auto picks the right model for each request and optimizes cache — cutting cost, not quality.","onb_auto_point_cache":"Automatic prompt-cache optimization to maximize savings","onb_auto_point_hard":"Hard tasks route to frontier models","onb_auto_point_routine":"Routine tasks route to open-source — a fraction of frontier cost","onb_auto_req_label":"Your request","onb_auto_tagline":"The standard router","onb_auto_toggle":"Router details","cache_analytics_advantage_checklist_title":"How routing lifts cache hits","cache_analytics_advantage_title":"Cache advantage","cache_analytics_attr_by":"By","cache_analytics_attr_no_reads":"No cache reads in this window yet — attribution is live and stamping requests.","cache_analytics_attr_seg_client":"Client-managed","cache_analytics_attr_seg_organic":"Organic","cache_analytics_attr_seg_routing":"Routing-managed","cache_analytics_attr_single_upstream":"single upstream","cache_analytics_attr_stamped_line":"{{stamped}} stamped · {{unattributed}} unattributed requests","cache_analytics_attribution_pending":"Attribution ships with pin-source stamping — new requests will be attributed from that point on.","cache_analytics_channels_tab":"Channels","cache_analytics_col_cost_request":"$/req","cache_analytics_col_cost_session":"$/session","cache_analytics_col_hit_rate":"Hit rate","cache_analytics_col_input_tokens":"Input tokens","cache_analytics_col_requests":"Requests","cache_analytics_col_saved":"Saved","cache_analytics_col_segment":"Segment","cache_analytics_col_spend":"Spend","cache_analytics_col_total":"Total","cache_analytics_composition_row_aria":"{{label}}: {{newPct}} new input · {{readPct}} cache read · {{writePct}} cache write","cache_analytics_composition_title":"Input composition by provider","cache_analytics_coverage_attr_desc":"Requests stamped with a cache pin source (routing / client / organic).","cache_analytics_coverage_attr_pending":"Not stamped yet — lands with attribution","cache_analytics_coverage_attr_title":"Attribution coverage","cache_analytics_coverage_empty":"No coverage data for this window.","cache_analytics_coverage_footnote":"MySQL-fallback windows are capped — very long ranges may be truncated when ClickHouse is unavailable.","cache_analytics_coverage_premig_desc":"Requests recorded before workspace migration (the workspace_id = 0 bucket).","cache_analytics_coverage_premig_title":"Pre-migration traffic","cache_analytics_coverage_session_desc":"Requests carrying a session ID — the denominator for cost-per-session numbers.","cache_analytics_coverage_session_title":"Session-ID coverage","cache_analytics_coverage_telemetry_desc":"Share of requests whose upstream response reported cache token detail.","cache_analytics_coverage_telemetry_title":"Cache telemetry coverage","cache_analytics_coverage_title":"Telemetry coverage","cache_analytics_dim_app":"App","cache_analytics_dim_channel":"Channel","cache_analytics_dim_model":"Model","cache_analytics_dim_provider":"Provider","cache_analytics_dim_task":"Task","cache_analytics_dim_use_case":"Use case","cache_analytics_dim_workspace":"Workspace","cache_analytics_dims_aria":"Breakdown dimension","cache_analytics_empty_desc":"Cache analytics could not be loaded for this time range. Try refreshing or picking a different window.","cache_analytics_empty_title":"No cache analytics available","cache_analytics_est":"Est.","cache_analytics_feat_affinity":"Affinity rules for Codex / Claude CLIs","cache_analytics_feat_affinity_desc":"Known agent CLIs are detected and routed with cache-friendly affinity out of the box.","cache_analytics_feat_cache_control":"Claude cache_control injection","cache_analytics_feat_cache_control_desc":"Admin toggle, off by default — enabling it is recommended to lift Anthropic cache hit rates.","cache_analytics_feat_pinning":"Session → channel + key pinning","cache_analytics_feat_pinning_desc":"Requests in the same session stick to one upstream channel and API key, keeping provider caches warm.","cache_analytics_feat_prompt_key":"prompt_cache_key synthesis","cache_analytics_feat_prompt_key_desc":"On the roadmap: synthesize a stable prompt_cache_key for providers that support it.","cache_analytics_legend_new":"New input","cache_analytics_legend_read":"Cache read","cache_analytics_legend_write":"Cache write","cache_analytics_matrix_rows_aria":"Matrix row dimension","cache_analytics_matrix_title":"Spend matrix","cache_analytics_no_data":"No data for this window","cache_analytics_other":"Other","cache_analytics_perspectives_title":"Cache perspectives","cache_analytics_price_billed":"Billed","cache_analytics_price_caption":"Billed vs provider list price · blended, incl. output tokens · Est.","cache_analytics_price_list":"List price","cache_analytics_price_title":"Billed vs list price by model","cache_analytics_range_30d":"Last 30 days","cache_analytics_range_7d":"Last 7 days","cache_analytics_range_90d":"Last 90 days","cache_analytics_range_custom":"Custom…","cache_analytics_range_end":"End date","cache_analytics_range_max_92":"Custom range is limited to 92 days.","cache_analytics_range_mtd":"Month to date","cache_analytics_range_start":"Start date","cache_analytics_range_today":"Today","cache_analytics_range_window":"Showing {{window}}","cache_analytics_retry":"Retry","cache_analytics_sessions_footnote":"$/session is averaged only over requests that carry a session id.","cache_analytics_share_csv":"Download CSV","cache_analytics_share_error_desc":"The shareable report needs cache data in the selected window. Try again or pick a different range.","cache_analytics_share_error_title":"Could not load the report","cache_analytics_share_include_absolute":"Include absolute spend","cache_analytics_share_png_failed":"PNG export is not supported in this browser — use Print instead.","cache_analytics_share_png_social":"Download PNG 1200×630","cache_analytics_share_png_square":"Download PNG 1080×1080","cache_analytics_share_print":"Print one-pager","cache_analytics_share_report":"Share report","cache_analytics_revenue_redacted":"Monetary figures are hidden — they require revenue or finance access. Token, hit-rate and coverage metrics are shown in full.","cache_analytics_share_retry":"Retry","cache_analytics_share_title":"Share cache report","cache_analytics_tab":"Cache analytics","cache_analytics_tile_at_list":"{{amount}} at list","cache_analytics_tile_cost_request":"Avg cost / request","cache_analytics_tile_cost_session":"Avg cost / session","cache_analytics_tile_effective":"Effective vs list","cache_analytics_tile_effective_sub":"vs provider list price","cache_analytics_tile_hit_rate":"Cache hit rate","cache_analytics_tile_read_tokens":"Cached tokens read","cache_analytics_tile_read_tokens_sub":"of {{total}} total input · {{requests}} requests","cache_analytics_tile_saved":"Saved by caching","cache_analytics_tile_saved_vs_list":"Saved vs list","cache_analytics_tile_session_coverage":"session id on {{pct}} of requests","cache_analytics_tile_spend":"Total spend","cache_analytics_trend_aria":"Cache hit rate trend: {{first}} → {{last}}","cache_analytics_trend_series":"Hit rate","cache_analytics_trend_title":"Cache hit rate over time","cache_analytics_truncated":"Showing top segments only — smaller segments are omitted.","cache_analytics_vs_prev":"vs previous period","onb_base_url_copy_aria":"Copy base URL","onb_base_url_label":"Base URL","onb_checklist_title":"Activation","onb_chip_caveat":"Caveat","onb_chip_pending":"Should work","onb_chip_verified":"Verified","onb_client_generic":"API","onb_coach_copied_toast":"Fixed setup copied — re-apply it, then test again.","onb_coach_copy_btn":"Copy fixed config","onb_coach_model_line":"Last attempt: {{model}}","onb_coach_title":"Almost — your last attempt failed","onb_code_empty_hint":"Enter a code first.","onb_code_failed":"Could not redeem this code.","onb_code_placeholder":"Enter code","onb_code_redeem_btn":"Redeem","onb_code_redeemed_toast":"Code redeemed!","onb_code_redeeming":"Redeeming…","onb_config_copied":"✓ Copied","onb_config_copy_btn":"Copy","onb_copy_failed":"Copy failed — clipboard unavailable","onb_fix_auth":"The key was not accepted. Re-copy the config below — it injects your current key.","onb_fix_base_url":"Your client could not reach the API — the base URL is probably off. Copy the fixed config below.","onb_fix_model":"That model id was not recognized. Copy the fixed config — it pins a valid model.","onb_fix_other":"The last request failed. Re-copy the config below and try again.","onb_fix_quota":"The request was blocked for insufficient credit. Add credit, or use the free test call.","onb_framing_done":"All set — {{done}} of {{total}}","onb_framing_one_left":"{{done}} of {{total}} · one step left","onb_framing_progress":"{{done}} of {{total}} complete","onb_have_code":"Have a code?","onb_impersonation_copy_blocked":"Config copy is disabled in the read-only account view.","onb_impersonation_note":"Read-only account view — full keys stay hidden.","onb_key_copied_feedback":"Copied","onb_key_copy_btn":"Copy key","onb_key_line_label":"Your API key","onb_key_none":"No keys yet","onb_key_unnamed":"API key","onb_less_btn":"Show fewer","onb_manual_anthropic_hint":"Bare host, no /v1 — Anthropic-protocol tools append /v1/messages themselves.","onb_manual_anthropic_label":"Anthropic-protocol base URL","onb_manual_copy_aria":"Copy {{label}}","onb_manual_model_label":"Model","onb_manual_models_hint":"List every available model id with GET {{url}} (same key in the Authorization header).","onb_manual_openai_hint":"For OpenAI SDKs and most tools — includes /v1.","onb_manual_openai_label":"OpenAI-compatible base URL","onb_manual_title":"Manual setup (any other client)","onb_masked_key_note":"The key is shown masked — Copy inserts your real key.","onb_more_btn":"More clients","onb_next_billing":"Manage billing","onb_next_invite":"Invite your team","onb_next_routing":"Set up routing","onb_next_secure":"Secure your agents","onb_next_title":"Next steps","onb_offer_claim_btn":"Claim in Billing","onb_offer_boost_title":"${{amount}} boost credit to collect","onb_offer_rail_armed_title":"+{{percent}}% team top-up match","onb_offer_rail_armed_note":"Your top-ups earn the bonus — up to ${{remaining}} this window.","onb_offer_rail_prompt_title":"Earn a +{{percent}}% team match","onb_offer_rail_prompt_note":"Invite a teammate who makes a call — your top-ups then earn +{{percent}}% bonus credit this month.","onb_offer_rail_prompt_btn":"Invite a teammate","onb_offer_rail_min_line":"On ${{min}}+ top-ups.","onb_offer_expires":"Expires in {{days}}d","onb_offer_free_claimable_title":"{{calls}} free calls — claimable","onb_offer_free_title":"{{calls}} free calls","onb_offer_referral_btn":"Copy invite link","onb_offer_referral_copied":"Invite link copied!","onb_offer_referral_failed":"Couldn't build your invite link.","onb_offer_referral_note":"You both get bonus credit when a friend signs up with your link.","onb_offer_referral_note_inviter":"You get bonus credit when a friend signs up with your link.","onb_offer_referral_note_invitee":"Your friend gets bonus credit when they sign up with your link.","onb_offer_referral_title":"Invite your friends","onb_offer_scoped_note":"orcarouter/auto routes within the covered models at $0 from your wallet.","onb_offer_scoped_title":"${{amount}} promo credit","onb_offer_topup_btn":"Top up now","onb_offer_topup_min_title":"+{{percent}}% on ${{amount}}+ top-up","onb_offer_topup_title":"+{{percent}}% top-up bonus","onb_offers_title":"Offers","onb_os_mac":"macOS / Linux","onb_os_toggle_aria":"Operating system","onb_os_win":"Windows","onb_playground_link":"Or try it in the Playground","onb_rail_title":"Connect your tool","onb_resume_banner":"Resume setup — finish connecting your key","onb_resume_continue":"Continue","onb_resume_dismiss_aria":"Dismiss","onb_reveal_failed":"Could not reveal the key","onb_rotate_btn":"Rotate","onb_rotate_cancel_btn":"Cancel","onb_rotate_confirm_btn":"Rotate key","onb_rotate_failed":"Rotation failed","onb_rotate_title":"Rotate this key?","onb_rotate_warning":"The old key stops working immediately, everywhere it is used. A new key is generated in its place.","onb_rotated_dismiss_btn":"Done","onb_rotated_note":"The old key is revoked. Update every place it was pasted.","onb_rotated_title":"New key — copy it now","onb_skip_btn":"Skip for now","onb_step_account":"Create your account","onb_step_credit":"Add credit","onb_step_credit_cta":"Add credit","onb_step_credit_free_cta":"Use free calls","onb_step_key":"Create an API key","onb_step_key_cta":"View key","onb_step_request":"Make your first request","onb_step_request_cta":"Send test","onb_steps_copy_btn":"Copy steps","onb_subtitle":"Connect a client and make your first request — you are minutes away.","onb_success_body":"You are live — see it in your request log.","onb_success_requests_link":"View requests","onb_success_title":"Your first request landed!","onb_test_btn":"Send a test request","onb_test_err_auth":"The key was rejected — copy it again above.","onb_test_err_base_url":"The API could not be reached — check your network and try again.","onb_test_err_line":"Test failed ({{code}})","onb_test_err_model":"The model was not recognized — try the default model.","onb_test_err_other":"The request failed — try again.","onb_test_err_quota":"Out of credit — add credit below to send a live request.","onb_test_free_btn":"Send a free test request","onb_test_free_subtitle":"Runs on your free calls — your wallet is never touched.","onb_test_need_credit":"Add credit to send a live test request.","onb_cc_need_credit":"Add credit or claim free calls before running {{client}} — the first request needs spendable balance or it fails with a quota error.","onb_cc_copied_announce":"Copied to clipboard","onb_test_ok":"{{model}} replied in {{elapsed}}ms","onb_test_ok_generic":"Reply received in {{elapsed}}ms","onb_test_running":"Sending…","onb_test_subtitle":"One request to {{model}} straight from your browser — confirms the key works, not your tool config.","onb_test_title":"Test your key in the browser","onb_title":"Get started","onb_topup_btn":"Add credit","onb_waiting_for":"Waiting for your first {{client}} request…","onb_cc_common_v1_hint":"OpenAI-compatible — base URL includes /v1.","onb_cc_common_api_key_step":"API Key: {{key}}","onb_cc_claude_code_intro":"Point Claude Code at OrcaRouter with three environment variables, then run the test command.","onb_cc_claude_code_baseurl_hint":"Anthropic protocol — bare host, no /v1. Claude Code appends /v1/messages itself; adding /v1 produces /v1/v1/messages and fails.","onb_cc_claude_code_paste_hint":"Paste the block into your terminal to set the three variables, then run the command below.","onb_cc_claude_code_win_note":"On Windows, Claude Code requires Git Bash: install Git for Windows and set CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH to your bash.exe (e.g. C:\\Program Files\\Git\\bin\\bash.exe). The block above is for PowerShell; if you run it inside Git Bash instead, use the export form.","onb_cc_codex_intro":"Add an OrcaRouter provider to ~/.codex/config.toml, export the key it references, and run the test prompt.","onb_cc_codex_baseurl_hint":"OpenAI Responses API — base URL includes /v1. Codex requires wire_api = \"responses\".","onb_cc_codex_paste_hint":"Save the block as ~/.codex/config.toml, then run the command below.","onb_cc_continue_intro":"Add an OrcaRouter model entry to ~/.continue/config.json — Continue routes chat, edit, and autocomplete through it.","onb_cc_continue_paste_hint":"Merge the models entry into ~/.continue/config.json (create the file if it does not exist), then reload your editor.","onb_cc_cherry_intro":"Create a new OpenAI provider in Cherry Studio and point it at OrcaRouter — no config files needed.","onb_cc_cherry_baseurl_hint":"Bare host, no /v1 — Cherry Studio appends /v1/chat/completions itself. If you ever get a 404, try adding /v1.","onb_cc_cherry_step_1":"Open Cherry Studio, go to Settings (gear) then Model Provider, and click + Add at the bottom to create a NEW provider of type OpenAI. Do not use the built-in \"cherryin\" provider — its API address is locked.","onb_cc_cherry_step_3":"API Address (Host): {{origin}} — bare address, no /v1 (Cherry appends it itself).","onb_cc_cherry_step_4":"Click Add Model and enter the Model ID {{model}} (the endpoint type stays OpenAI).","onb_cc_cherry_step_5":"Toggle the provider on, pick the model in the chat screen, and send a message.","onb_cc_open_webui_intro":"Run Open WebUI with the OrcaRouter connection prefilled via environment variables, then open http://localhost:3000.","onb_cc_open_webui_paste_hint":"Run the block in a terminal with Docker installed, then open http://localhost:3000 and pick a model from the model picker.","onb_cc_n8n_intro":"Create an OpenAI credential in n8n that points at OrcaRouter, then use it from an OpenAI Chat Model node.","onb_cc_n8n_step_1":"In n8n, open Credentials, then Create credential, and choose OpenAI.","onb_cc_n8n_step_3":"Base URL: {{url}}","onb_cc_n8n_step_4":"In your workflow, add an OpenAI Chat Model node (or an AI Agent with an OpenAI Chat Model) and select the credential you just created.","onb_cc_n8n_step_5":"Set the model to {{model}} and execute the node to test.","onb_cc_cursor_intro":"Override the OpenAI base URL in Cursor Settings and add an OrcaRouter model as a custom model.","onb_cc_cursor_baseurl_hint":"OpenAI-compatible override — base URL includes /v1.","onb_cc_cursor_step_1":"Open Cursor Settings, then Models (requires Cursor Pro — the free plan cannot use custom models).","onb_cc_cursor_step_2":"Set OpenAI API Key to {{key}}","onb_cc_cursor_step_3":"Enable Override OpenAI Base URL and set it to {{url}}","onb_cc_cursor_step_4":"Click Add or search model, choose Add Custom Model, and enter {{model}} — the custom model name IS the model ID sent upstream, so use a real vendor/model id, not a nickname.","onb_cc_cursor_step_5":"Select the model in the chat panel and start using it.","onb_cc_cursor_caveat":"Needs Cursor Pro. Requests reach OrcaRouter and bill, but Cursor may not render the reply (a Cursor-side BYOK limitation). Prefer the CLI tools or Cherry Studio for reliable use.","onb_cc_cursor_note":"Needs Cursor Pro. Verified: requests reach OrcaRouter and bill correctly, but Cursor may not render the reply — a Cursor-side limitation with custom (BYOK) endpoints, not an OrcaRouter problem. Prefer the CLI tools or Cherry Studio for reliable use.","onb_cc_deploy_chat_intro":"Point your DeployChat deployment at OrcaRouter with three environment variables, then redeploy.","onb_cc_deploy_chat_paste_hint":"Add these to your deployment environment (.env, Docker env, or your platform dashboard) and restart the app.","onb_cc_codex_ide_intro":"The Codex VS Code extension (also Cursor / Windsurf) reads the same ~/.codex/config.toml as the Codex CLI. Add the OrcaRouter provider, then set ORCA_KEY as a persistent OS-level environment variable and fully restart your editor.","onb_cc_codex_ide_paste_hint":"Save the block as ~/.codex/config.toml, then set the key with the command below.","onb_cc_codex_ide_note":"The extension reads ORCA_KEY from the OS environment, so a shell `export` in an open terminal won't reach an editor opened from the Dock / Start menu — set it as a persistent OS-level variable instead. Windows: the setx above. macOS: `launchctl setenv` (add a LaunchAgent to persist across reboots). Linux: append the export to ~/.profile (or use systemd ~/.config/environment.d). Fully quit and reopen your editor afterward.","onb_cc_aionui_intro":"Add a custom OpenAI provider in AionUi — a desktop chat app — and point it at OrcaRouter. No config files needed.","onb_cc_aionui_step_1":"Open AionUi, go to Settings then the Model configuration tab, and Add a new provider (type: custom / OpenAI).","onb_cc_aionui_step_2":"API request address: {{url}} — keep the /v1 (AionUi expects the /v1 form).","onb_cc_aionui_step_4":"Add a model with the Model name {{model}}, then Save.","onb_cc_aionui_step_5":"Open the chat screen, pick the model, and send a message.","onb_rail_subtitle":"Point any client at OrcaRouter, then run your first request.","onb_cc_tab_test":"Test the key","onb_cc_tab_connect":"Connect a tool","onb_cc_go_key_check":"No terminal? Test your key","onb_cc_more_integrations":"Don't see your tool? Browse all integrations","onb_cc_run_setup_label":"Then set the key & fully restart your editor","onb_cc_run_confirm":"Run it in {{client}} — this page confirms here the moment your first request arrives.","onb_cc_connected":"✓ First request received — your key is working.","onb_cc_run_block_label":"Test command","onb_cc_copy_config_aria":"Copy configuration","onb_cc_copy_test_cmd_aria":"Copy test command","onb_cc_copy_setup_cmd_aria":"Copy setup command","onb_cc_run_label":"Then run this to test the connection","onb_cc_full_guide":"Full guide","onb_more_clients_count":"More clients · {{count}}","onb_cc_cat_config":"Config","onb_cc_cat_selfhost":"Self-host","onb_cc_cat_desktop":"Desktop","onb_cc_cat_ide":"IDE","onb_cc_cat_cli":"CLI","onb_cc_group_config":"Config tools","onb_cc_group_selfhost":"Self-hosted & automation","onb_cc_group_desktop":"Desktop apps","onb_cc_group_ide":"Editor / IDE","onb_cc_group_cli":"CLI agents","onb_cc_group_popular":"Popular","onb_cc_search_empty":"No client matches \"{{query}}\".","onb_cc_search_results":"{{count}} clients match \"{{query}}\".","onb_cc_search_aria":"Search clients","onb_cc_search_placeholder":"Search {{count}} clients — Cline, Codex, Kilo, OpenCode…","onb_cc_ccswitch_step_5":"Set Name and Model to {{model}}, select the provider (shows \"in use\"), then run CC Switch's built-in test.","onb_cc_ccswitch_step_3":"Base URL: {{origin}} for Claude Code (bare host), or {{origin}}/v1 for OpenAI-protocol apps.","onb_cc_ccswitch_step_2":"Pick the target app at the top (Claude Code / Codex / Gemini), then click + to add a provider.","onb_cc_ccswitch_step_1":"Install the CC Switch desktop app (macOS: brew install --cask cc-switch; Windows: the .msi; Linux: .deb / .AppImage).","onb_cc_ccswitch_baseurl_hint":"CC Switch writes another CLI's config. Base URL depends on the target: bare host for Claude Code (Anthropic), or add /v1 for OpenAI-protocol apps.","onb_cc_ccswitch_intro":"CC Switch manages provider configs for Claude Code, Codex, and Gemini CLI from one place. Add an OrcaRouter provider and it writes the target CLI's config for you.","onb_cc_copilot_baseurl_hint":"Anthropic protocol (COPILOT_PROVIDER_TYPE=anthropic) — bare host, no /v1. With /v1 the path becomes /v1/v1/messages and 404s.","onb_cc_copilot_note":"Use the CLI, not the VS Code extension (its Add-Models picker has no custom base-URL field). Non-interactive runs need --allow-all. Skip --effort with BYOK models — Copilot rejects reasoning effort for a custom vendor/model.","onb_cc_copilot_paste_hint":"Paste the block into your terminal to set the four variables, then run the command below.","onb_cc_copilot_intro":"GitHub Copilot CLI supports BYOK. Point it at OrcaRouter with four environment variables (Anthropic protocol), then run the test.","onb_cc_nanobot_note":"Use the predefined \"custom\" provider name — a custom name gives a provider 'None' error, and don't add apiType to it. For reasoning, set reasoningEffort AND raise maxTokens above the thinking budget (~16000), or the upstream returns a 400.","onb_cc_nanobot_paste_hint":"Save the block as ~/.nanobot/config.json, then run the command below.","onb_cc_nanobot_intro":"Point nanobot at OrcaRouter via its built-in custom provider in ~/.nanobot/config.json, then run the test.","onb_cc_factory_note":"Use provider \"generic-chat-completion-api\" for the OpenAI-compatible protocol. --auto controls autonomy, not reasoning (use -r for reasoning effort). The VS Code extension shares this same config.json.","onb_cc_factory_paste_hint":"Save the block as ~/.factory/config.json, then run the command below.","onb_cc_factory_intro":"Add an OrcaRouter custom model to ~/.factory/config.json, then run the test with droid exec.","onb_cc_oh_my_pi_note":"Requires bun >= 1.3.14. The apiKey field is the NAME of an env var; with authHeader it is sent as Authorization: Bearer. Model references are three segments: orcarouter/orcarouter/auto.","onb_cc_oh_my_pi_paste_hint":"Save the block as ~/.omp/agent/models.yml, then run the command below.","onb_cc_oh_my_pi_intro":"Add an OrcaRouter provider to ~/.omp/agent/models.yml, export the key it names, and run the test.","onb_cc_pi_note":"The apiKey field is the NAME of an environment variable, not the key itself — pi injects ORCA_KEY as the Bearer token.","onb_cc_pi_paste_hint":"Save the block as ~/.pi/agent/models.json, then run the command below.","onb_cc_pi_intro":"Declare an OrcaRouter provider in ~/.pi/agent/models.json, export the key it names, and run the test.","onb_cc_crush_note":"The first run downloads the platform binary, so initial startup needs network access.","onb_cc_crush_paste_hint":"Save the block as ~/.config/crush/crush.json, then run the command below.","onb_cc_crush_intro":"Add an OrcaRouter provider to Crush's config, then run the test prompt.","onb_cc_kilo_step_7":"Send a test message to confirm the connection.","onb_cc_kilo_step_6":"Pick a model, or click + Add model and set the ID to {{model}} (a routing alias won't appear in the fetched list). Save.","onb_cc_kilo_step_4":"Base URL: {{url}}","onb_cc_kilo_step_3":"Provider ID: orcarouter (lowercase, no slashes). Display name: OrcaRouter.","onb_cc_kilo_step_2":"Open Settings then Providers, find Custom provider under Popular providers, and click + Connect.","onb_cc_kilo_step_1":"Install Kilo Code from the VS Code Marketplace and open it from the Kilo Code icon in the Activity Bar.","onb_cc_kilo_intro":"Connect Kilo Code (VS Code) through its Custom provider — an OpenAI-compatible endpoint by base URL.","onb_cc_hermes_note":"Put the key under {{env_var}} (the \u003cVENDOR>_API_KEY derived from the host), NOT OPENAI_API_KEY — a custom provider sends the latter as a placeholder and the upstream returns 401. Windows is not natively supported: run inside WSL2.","onb_cc_hermes_paste_hint":"Save the two files as shown, then launch: hermes (or hermes --tui).","onb_cc_hermes_intro":"A terminal agent from Nous Research. The endpoint goes in config.yaml and the key in .env; then launch hermes and pick a model with /model.","onb_cc_openclaw_note":"baseUrl lives under models.providers.\u003cname>, not on a model entry. The default agent is \"main\"; model references use provider/model (orcarouter/orcarouter/auto).","onb_cc_openclaw_paste_hint":"Save the block as ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json, then run the command below.","onb_cc_openclaw_intro":"Add an OrcaRouter provider to ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json, then run the local agent.","onb_cc_opencode_caveat":"Claude reasoning models over the OpenAI protocol hit a temperature 400 unless you set reasoningEffort or use a non-reasoning model (e.g. orcarouter/auto). See the guide.","onb_cc_opencode_note":"Model references are three segments (provider + vendor/model): orcarouter/orcarouter/auto. For a Claude reasoning model add \"options\": { \"reasoningEffort\": \"high\" }, or use a non-reasoning model — otherwise the upstream returns a temperature 400.","onb_cc_opencode_paste_hint":"Save the block as ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json, then run the command below.","onb_cc_opencode_intro":"Add an OrcaRouter provider to ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json, then run the test prompt.","onb_cc_cline_step_6":"Send a message in Cline to confirm the connection.","onb_cc_cline_step_5":"Model ID: {{model}}","onb_cc_cline_step_3":"Base URL: {{url}}","onb_cc_cline_step_2":"In Cline, open Settings and set API Provider to \"OpenAI Compatible\".","onb_cc_cline_step_1":"Install the Cline extension from the VS Code Marketplace and open it from the Activity Bar.","onb_cc_cline_intro":"Add an OpenAI-compatible provider in Cline (VS Code) and point it at OrcaRouter.","onb_key_create_btn":"Create a key","onb_test_result_body_label":"Test response","onb_test_error_body_label":"Error details","onb_config_block_label":"Setup configuration","onb_step_completed":"completed","onb_step_not_completed":"not completed","onboarding_page_enabled":"Pre-first-call onboarding page","onboarding_page_enabled_hint":"Show new users the Get Started page (API key, in-page test, connect guides) until their first successful API call. Off = today’s console behavior.","partner.bank.dest_label":"Payout destination","partner.bank.dest_credits":"Convert to account credits","partner.bank.dest_credits_tag":"Default","partner.bank.dest_bank_tag":"Optional","partner.bank.credits_active":"Current destination","partner.bank.switch_to_credits_cta":"Switch to credits","partner.bank.switched_to_credits":"Now receiving payouts as credits.","partner.view.payouts.note_credits":"Payouts are added to your workspace balance as account credits. Set up bank transfer in Payment Method to withdraw in USD instead.","partner.view.payouts.convert_cta":"Convert to credits","partner.view.payouts.convert_hint":"Convert a completed month's earnings into account credits — settles your oldest unsettled month first.","partner.view.payouts.convert_success":"Converted {{amount}} of {{month}} earnings to credits.","partner.view.payouts.convert_failed":"Credit conversion failed.","partner.bank.switch_confirm_title":"Switch to account credits?","partner.bank.switch_confirm_body":"This removes your saved bank details and pays future earnings as account credits. You can add a bank account again anytime.","nav_offers":"Offers","offers_seo_title":"Free AI API Credits & Free AI Models — OrcaRouter Offers","offers_seo_desc":"Get free AI API credits and call free AI models on OrcaRouter. Live voucher drops, student credits and hackathon grants — no account needed to browse.","offers_eyebrow":"Live offers · no login required","offers_hero_l1":"Free AI API credits &","offers_hero_l2":"free AI models.","offers_hero_sub":"Claim free AI API credits from live voucher drops, student programs and partner hackathons — then call a rotating set of free AI models at $0. Browse without an account; claiming takes two clicks.","offers_stat_hackathons":"Hackathons live","offers_stat_vouchers":"Credit drops","offers_stat_match":"Top deposit match","offers_stat_start":"To start","offers_filter_all":"All","offers_filter_open":"Open to all","offers_filter_hackathons":"Hackathons","offers_filter_vouchers":"Vouchers","offers_filter_soon":"Ending soon","offers_kind_hackathon":"Hackathon","offers_kind_voucher":"Voucher","offers_kind_community":"Community","offers_badge_live":"Live","offers_badge_open":"Open","offers_badge_sold_out":"Sold out","offers_badge_almost_gone":"Almost gone","offers_badge_new_accounts":"New accounts","offers_term_starter":"Starter","offers_term_match":"Match","offers_term_cap":"Cap","offers_term_min_topup":"Min top-up","offers_claimed":"Claimed","offers_closes_in":"Closes in","offers_enroll_closes_in":"Enrollment closes in","offers_join_cta":"Join","offers_claim_cta":"Claim {{amount}}","offers_card_required":"card required","offers_all_models":"all models","offers_gate_region":"Not available in your region","offers_code_placeholder":"Enter access code","offers_code_unlock":"Unlock","offers_code_none":"No code? Join the waitlist","offers_waitlist_cta":"Join the waitlist","offers_waitlist_email_placeholder":"you@email.com","offers_waitlist_join":"Join","offers_waitlist_done":"You're on the list — we'll email you about future campaigns.","offers_loading":"Loading offers…","offers_error":"Couldn't load offers.","offers_retry":"Retry","offers_empty_title":"No live drops right now","offers_empty_sub":"New voucher drops and hackathons land regularly — check back soon.","offers_models_title":"Free AI models — $0 per token.","offers_models_sub":"Free AI models on OrcaRouter cost $0 per token: no credit required, no trial clock. The lineup rotates as new open-weight and promotional models land, and every one is reachable through the same OpenAI-compatible endpoint as the paid catalog.","offers_models_all":"See all models","offers_cta_title":"Start building today.","offers_cta_sub":"A key takes 30 seconds. Claim your free AI API credits, call free AI models at $0, tap the full 40+ provider catalog — and only pay when you scale.","offers_cta_btn":"Get your API key","offers_cta_docs":"Read the docs","offers_cta_fine":"No credit card to start · usage-based pricing","offers_terms_note":"Offers vary by region & account. Terms shown on each claim page.","offers_ssg_how_h2":"How claiming works","offers_ssg_how_body":"Each offer deep-links to its claim page. Open offers claim in two clicks; community offers unlock with an access code or an eligible email (for example a student address). Eligibility is always verified server-side at claim time.","offers_ssg_campaigns_h2":"Hackathon campaigns","offers_ssg_campaigns_body":"Partner hackathons grant starter credit when you join and can match your top-ups while the campaign window is open. Terms — starter grant, match rate, caps and deadlines — are shown on every card.","offers_models_calls":"{{count}} calls","offers_waitlist_email_label":"Email address","redemption_waitlist_col_audience":"Audience","offers_badge_unavailable":"Unavailable","redeem_email_domain_title":"This offer is for a specific community","redeem_email_domain_sub":"Your account email isn’t eligible for this offer. Sign in with an eligible email to claim it.","redeem_email_domain_cta":"Update your email","payment_active_channel_title":"Active card payment channel","payment_active_channel_desc":"Choose which card / fiat channel handles new top-ups — only one is active at a time. Enter each channel's credentials in its section below; it takes effect once selected and fully configured. Crypto (USDT) is independent and controlled by its own switch.","payment_offsession_note":"Subscriptions and auto top-up are part of Stripe saved-card off-session charging, governed by the switch below — independent of which channel is primary.","payment_card_channel_label":"Card payment channel","payment_card_channel_none":"Card payments off","stripe_offsession_switch_label":"Allow off-session charging of saved Stripe cards (auto top-up / subscriptions / residual cards)","stripe_offsession_switch_extra":"Independent of the primary channel: even with Airwallex as primary, saved Stripe cards are still auto-charged (auto top-up / new subscriptions) as long as this is on and Stripe credentials exist. Turn it off (e.g. when Stripe is suspended) to stop app-initiated off-session charges. Note: subscriptions already active in Stripe keep billing on Stripe’s side until you cancel them in Stripe.","airwallex_offsession_switch_label":"Allow Airwallex card vaulting and off-session charging (card binding / auto top-up)","airwallex_offsession_switch_extra":"Default off. Turn on only after the Airwallex transaction review is closed and account-level risk controls (top-up rate limits, multi-card detection) are in place — merchant-initiated charges bypass 3DS, so disputes hit the chargeback rate directly on the only live card rail. Independent of the primary channel switch above.","airwallex_3ds_exempt_label":"FORCE_3DS regional exemptions (IP country codes, CSV)","airwallex_3ds_exempt_placeholder":"e.g. JP,KR — empty = force 3DS everywhere (recommended)","airwallex_3ds_exempt_extra":"One-time top-ups from these visitor IP countries skip forced 3DS and fall back to Airwallex's risk-based dynamic 3DS. Payments that vault a card (save-card top-ups and card binding) never take this exemption, but they do follow the force-3DS switch above. Matching uses the server-side GeoIP (MaxMind) country resolved from the client IP — never client-supplied headers — and requires GEOIP_COUNTRY_DB_PATH; without the database no exemption ever applies (safe default). Add countries only with clean fraud data and high checkout drop-off.","airwallex_enable_via_channel_selector":"Enablement is set by the \"Active card payment channel\" selector at the top — enter credentials only here. Takes effect once Airwallex is selected and its credentials are complete.","billing.error.off_session_disabled":"Saved-card charging (subscriptions / auto top-up) is currently unavailable.","billing.pay_with_airwallex":"Pay with card (Airwallex)","billing.add_credits_min_hint_airwallex":"Minimum ${{min}}. You'll be redirected to Airwallex to complete payment.","airwallex_settings_title":"Airwallex settings","airwallex_webhook_fill_in":"fill in","airwallex_sandbox_env_label":"Sandbox (Demo) environment","airwallex_settings_desc":"Airwallex card channel: one-time top-ups, plus optional card vaulting for auto top-up (governed by the off-session switch in the Active channel section, default off). Create the keys in the Airwallex dashboard.","airwallex_api_key_placeholder":"Airwallex API Key (sensitive, not shown)","airwallex_client_id_placeholder":"Airwallex Client ID (sensitive, not shown)","airwallex_webhook_secret_placeholder":"Airwallex Webhook Secret (sensitive, not shown)","airwallex_unit_price_label":"USD charged per $1 of credit","airwallex_unit_price_placeholder":"e.g. 1.00","airwallex_max_topup_placeholder":"Default 20000; caps refund/chargeback exposure","airwallex_update_settings_btn":"Update Airwallex settings","offers_free_plan_prefer_hint":"Turn on “Use my free models first” on any router to serve these before paid models.","behavior_row_free_first_title":"Free models first","behavior_row_free_first_on":"On · free models before paid","behavior_row_free_first_off":"Off · routes by strategy","free_first_label":"Use my free models first","free_first_help":"When your workspace has claimed free-package models with calls remaining, the router serves those before spending wallet balance — within the same difficulty tier, so hard prompts still escalate to a paid model when no free one fits. Falls back to paid automatically once free calls run out. Applies to free-package models only; promo credit is already spent before cash at billing.","free_first_hint":"Spend claimed free models before paid ones, within the same difficulty tier.","free_router_prefer_tip_title":"Use these from your own routers","free_router_prefer_tip":"Turn on “Use my free models first” on any router to reach for these free models before paid ones — within the same difficulty tier.","blog_latest_models_title":"Latest models","blog_latest_models_view_all":"View all models","blog_latest_models_new_badge":"NEW","blog_latest_models_prev":"Scroll to previous models","blog_latest_models_next":"Scroll to next models","blog_latest_models_attribution":"Benchmarks: {{source}} · updated daily","blog_latest_models_per_million":"per 1M tokens","blog_bench_intelligence":"Intelligence","blog_bench_coding":"Coding","blog_bench_math":"Math","blog_compared_in_title":"Compared in this article","blog_compared_in_stated":"Compared directly","blog_compared_in_same_para":"Discussed together","blog_compared_in_cta":"Compare","blog_compared_in_price":"In / 1M","blog_compared_in_note":"Detected from this article","blog_compared_in_winner":"{{model}}, {{label}}: {{value}}, best of the two","blog_compared_in_metric":"{{model}}, {{label}}: {{value}}","leaderboard_nav_consolidated":"Consolidated","leaderboard_consolidated_heading":"Consolidated ranking","leaderboard_consolidated_note":"One blended rank per model — LMArena votes, independent benchmarks, ecosystem adoption and OrcaRouter production evidence, with fixed public weights. New models enter from external evidence on day one.","leaderboard_consolidated_coming":"Consolidated ranking is warming up","leaderboard_consolidated_coming_body":"External benchmark feeds are not enabled on this deployment yet.","leaderboard_consolidated_empty":"No consolidated data yet","leaderboard_consolidated_empty_body":"Rankings appear after the first external ingest run completes.","leaderboard_col_composite":"Composite","leaderboard_col_sources":"Sources","leaderboard_col_evidence":"Evidence","leaderboard_provisional_badge":"provisional","leaderboard_nav_faq":"FAQ","leaderboard_fresh_updated":"Updated {{date}}","leaderboard_fresh_sources":"5 evidence sources","leaderboard_fresh_sla":"New models listed within 48 h","leaderboard_method_heading":"How this rank is built","leaderboard_method_bench":"Independent benchmarks","leaderboard_method_fp":"Production evidence","leaderboard_method_adopt":"Ecosystem adoption","leaderboard_faq_heading":"Frequently asked questions","leaderboard_faq_q1":"How is the AI model leaderboard ranked?","leaderboard_faq_a1":"Each model gets one blended score from four evidence families — blind human preference (LMArena), independent benchmarks (Artificial Analysis, SWE-bench), OrcaRouter production reliability, and ecosystem adoption (OpenRouter) — combined with fixed public weights of 40 / 30 / 20 / 10.","leaderboard_faq_q2":"Why does a brand-new model already have a rank?","leaderboard_faq_a2":"New models enter the board from external evidence within 48 hours of release. The rank hardens as community battles and production traffic accumulate.","leaderboard_faq_q3":"Can I export or embed this data?","leaderboard_faq_a3":"Yes — JSON and CSV export, an embeddable per-model rank badge, and an RSS feed of rank changes are free with attribution. Links are in the footer below.","leaderboard_nav_battle":"Blind Battle","leaderboard_battle_note":"Two anonymous answers, one vote. Your battles feed the 20% production-evidence weight in the consolidated rank.","leaderboard_weight_pref":"Human preference","leaderboard_faq_q4":"How often is the leaderboard updated?","leaderboard_faq_a4":"External feeds refresh daily and OrcaRouter telemetry is live; the board shows its last-updated date in the header.","leaderboard_faq_q5":"Why is a model missing from the board?","leaderboard_faq_a5":"A model needs at least two independent evidence sources to rank, and the board lists the top 25 by composite score — models with thinner evidence stay unlisted until another source picks them up.","leaderboard_faq_q6":"Are different use cases ranked separately?","leaderboard_faq_a6":"Yes — the pills above the consolidated table switch between text, coding, vision, math, reasoning and agentic boards, and battles only pair like with like.","leaderboard_faq_q7":"When does a new model’s rank harden?","leaderboard_faq_a7":"Once a model carries three evidence families including OrcaRouter’s own battle and traffic data, its rank rests on the full blend rather than external evidence alone.","leaderboard_faq_q8":"Where does the data come from?","leaderboard_faq_a8":"LMArena (CC-BY-4.0), Artificial Analysis, SWE-bench and OpenRouter rankings, plus OrcaRouter production telemetry — all attributed under the board.","leaderboard_faq_q9":"Can vendors game this ranking?","leaderboard_faq_a9":"Hard to: the weights are public, no self-reported numbers are used, and blind community battles plus live traffic anchor every score.","leaderboard_seg_aria":"Leaderboard segment","leaderboard_seg_text":"Text","leaderboard_seg_coding":"Coding","leaderboard_labshare_title":"Share of routed tokens by lab","leaderboard_labshare_others":"Others","leaderboard_pareto_count":"Models on the Pareto frontier","leaderboard_pareto_cheapest":"Cheapest frontier model ($/1M blended)","leaderboard_pareto_smartest":"Highest intelligence on the frontier","leaderboard_provisional_tip":"Provisional: fewer than three evidence families, or no OrcaRouter battle data yet. The rank hardens as more sources land.","leaderboard_show_all":"Show all {{count}}","leaderboard_show_top":"Show top {{count}}","leaderboard_col_momentum":"Momentum","leaderboard_momentum_tip":"Community buzz and rating movement — context only, never a rank input.","leaderboard_col_reliability":"Reliability","leaderboard_col_price":"$/1M blended","leaderboard_seg_vision":"Vision","leaderboard_seg_math":"Math","leaderboard_seg_reasoning":"Reasoning","leaderboard_seg_agentic":"Agentic","leaderboard_persp_speed_title":"Intelligence vs speed","leaderboard_persp_speed_note":"Output tokens per second, measured on real traffic.","leaderboard_persp_value_title":"Intelligence per dollar","leaderboard_persp_value_note":"AA Index points per blended $/1M tokens — value kings.","leaderboard_follow_label":"New models, rank changes and drops — follow along:","leaderboard_col_rank_tip":"Position by composite score within this segment.","leaderboard_col_model_tip":"Click through for the full model page: pricing, specs, provider routes.","leaderboard_col_composite_tip":"One blended 0–100 score: human preference 40%, independent benchmarks 30%, OrcaRouter production evidence 20%, ecosystem adoption 10%.","leaderboard_col_reliability_tip":"7-day success rate and median (p50) latency, measured on OrcaRouter gateway traffic.","leaderboard_col_price_tip":"Average of input and output price per 1M tokens; hover a value for the exact in → out split.","leaderboard_col_evidence_tip":"The raw per-source signals behind the blend — hover any chip for what it measures.","leaderboard_sig_arena":"LMArena community Elo — blind human votes on the text arena (CC-BY-4.0).","leaderboard_sig_vision":"LMArena vision arena Elo — blind human votes on multimodal answers.","leaderboard_sig_aa":"Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index — independent composite benchmark (0–100).","leaderboard_sig_aacode":"Artificial Analysis coding benchmark score.","leaderboard_sig_aamath":"Artificial Analysis math benchmark score.","leaderboard_sig_gpqa":"GPQA Diamond — graduate-level reasoning questions, via Artificial Analysis.","leaderboard_sig_tau":"τ²-Bench — agentic tool-use benchmark, via Artificial Analysis.","leaderboard_sig_swe":"SWE-bench Verified — % of real GitHub issues resolved (best submission per model).","leaderboard_sig_or":"OpenRouter token share — real-world ecosystem adoption.","leaderboard_sig_win":"OrcaRouter Blind Battle win rate — our own community, blind pairwise votes.","leaderboard_col_volume":"Volume","leaderboard_col_volume_tip":"Share of OrcaRouter routed tokens (30-day window). Bars are relative to the busiest model; the label is the absolute share. Arrows mark rank movement vs the previous window.","leaderboard_nav_methodology":"Methodology","leaderboard_meth_heading":"Methodology — how this leaderboard works","leaderboard_meth_intro":"Every number on this page is measured, never self-reported. This is the full method behind the consolidated rank — the same rules for every model, every day.","leaderboard_meth_blend_h":"One blended score, fixed public weights","leaderboard_meth_blend_b":"Each model gets a composite score from four independent evidence families: blind human preference 40%, independent benchmarks 30%, OrcaRouter production evidence 20% and ecosystem adoption 10%. The weights are fixed and public — no editorial adjustments, no paid placement, no vendor submissions.","leaderboard_meth_sources_h":"What feeds each family","leaderboard_meth_sources_b":"Human preference comes from LMArena’s community Elo — blind pairwise votes on the text and vision arenas (CC-BY-4.0). Independent benchmarks combine Artificial Analysis (Intelligence Index plus coding, math, GPQA Diamond and τ²-Bench) with SWE-bench Verified, the share of real GitHub issues a model resolves. Production evidence is OrcaRouter’s own: Blind Battle win rates plus live gateway telemetry — success rate, latency and routed-token volume. Adoption uses OpenRouter’s published token share.","leaderboard_meth_norm_h":"How scores become comparable","leaderboard_meth_norm_b":"Sources score on different scales (Elo, 0–100 indices, resolved-%), so each signal is standardized against the current board and mapped to 0–100: 50 is the board average and every 15 points is one standard deviation, clamped at the extremes. A model needs at least two independent evidence families to rank at all, and the board lists the top 25 by composite.","leaderboard_meth_seg_h":"Per-use-case boards","leaderboard_meth_seg_b":"The text, coding, vision, math, reasoning and agentic boards re-run the same blend over segment-appropriate signals — coding swaps in the coding benchmarks and SWE-bench Verified, vision uses the LMArena vision arena — and Blind Battles only ever pair models within the same segment.","leaderboard_meth_fresh_h":"Freshness and fair play","leaderboard_meth_fresh_b":"External feeds refresh daily and first-party telemetry is live; new models enter from external evidence within 48 hours of release. No self-reported vendor numbers are used anywhere, community buzz is shown as context but never feeds a rank, and every external source is attributed under the board.","leaderboard_seo_seg_title":"Best {{segment}} AI models — live leaderboard | OrcaRouter","leaderboard_seo_seg_desc":"{{segment}} AI models ranked by blended evidence — human preference, independent benchmarks, OrcaRouter production data and ecosystem adoption — refreshed daily.","leaderboard_momentum_flat":"Flat","stripe_fee_passthrough_enabled":"Customer pays the transaction fee","stripe_fee_passthrough_rate":"Transaction fee rate (%)","stripe_fee_passthrough_hint":"e.g. 4 = add 4% on top of the top-up amount","stripe_fee_passthrough_fixed":"Fixed fee per transaction ($)","stripe_fee_passthrough_fixed_hint":"e.g. 0.30 to match the Stripe fixed fee","offer_board_title":"Public offers board","offer_board_voucher_desc":"Show this voucher on the public /offers page","offer_board_campaign_desc":"Show this hackathon on the public /offers page","offer_board_listed_label":"List on the public offers page","offer_board_listed_warning":"Anyone can see this card, including logged-out visitors. For open offers the claim link is published too, so your anti-fraud gates become load-bearing.","offer_board_blurb_label":"Card blurb","offer_board_blurb_voucher_placeholder":"One line that sells the drop.","offer_board_blurb_campaign_placeholder":"One line that sells the hackathon.","offer_board_blurb_voucher_hint":"The voucher name is the card title; this is the subtitle beneath it.","offer_board_blurb_campaign_hint":"The campaign name is the card title; this is the subtitle beneath it. The partner name renders as the co-brand.","offer_board_featured_label":"Feature it","offer_board_featured_hint":"Pins the card to the hero slot.","offer_board_rank_label":"Rank","offer_board_rank_hint":"Lower sorts first. Featured offers win regardless.","offer_board_audience_label":"Who is it for?","offer_board_audience_derive":"Derive from the armed gates","offer_board_audience_open":"Open to everyone","offer_board_audience_code":"Invite code required","offer_board_audience_email":"Email domain","offer_board_audience_region":"Region","offer_board_audience_community":"Community","offer_board_audience_code_hint":"The claim link is withheld from the public payload; the card asks for the code instead.","offer_board_audience_region_hint":"Set a country scope above, or the card falls back to its derived audience.","offer_board_audience_name_label":"Audience label","offer_board_audience_name_placeholder":"e.g. Students, Vercel community","offer_board_domains_label":"Allowed email domains","offer_board_domains_hint":"Suffix match — \"edu\" matches mit.edu; \"mit.edu\" matches cs.mit.edu. Enforced at claim time, whether or not the card is listed.","offer_board_domains_verify_hint":"Requires email verification to be turned on in system settings.","offer_board_waitlist_label":"Collect a waitlist","offer_board_waitlist_hint":"Ineligible or sold-out visitors can leave an email instead of hitting a dead end.","offer_board_audience_locked":"The audience and waitlist settings are locked once a campaign leaves draft — they live on the join code and freeze with the rest of the terms.","offer_board_save":"Save listing","offer_board_saved":"Listing updated","offer_board_blurb_too_long":"The card blurb is limited to 160 characters","offer_board_label_too_long":"The audience label is limited to 64 characters","offer_board_audience_invalid":"Pick a valid audience for the public card","offer_board_domain_invalid":"Email domains must be bare lowercase domains, e.g. edu, mit.edu","offer_board_domain_too_many":"At most 50 email domains","offer_board_domains_required":"Add at least one email domain, or change the audience","offer_board_domains_need_verify":"Email domain gating needs email verification turned on in system settings","offer_board_batch_not_listable":"A batch of single-use codes cannot be listed on the public offers page","offers_ssg_title":"Free AI API credits & free AI models","offers_list_h2":"Live free AI credit offers","offers_list_sub":"Most offers below grant credit you can spend on any model in the catalog; a scoped one names its model on the card. Vouchers claim instantly; hackathon campaigns grant starter credit on join and can match your top-ups while the window is open.","offers_how_h2":"How to get free AI API credits","offers_how_1_t":"Create an account","offers_how_1_b":"An API key takes 30 seconds. No card, no sales call.","offers_how_2_t":"Claim an offer","offers_how_2_b":"Open offers claim in two clicks. Student and community offers unlock with an eligible email or an invite code.","offers_how_3_t":"Call any model","offers_how_3_b":"Credit works across the catalog — one OpenAI-compatible endpoint, 40+ providers. Free AI models cost $0 regardless.","offers_faq_h2":"Free AI credit — questions","offers_faq_1_q":"How do I get free AI API credits?","offers_faq_1_a":"Create an OrcaRouter account and claim any open offer on this page — most grant credit instantly, with no card required. Student and community offers unlock with an eligible email address or an invite code, and partner hackathons grant starter credit when you join. New offers are listed here as they go live.","offers_faq_2_q":"Which AI models are free to use?","offers_faq_2_a":"OrcaRouter keeps a rotating set of free AI models callable at $0 per token, listed on this page. The lineup changes as new open-weight and promotional models land. Promo credit from a voucher or hackathon is usually spendable on any model in the catalog, free or paid; a scoped offer says so on its card.","offers_faq_3_q":"Do I need a credit card for free AI API credits?","offers_faq_3_a":"No. Creating an account and claiming an open offer requires no payment method. A small number of partner offers ask for a card on file as an anti-abuse check — those are labelled \"card required\" on the card itself before you claim.","offers_faq_4_q":"Are there free AI credits for students?","offers_faq_4_a":"Yes, when a student offer is live. Student offers verify eligibility from your account's verified email domain (for example a .edu address) at claim time. If none is live right now, join the waitlist on any card that offers one and we will email you when the next drop lands.","offers_faq_5_q":"How do hackathon credits work?","offers_faq_5_a":"A partner hackathon grants starter credit the moment you join, and can match your top-ups while the campaign window is open. Each card shows the exact terms — starter grant, match rate, cap, minimum top-up and deadlines — before you commit.","offers_faq_6_q":"Does free credit expire?","offers_faq_6_a":"Promo credit carries its own expiry, shown on the claim page before you confirm. Free AI models do not expire — they are $0 for as long as they are in the lineup.","offers_faq_7_q":"Which models can I spend free AI credit on?","offers_faq_7_a":"Most offers grant wallet credit spendable across the whole catalog — 40+ providers behind one OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Some offers are scoped to a named model or family; when they are, the scope is printed on the card and enforced at claim time.","offers_faq_8_q":"Is there a free AI API without a trial clock?","offers_faq_8_a":"Yes. The free AI models on this page are $0 per token for as long as they stay in the lineup — there is no countdown and no expiring trial. Promo credit is separate and does carry an expiry, which is always shown before you claim.","offers_faq_9_q":"How is this different from free credits from OpenAI or Anthropic?","offers_faq_9_a":"Credit claimed here is not tied to one provider. The same balance calls models from 40+ upstream providers through a single OpenAI-compatible endpoint, so you can compare models or switch without a second account, a second key or a second bill.","offers_faq_10_q":"Why is my region or account not eligible?","offers_faq_10_a":"Some offers are limited by region, restricted to new accounts, or reserved for a named community. The card states the restriction up front, and eligibility is verified server-side at claim time. When you are not eligible and the card offers a waitlist, join it and we will email you when a matching offer opens.","offers_how_label":"Getting started","offers_models_label":"Always free","offers_faq_label":"Questions","offer_board_featured_voucher_hint":"Sorts the card ahead of the rest of the grid.","offers_models_loading":"Loading the current lineup…","offers_models_error":"Couldn't load the lineup just now — see the full catalog for current pricing.","offers_models_none":"No $0 models are available right now. See the full catalog for current pricing.","offer_board_listing_stale":"Still loading this campaign — try again in a moment.","nav_developers":"Developers","nav_api_references":"API References","nav_secure_agents":"Secure Agents","nav_connect_agents":"Connect Agents","nav_docs_desc":"Guides, SDKs, quickstarts","nav_api_references_desc":"Every endpoint and parameter","nav_secure_agents_desc":"Guardrails, firewall, agent hardening","nav_connect_agents_desc":"Cursor, LangChain, n8n, and more","models_filter_show_all":"Show all {{n}}","models_card_call_cta":"Call it","models_card_call_aria":"Show how to call {{name}}","models_guide_title":"How to call any model","models_guide_step_copy":"Copy the model ID from any card","models_guide_step_paste":"Paste it into the model field","models_guide_step_send":"POST to our OpenAI-compatible endpoint","models_guide_hide_aria":"Hide the quick-start guide","models_guide_show":"Show quick start","models_snippet_title":"Call {{model}}","models_snippet_intro":"OrcaRouter speaks the OpenAI API. Point any OpenAI SDK at our base URL and pass this model ID — no other changes.","models_snippet_model_id":"Model ID","models_card_offer":"Offer","models_card_offers_count":"{{n}} offers","models_cap_vision":"Vision","models_cap_audio_in":"Audio in","models_cap_tools":"Tools","models_cap_reasoning":"Reasoning","models_cap_json":"JSON mode","models_cap_row_label":"Capabilities","models_cap_more_aria":"{{n}} more capabilities","models_page_h1":"Models","models_page_subhead":"{{n}} models · {{p}} providers · one API key, one bill","models_filters_aside_aria":"Filters","models_results_heading":"Model catalog","models_table_col_model":"Model","models_table_col_input":"Input /M","models_table_col_output":"Output /M","models_table_col_actions":"Actions","models_table_caption":"{{n}} models with capabilities, context window and per-million token prices","models_compare_select":"Compare","models_compare_select_aria":"Select {{name}} to compare","models_compare_remove_aria":"Remove {{name}} from comparison","models_compare_ready":"{{n}} models selected","models_compare_need_more":"Pick {{n}} more to compare","models_compare_cta":"Compare","models_compare_clear":"Clear","models_compare_bar_aria":"Model comparison selection","nav_pg_chat_desc":"Compare replies side by side","nav_pg_image_desc":"Generate from a prompt","nav_pg_video_desc":"Text and image to video","nav_blog_desc":"Engineering notes and releases","pg_hero_lead":"Try OpenAI, Anthropic, Google and 200+ other models directly in the OrcaRouter playground. No credit card required; compare models side by side, and copy the exact API request behind any answer.","pg_mode_open":"Open playground","pg_about_do_h2":"What you can do","pg_about_do_1":"Send a prompt to any of 200+ frontier and open-weights models without writing any code or installing an SDK.","pg_about_do_2":"Switch model in one click to compare outputs without rewriting the prompt.","pg_about_do_3":"Turn on web search for any model and read the sources it cited, listed under the answer.","pg_about_do_4":"Copy the exact API request behind any conversation — curl or SDK — and paste it straight into your own code.","pg_about_when_h2":"When to use the playground","pg_about_when_body":"The playground is the fastest path from \"I read about a new model\" to \"I have a feel for whether it solves my problem\". Useful for prompt iteration before you wire a model into a production application, for spec-style A/B comparisons across vendors, and for confirming that a given model handles your domain (long documents, code, multilingual, etc.) before you commit to integration work.","pg_about_routing_h2":"How model routing works","pg_about_routing_body":"Leave the model set to Auto and the OrcaRouter routing engine classifies your prompt, scores every candidate model on price, quality and live latency, and picks the cheapest model that clears the quality bar — you see the picked model on every reply. Prefer full control? Choose any specific model from the model catalog, or watch two models race the same prompt on the leaderboard’s Battle Mode. Per-model pricing for everything you try here is listed on the pricing page.","pg_faq_h2":"Playground FAQ","pg_faq_1_q":"Is the AI playground free to use?","pg_faq_1_a":"Yes. You can browse every model and set up prompts without an account, and when guest mode is enabled you get a small number of free messages per day. Signing up unlocks every model with pay-as-you-go pricing at provider cost — no credit card required.","pg_faq_2_q":"Which AI models can I test in the playground?","pg_faq_2_a":"200+ models across OpenAI (GPT-5, GPT-4o), Anthropic (Claude Opus, Claude Sonnet), Google (Gemini Pro, Gemini Flash), DeepSeek, Llama and more — the same curated catalog the OrcaRouter API serves, including image and video generation models.","pg_faq_3_q":"Do I need an API key to try it?","pg_faq_3_a":"No key is needed to browse models or, when guest mode is on, to send your first free messages. To send unlimited messages, compare models side by side, or attach images, sign in and the playground uses one of your API keys automatically.","pg_faq_4_q":"Can I compare two AI models on the same prompt?","pg_faq_4_a":"Yes — Compare mode fans one prompt out to up to three models side by side, streaming each answer as it arrives, so you can read them against each other before committing to a model in code.","pg_faq_5_q":"Is the API OpenAI-compatible?","pg_faq_5_a":"Yes. Everything you do in the playground maps to a standard OpenAI-compatible request — swap your base URL to api.orcarouter.ai/v1 and keep your existing SDK. The playground can show you the exact request payload for any conversation.","pg_more_h2":"Keep exploring","pg_image_h1":"AI image generator playground","pg_image_lead":"Generate images from a text prompt with the image models OrcaRouter routes to. Pick a model, set size and count, and generate straight in the browser. No credit card; sign in to save what you make.","pg_image_seo_title":"AI Image Generator Playground — Generate images in your browser","pg_image_seo_description":"Generate images from a text prompt with the image models OrcaRouter routes to. Pick a model, set size and count, and generate in your browser. No credit card required.","pg_video_h1":"Text to video playground","pg_video_lead":"Turn a prompt or a still image into video with the Kling and Seedance model families, and watch the clip render in the page. Same key, same billing, nothing to install.","pg_video_seo_title":"Text to Video Playground — Generate AI video in your browser","pg_video_seo_description":"Turn text or a still image into video with Kling and Seedance video models, and watch it render in your browser. No credit card required.","airwallex_force_3ds_label":"Force 3DS on all card payments","airwallex_force_3ds_desc":"Off: Airwallex risk engine decides per transaction (dynamic 3DS). On: every card payment is challenged regardless of risk score.","apps_orcapal_title":"OrcaPal","apps_orcapal_desc":"A low-poly orca raised on this workspace's real traffic. Feed it by shipping.","apps_orcapal_connected":"Connected","orcapal_open":"Open OrcaPal","orcapal_open_failed":"Could not open OrcaPal","orcapal_admin_only":"Reading workspace telemetry requires the Admin or Owner role","orcapal_metrics_disabled":"Workspace metrics export is switched off on this deployment","orcapal_insecure_origin":"OrcaPal is configured over http, so a key cannot be handed to it safely — it needs an https address","orcapal_same_origin":"OrcaPal is configured on the console's own address, which would give it your dashboard session — it needs its own host","orcapal_connect_invite":"Connect to raise a creature on this workspace’s real traffic","orcapal_setup_aria":"Set up OrcaPal for this workspace","orcapal_connected_sub":"Connected — open it to see this workspace swim","orcapal_state_live":"OrcaPal is live","orcapal_state_offline":"OrcaPal is not connected","models_snippet_lang_group":"Snippet language","nav_sol_adaptive_routing":"Adaptive Routing","nav_sol_adaptive_routing_desc":"Every prompt graded, then routed to the model that clears your bar.","nav_sol_agent_firewall":"Agent Firewall","nav_sol_agent_firewall_desc":"Tool and MCP calls graded before they run.","nav_sol_budgets_roles":"Budgets, Roles & Audit","nav_sol_budgets_roles_desc":"Seats, spend caps, RBAC and a full audit trail.","nav_sol_byok":"Bring Your Own Key","nav_sol_byok_desc":"Use your own provider keys, rate limits and credits.","nav_sol_code_review":"AI Code Review","nav_sol_code_review_desc":"Frontier-quality PR review on your repos. Token cost only.","nav_sol_col_build":"Build","nav_sol_col_build_eyebrow":"ship without a redeploy","nav_sol_col_govern":"Govern","nav_sol_col_govern_eyebrow":"enforced, not logged","nav_sol_col_observe":"Observe","nav_sol_col_observe_eyebrow":"proof, not vibes","nav_sol_col_route":"Route","nav_sol_col_route_eyebrow":"the gateway","nav_sol_compliance":"Compliance & Governance","nav_sol_compliance_desc":"32 framework packs with exportable evidence.","nav_sol_failover":"Automatic Failover","nav_sol_failover_desc":"Configure a fallback chain; retries land before the response starts.","nav_sol_feat_desc":"A real prompt graded and routed, model and price shown.","nav_sol_feat_eyebrow":"See it live","nav_sol_feat_title":"Watch the router pick","nav_sol_guardrails":"Guardrails","nav_sol_guardrails_desc":"PII Shield and content policy, enforced before you’re billed.","nav_sol_insights":"Insights","nav_sol_insights_desc":"Routing, latency, spend and model quality in one view.","nav_sol_integrations":"Integrations & MCP","nav_sol_integrations_desc":"Cursor, LangChain, n8n, Vercel AI SDK and the MCP server.","nav_sol_orcaid":"OrcaID — Agent Identity","nav_sol_orcaid_desc":"Every agent gets its own keys, budget and kill switch.","nav_sol_playground":"Playground","nav_sol_playground_desc":"Test 200+ models in the browser. Battle two side by side.","nav_sol_prompts":"Prompt Management","nav_sol_prompts_desc":"Versioned prompts behind labels. Roll back without a deploy.","nav_sol_rail_usecase":"By use case","nav_sol_request_logs":"Request Logs","nav_sol_request_logs_desc":"Grade, model, latency and cost on every call. Copy as cURL.","nav_sol_routing_dsl":"Routing Rules (DSL)","nav_sol_routing_dsl_desc":"Express routing as code — YAML + CEL, live in seconds.","nav_sol_uc_agent_builders":"Agent Builders","nav_sol_uc_agent_builders_gloss":"Identity and budgets","nav_sol_uc_enterprise":"Enterprise","nav_sol_uc_enterprise_gloss":"SSO, private, SLA","nav_sol_uc_finops":"FinOps & Finance","nav_sol_uc_finops_gloss":"Every dollar attributed","nav_sol_uc_platform":"Platform & Infrastructure","nav_sol_uc_platform_gloss":"One endpoint, upstream 429s absorbed","nav_sol_uc_product_teams":"AI Product Teams","nav_sol_uc_product_teams_gloss":"Ship on every model","nav_sol_uc_security":"Security & Compliance","nav_sol_uc_security_gloss":"Policy before spend","nav_sol_zero_markup":"Zero-Markup Cost","nav_sol_zero_markup_desc":"Provider price, $0 per token added, glass-box receipts.","nav_solutions":"Solutions","sol_adaptive_routing_b1":"Four objectives per workspace — Cheapest, Balanced, Quality, or Adaptive, which learns the trade-off from your own traffic.","sol_adaptive_routing_b2":"Online learning: the router keeps updating from live production outcomes, not a frozen benchmark run.","sol_adaptive_routing_b3":"Routing adds under 1ms by default; opt into semantic embedding and you also pay for the embedding call. Either way the grade and chosen model land on every receipt.","sol_adaptive_routing_cta":"Watch the router pick","sol_adaptive_routing_fold_1_b":"The same OpenAI-compatible request reaches any provider, and health-aware balancing spreads load across the ones that are up. Per-channel health, weight and priority take unhealthy upstreams out of rotation automatically, and provider-specific quirks are normalised in the adapter so your client code never branches.","sol_adaptive_routing_fold_1_t":"40+ providers, one endpoint","sol_adaptive_routing_h1":"One model name. Every model behind it.","sol_adaptive_routing_receipt":"75.5% on the public RouterArena leaderboard (June 2026) — ahead of GPT-5, Azure, Martian and NotDiamond.","sol_adaptive_routing_sub":"Point your client at orcarouter/auto and every prompt is graded and sent to the model that clears your quality bar at the lowest price — with semantic embedding as an opt-in upgrade.","sol_agent_firewall_b1":"REVIEW routes to a human approval queue with notifications — the agent waits, it does not guess.","sol_agent_firewall_b2":"MCP server gating: allowlist which servers, and which tools within them, an agent may reach.","sol_agent_firewall_b3":"Per-agent autonomy levels, a threat taxonomy, and a full activity thread behind every decision.","sol_agent_firewall_cta":"See the firewall in action","sol_agent_firewall_h1":"Safe for your team. And your agents.","sol_agent_firewall_receipt":"ALLOW · REVIEW · BLOCK — evaluated before the tool runs, not after.","sol_agent_firewall_sub":"Every tool call and MCP invocation is risk-scored and graded ALLOW, REVIEW or BLOCK before it executes.","sol_budgets_roles_b1":"Spend caps at workspace, key and agent level, with auto-topup on idempotent per-charge keys.","sol_budgets_roles_b2":"Roles and scoped invites for humans; SSO and passkeys for how they sign in.","sol_budgets_roles_b3":"The audit log covers configuration changes, not just requests — who turned enforcement off, and when.","sol_budgets_roles_cta":"Set up a workspace","sol_budgets_roles_h1":"Who can spend what — and the record that proves it.","sol_budgets_roles_receipt":"Team includes 10 seats. Enterprise adds SSO and private deployment.","sol_budgets_roles_sub":"Workspaces, seats and role-based access, with hard spend caps and an audit trail that outlives the people who set it.","sol_byok_b1":"Your negotiated rates, your committed spend, your rate limits — the invoice relationship stays yours.","sol_byok_b2":"BYOK keys join the same routing pool, so automatic failover can still reach them.","sol_byok_b3":"Per-key enable and disable with role-gated access; the secret is never returned to a client after creation.","sol_byok_cta":"Connect a provider key","sol_byok_h1":"Your provider contract. Our gateway.","sol_byok_receipt":"You pay the provider directly. Our BYOK fee is a share of the standard price, not a markup on your tokens.","sol_byok_sub":"Attach your own OpenAI, Anthropic or Azure keys and route through OrcaRouter while paying the provider directly.","sol_compliance_b1":"32 packs including GDPR, SOC 2, HIPAA, PCI DSS, EU AI Act, NIST AI RMF, OWASP LLM Top 10, ISO 27001 and ISO 42001.","sol_compliance_b2":"Observe-to-enforce promotion per pack, with an impact preview before you go live.","sol_compliance_b3":"Evidence exports as a signed PDF, or as raw CSV/JSON, with a shareable read-only link for reviewers.","sol_compliance_cta":"See framework coverage","sol_compliance_fold_1_b":"Region pinning is set per workspace and enforced at routing time, so regulated traffic never leaves the geography you chose. Retention controls and zero-retention routes cover what happens afterwards — the two questions every compliance reviewer asks before they read anything else.","sol_compliance_fold_1_t":"Where your data goes, and how long it stays","sol_compliance_h1":"Coverage you can hand to an auditor.","sol_compliance_receipt":"Coverage means automated runtime controls. It is not a certification.","sol_compliance_sub":"Install a framework pack and its controls become live guardrail and firewall policy — with exportable, signed evidence behind them.","sol_failover_b1":"Name up to five fallback models, chosen from a catalogue of 200+ across 40+ providers.","sol_failover_b2":"Failover happens pre-stream — your client sees one clean response, not a truncated one followed by an error.","sol_failover_b3":"Every retry is on the receipt: what failed, what served it instead, and how long each attempt took.","sol_failover_cta":"See the failover path","sol_failover_h1":"A provider goes down. No one notices.","sol_failover_receipt":"43 provider adapters in the relay layer today — OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Bedrock, Vertex, Azure and 37 more.","sol_failover_sub":"When an upstream rate-limits or 5xxs, a configured fallback chain is retried against a healthy model before the response has started streaming.","sol_guardrails_b1":"Enforced inline, not logged after the fact: the model never sees what the policy rejected.","sol_guardrails_b2":"Observe mode first — see what would have blocked against real traffic before enforcement goes on.","sol_guardrails_b3":"A preset template library plus custom patterns, with per-match suppression and export.","sol_guardrails_cta":"Browse the guardrail library","sol_guardrails_h1":"Guardrails that stop things.","sol_guardrails_receipt":"Blocked pre-billing. A rejected request costs $0.00.","sol_guardrails_sub":"PII Shield and content policy run before the upstream call is made — a blocked request returns a clean 400 and is never billed.","sol_index_h1":"Everything OrcaRouter does","sol_index_sub":"Route, observe, govern and build on 200+ models through one OpenAI-compatible endpoint.","sol_index_usecase_h2":"By use case","sol_insights_b1":"Model mix over time — watch adaptive routing shift as your prompt distribution changes.","sol_insights_b2":"Spend by key, workspace, agent and model, so a surprise line item always has an owner.","sol_insights_b3":"Agent tool-call rate spikes flagged against learned hour-of-week baselines rather than a fixed threshold.","sol_insights_cta":"Open Insights","sol_insights_fold_1_b":"Tool-call rate anomalies are scored against a learned hour-of-week baseline, so Monday 9am traffic is never compared to Sunday 3am. Baselines are per workspace, which means there is no global threshold to tune, and detections surface alongside the firewall activity they came from.","sol_insights_fold_1_t":"Spikes measured against your own normal","sol_insights_h1":"Routing, latency, spend and quality in one view.","sol_insights_receipt":"Rate-anomaly baselines are learned per workspace, per hour-of-week.","sol_insights_sub":"Where the traffic went, what it cost, how fast it came back, and whether the router’s choices are holding up.","sol_notfound_h1":"Solution not found","sol_notfound_sub":"That page has moved or never existed. Everything OrcaRouter does is one click away.","sol_orcaid_b1":"An agent’s spend is attributable and capped independently of the humans who deployed it.","sol_orcaid_b2":"Revoke one agent without rotating a shared key or disturbing anything else.","sol_orcaid_b3":"Firewall policy, guardrails and routing rules all bind to the agent identity.","sol_orcaid_cta":"Give an agent an identity","sol_orcaid_h1":"The identity layer for your AI agents.","sol_orcaid_receipt":"Per-agent keys, a monthly budget, a spend statement and an instant kill switch.","sol_orcaid_sub":"Every agent gets a governed identity — its own API keys, its own monthly budget, its own spend statement, and an instant kill switch.","sol_page_back":"All solutions","sol_page_eyebrow":"Solutions","sol_page_related_h2":"Related","sol_prompts_b1":"A/B split traffic across two versions of a label, and roll back by moving the label if it goes badly.","sol_prompts_b2":"One-click rollback: move the label back and the next request picks it up.","sol_prompts_b3":"Webhooks fire on promotion, so your own systems stay in sync with what is live.","sol_prompts_cta":"Version your first prompt","sol_prompts_h1":"Change prompts. Not code.","sol_prompts_receipt":"Promote a label to roll out. No redeploy, no client change.","sol_prompts_sub":"Workspace-scoped system prompts, versioned behind named labels and injected via token binding — so a rollout is a label move, not a deploy.","sol_request_logs_b1":"Filter by key, model, group, request ID or type, and copy any request back out as a runnable cURL.","sol_request_logs_b2":"Failures split into upstream and request-parameter errors, so the ones you can act on are separated from the ones you cannot.","sol_request_logs_b3":"Turn on payload capture and the request body is retained apart from the log line, so you can prove exactly what was sent.","sol_request_logs_cta":"Explore a live log","sol_request_logs_fold_1_b":"Errors are split into two buckets: upstream failures, and the request-parameter errors that are yours to fix. The parameter bucket breaks down per reason so you can go straight to the malformed field; the upstream bucket stays a count, because a provider’s bad afternoon is not a list you can action.","sol_request_logs_fold_1_t":"What broke, and whether it mattered","sol_request_logs_h1":"A route is never a black box.","sol_request_logs_receipt":"grade · model · provider · latency · cached_tokens · cost — on every row.","sol_request_logs_sub":"Every request keeps a structured record — grade, chosen model, provider, latency, token counts, cost, and why it failed if it did.","sol_uc_agent_builders_b1":"Each agent gets its own key, budget and kill switch, separate from the humans who deployed it.","sol_uc_agent_builders_b2":"Every tool and MCP call is graded before it runs, with the risky ones held for human approval.","sol_uc_agent_builders_b3":"Automatic failover keeps long agent loops alive when a single provider starts rate-limiting.","sol_uc_agent_builders_cta":"See the agent firewall","sol_uc_agent_builders_h1":"Give every agent an identity, a budget, and a leash.","sol_uc_agent_builders_receipt":"Every tool and MCP call graded before it runs. Kill switch per agent.","sol_uc_agent_builders_sub":"Autonomous workloads need spend caps and tool-call review that a shared API key cannot express.","sol_uc_enterprise_b1":"SSO, scoped roles and an audit log that records configuration changes, not just requests.","sol_uc_enterprise_b2":"Private or on-premise deployment for traffic that cannot leave your own infrastructure.","sol_uc_enterprise_b3":"SLA commitments and dedicated support, with framework packs already wired to runtime controls.","sol_uc_enterprise_cta":"Contact sales","sol_uc_enterprise_h1":"Your gateway, inside your perimeter.","sol_uc_enterprise_receipt":"SLA commitments plus private and on-premise deployment.","sol_uc_enterprise_sub":"Everything above, plus the deployment model, contract and support posture procurement needs before it signs.","sol_uc_finops_b1":"Zero markup means the provider’s price is the price — there is no spread to reconcile.","sol_uc_finops_b2":"Hard caps at workspace, key and agent level, so a runaway job stops instead of arriving as an invoice.","sol_uc_finops_b3":"Spend breaks down by team, key, agent and model, so every line item has a name against it.","sol_uc_finops_cta":"See the price list","sol_uc_finops_h1":"Every dollar has an owner.","sol_uc_finops_receipt":"$0 per token added. The provider’s price is the price.","sol_uc_finops_sub":"Provider-price billing with per-key, per-workspace and per-agent attribution, and caps that actually stop spend.","sol_uc_platform_b1":"A fallback chain of up to five models means one provider’s outage is not your outage.","sol_uc_platform_b2":"Routing rules ship as version-controlled code, so staging and production diverge without forking the app.","sol_uc_platform_b3":"Structured per-request logs give every team the same answer to “what did that call actually do”.","sol_uc_platform_cta":"Read the architecture","sol_uc_platform_h1":"One endpoint your whole company can build on.","sol_uc_platform_receipt":"Up to five fallback models per request, picked from 200+ in the catalogue.","sol_uc_platform_sub":"Central routing, failover and observability for every team’s AI traffic, without each of them holding provider keys.","sol_uc_product_teams_b1":"Adaptive routing picks the model per prompt, so a better one landing next month needs no migration.","sol_uc_product_teams_b2":"Prompt versions move behind labels — experiment and roll back without waiting on a deploy train.","sol_uc_product_teams_b3":"The Playground runs the real gateway, so what you validate is what you ship.","sol_uc_product_teams_cta":"Start free","sol_uc_product_teams_h1":"Ship on every model. Commit to none.","sol_uc_product_teams_receipt":"One base URL change is the whole migration.","sol_uc_product_teams_sub":"Swap the model under a feature without touching client code, renegotiating a contract, or shipping a release.","sol_uc_security_b1":"Guardrails reject at the gateway, before the upstream call is made or billed.","sol_uc_security_b2":"The agent firewall grades every tool and MCP call before it executes, with a human queue for the ambiguous ones.","sol_uc_security_b3":"Framework packs turn controls into live policy and export signed evidence on demand.","sol_uc_security_cta":"See framework coverage","sol_uc_security_h1":"Policy that runs before the spend, not after the incident.","sol_uc_security_receipt":"32 framework packs. Observe first, then enforce.","sol_uc_security_sub":"Controls that block at request time and produce the evidence trail your auditor asks for.","sol_zero_markup_b1":"No blended rate, no rounded-up token count, and no “our price” column sitting next to theirs.","sol_zero_markup_b2":"Cached and repeated prompt tokens bill at the provider’s cache rate across 5-minute and 1-hour windows.","sol_zero_markup_b3":"cached_tokens and the provider’s own unit price appear on every receipt.","sol_zero_markup_cta":"See the price list","sol_zero_markup_fold_1_b":"Repeated and cached prompt tokens bill at the provider’s cache rate, often a fraction of the input price, across 5-minute and 1-hour ephemeral windows. Every receipt carries cached_tokens, so the saving is auditable rather than asserted.","sol_zero_markup_fold_1_t":"Pay once. Reuse for free.","sol_zero_markup_h1":"Zero markup. Zero black boxes.","sol_zero_markup_receipt":"$0.00 per token, on every plan — including Free.","sol_zero_markup_sub":"You pay each provider their exact list price. We add $0 per token — the platform is funded by plans, not by a spread on your traffic.","sol_cta_h2":"Start routing in about a minute.","sol_cta_note":"Free plan · zero markup on every token","sol_cta_primary":"Get your API key","sol_cta_secondary":"Try it in the Playground","sol_cta_sub":"Create a key, change one base URL, and every model on OrcaRouter is available to your code. No card, no sales call.","sol_story_adaptive_routing_1_b":"You write orcarouter/auto once. From then on, each prompt is read on its way through and sent to whichever model answers it best for the least money. A new frontier model lands on a Tuesday and your traffic starts using it — no migration, no client release, no meeting.","sol_story_adaptive_routing_1_t":"One name. Every model.","sol_story_adaptive_routing_2_b":"Point a workspace at the objective you actually want. Cheapest. Quality. Balanced. Or Adaptive, which learns the trade-off from your own traffic instead of someone else’s benchmark. Every choice it makes arrives on the receipt with the grade that produced it.","sol_story_adaptive_routing_2_t":"A default, not a black box.","sol_story_agent_firewall_1_b":"read_file is fine. http.fetch deserves a look. shell.exec does not happen. Every tool call and every MCP invocation is risk-scored and stamped ALLOW, REVIEW or BLOCK while the agent is still waiting for an answer.","sol_story_agent_firewall_1_t":"Graded before it runs.","sol_story_agent_firewall_2_b":"REVIEW sends the call to a human with the context attached, and the agent waits. Allowlist which MCP servers it can reach and which of their tools. Set how much autonomy it gets. Read the whole thread afterwards.","sol_story_agent_firewall_2_t":"A queue, not a guess.","sol_story_budgets_roles_1_b":"Set the ceiling at the workspace, the key or the agent. When it is reached, spend stops — it does not warn you and keep going. Auto-topup, when you want it, runs on idempotent per-charge keys so a retry never bills twice.","sol_story_budgets_roles_1_t":"A cap that actually stops.","sol_story_budgets_roles_2_b":"Seats, scoped invites and roles for the humans. SSO and passkeys for how they get in. And an audit log that covers configuration, not just traffic — so “who turned enforcement off, and when” has an answer for as long as your retention window keeps it.","sol_story_budgets_roles_2_t":"The record outlives the team.","sol_story_byok_1_b":"Bring your own OpenAI, Anthropic or Azure keys and the invoice relationship stays exactly where it is. Your committed spend still counts. Your rate limits are still yours. We are the gateway, not the reseller.","sol_story_byok_1_t":"Keep the contract you negotiated.","sol_story_byok_2_b":"A BYOK key is a first-class member of the routing pool, so failover can still reach it and your logs still explain it. Enable or disable per key, gate access by role, and know the provider secret is never handed back after the moment you create it — rotation replaces it rather than revealing it.","sol_story_byok_2_t":"Your keys, our safety net.","sol_story_compliance_1_b":"Install a framework pack and its controls become live guardrail and firewall policy on your traffic. GDPR, SOC 2, HIPAA, PCI DSS, the EU AI Act, NIST AI RMF, OWASP LLM Top 10, ISO 27001 and 42001 — 32 of them, each mapping the controls the gateway can automate and naming the ones it cannot.","sol_story_compliance_1_t":"Controls, not a spreadsheet.","sol_story_compliance_2_b":"Every pack starts in observe, shows you the impact preview, and goes live when you say so. What comes out the other end is a signed PDF, CSV or JSON — or a read-only link a reviewer can open without an account.","sol_story_compliance_2_t":"Evidence you can send.","sol_story_failover_1_b":"A provider starts throwing 503s. With a fallback chain configured, the request is already moving — it lands on a healthy model before a single token has reached your user. They see one clean answer. You see both attempts on the receipt.","sol_story_failover_1_t":"The outage nobody files a ticket about.","sol_story_failover_2_b":"You name up to five models for the chain, chosen from 200+ across 40+ providers — enough that no single upstream’s bad afternoon has to become your incident review. Health, weight and priority are tracked per channel; the ones that are struggling quietly leave the rotation.","sol_story_failover_2_t":"Somewhere to go, always.","sol_story_guardrails_1_b":"A card number goes into a prompt. The request never reaches the model, comes back as a clean 400, and costs nothing — because the check runs before the upstream call, not in a report you read on Thursday.","sol_story_guardrails_1_t":"Stopped, not noted.","sol_story_guardrails_2_b":"Turn a policy on in observe mode and watch what it would have blocked against real traffic. When the numbers look right, promote it. Nobody has to guess how much a new rule is about to break.","sol_story_guardrails_2_t":"See it before you enforce it.","sol_story_h2":"How it works","sol_story_insights_1_b":"Your prompt distribution changes, and adaptive routing changes with it. Insights shows that happening — which models are taking the work this week, what they cost, how fast they came back, and whether quality held while the mix shifted.","sol_story_insights_1_t":"Watch the mix move.","sol_story_insights_2_b":"Tool-call rate spikes are scored against a baseline learned per workspace, per hour of the week — so Monday at 9am is compared to other Mondays at 9am, not to Sunday at 3am. You hear about it as a signal, while it is still a signal.","sol_story_insights_2_t":"Surprises arrive early.","sol_story_orcaid_1_b":"It runs at three in the morning, it retries, and it has no judgement about money. So it gets its own identity: its own keys, its own monthly budget, its own spend statement — separate from the humans who deployed it.","sol_story_orcaid_1_t":"An agent is not a person.","sol_story_orcaid_2_b":"When something goes wrong you revoke that agent and nothing else moves. No shared key to rotate, no other workload to apologise to. Firewall policy, guardrails and routing rules all bind to the identity, so the leash comes with it.","sol_story_orcaid_2_t":"One switch, one agent.","sol_story_prompts_1_b":"Prompts live in the workspace, versioned behind names like production and canary. Point the label at v4 and the next request uses it. No redeploy, no client update, no waiting for the train.","sol_story_prompts_1_t":"A rollout is a label move.","sol_story_prompts_2_b":"Split traffic across two versions of a label, and move it back if the new one goes badly — the rollback is the same one move as the rollout. Webhooks fire on promotion so the rest of your tooling knows what is live.","sol_story_prompts_2_t":"And a rollback is the same move.","sol_story_request_logs_1_b":"Grade. Model. Provider. Latency. Tokens in, tokens out, tokens served from cache. What it cost. And when something failed, what failed and what picked it up. Not a sample — every request.","sol_story_request_logs_1_t":"Every call, on the record.","sol_story_request_logs_2_b":"Find the request, copy it out as a runnable cURL, and you are debugging the actual call rather than your memory of it. Switch payload capture on and the body is kept apart from the log line, so you can prove what was sent long after the argument started.","sol_story_request_logs_2_t":"From a log line to a reproduction.","sol_story_uc_agent_builders_1_b":"Autonomous workloads need a budget of their own, a tool policy of their own, and an off switch that does not take the rest of production with it. That is three things a single key in an environment variable will never give you.","sol_story_uc_agent_builders_1_t":"A shared API key cannot express this.","sol_story_uc_agent_builders_2_b":"Agents run long enough to meet a rate limit. Automatic failover keeps the loop alive across 200+ models, and every tool call it makes on the way is graded before it runs.","sol_story_uc_agent_builders_2_t":"Long loops, live providers.","sol_story_uc_enterprise_1_b":"Some traffic cannot leave your own infrastructure, and no amount of certification changes that. Private and on-premise deployment puts the gateway where the data already is.","sol_story_uc_enterprise_1_t":"Inside your perimeter.","sol_story_uc_enterprise_2_b":"SSO and scoped roles. An audit log covering configuration, not just requests. Framework packs already wired to runtime controls. SLA commitments and a named contact rather than a support queue.","sol_story_uc_enterprise_2_t":"What procurement asks for.","sol_story_uc_finops_1_b":"A gateway that marks up tokens puts a number between you and the provider’s invoice, and you spend the quarter explaining it. We add $0.00, so the provider’s price is the price and there is nothing to explain.","sol_story_uc_finops_1_t":"No spread to reconcile.","sol_story_uc_finops_2_b":"Spend breaks down by team, key, agent and model. Caps hold at each of those levels, so a runaway job stops rather than arriving as a surprise at month end.","sol_story_uc_finops_2_t":"Every line item has a name.","sol_story_uc_platform_1_b":"Every team gets the same OpenAI-compatible base URL and nobody has to hold provider keys. Routing, failover and logging happen once, centrally, instead of being reimplemented in six services with six different bugs.","sol_story_uc_platform_1_t":"One endpoint the whole company builds on.","sol_story_uc_platform_2_b":"That is the first question, and it should be. The answer is 200+ models in the retry pool and rules that ship as version-controlled code, so staging and production can diverge without anyone forking the app.","sol_story_uc_platform_2_t":"Not a new single point of failure.","sol_story_uc_product_teams_1_b":"The hardest part of shipping an AI feature is committing to a model before you know what the traffic looks like. Route through one endpoint and that decision stays reversible — every week, without a release.","sol_story_uc_product_teams_1_t":"Pick a model later.","sol_story_uc_product_teams_2_b":"Version prompts behind labels, A/B them, roll back in one move. Try the whole thing in the Playground first — it runs the real gateway, so what you validate is what you ship.","sol_story_uc_product_teams_2_t":"Iterate on the prompt, not the pipeline.","sol_story_uc_security_1_b":"Most AI observability tells you what already happened. Guardrails reject at the gateway and the firewall grades every tool call before it executes — so the control is a decision, not a note in a report.","sol_story_uc_security_1_t":"Before the spend, not after the incident.","sol_story_uc_security_2_b":"Framework packs turn controls into running policy and export signed evidence when someone asks. Coverage means automated runtime controls — we say that plainly, because it is not a certification and pretending otherwise helps nobody.","sol_story_uc_security_2_t":"The evidence is already collected.","sol_story_zero_markup_1_b":"No blended rate. No rounded-up token count. No column labelled “our price” sitting next to theirs. We add exactly $0.00 per token, on every plan including the free one, because the platform is paid for by subscriptions rather than by a spread on your traffic.","sol_story_zero_markup_1_t":"The provider’s price. Full stop.","sol_story_zero_markup_2_b":"Each request shows the grade, the model that served it, the provider behind it, the unit price they charge and the tokens that came from cache. Cost stops being a number you reconcile at month end and becomes something you can read one call at a time.","sol_story_zero_markup_2_t":"A receipt, not an estimate.","nav_sol_api_keys":"API Keys & Token Governance","nav_sol_api_keys_desc":"Scoped keys with their own limits, budgets and revocation.","nav_sol_apps":"Apps & Add-ons","nav_sol_apps_desc":"Products built on your gateway. Pay only what runs.","nav_sol_data_residency":"Data Residency & Privacy","nav_sol_data_residency_desc":"Declared region, region-partitioned evidence, retention controls.","nav_sol_prompt_caching":"Prompt Caching","nav_sol_prompt_caching_desc":"Cached tokens bill at the provider’s cache rate, not full price.","sol_api_keys_b1":"Scope a key to specific models, a spend ceiling, a rate limit and an expiry date when you create it.","sol_api_keys_b2":"Every request in the logs carries the key that made it, so attribution and revocation are the same lookup.","sol_api_keys_b3":"Revoke one key without touching the others; re-revealing a key is a role-gated action and is written to the audit log.","sol_api_keys_cta":"Create your first key","sol_api_keys_h1":"One key per job, not one key for everything.","sol_api_keys_receipt":"Shown once. Scoped at creation. Revoked without collateral.","sol_api_keys_sub":"Issue as many keys as you have workloads, each with its own scope, its own ceiling, and its own off switch.","sol_apps_b1":"Set up once, then pay only the token cost of what actually runs. No per-seat fee and no per-repo fee.","sol_apps_b2":"An app that runs through the gateway is a workload like any other: its spend shows up beside everything else and obeys the same caps.","sol_apps_b3":"For those apps, guardrails, the agent firewall and routing rules apply exactly as they do to your own code.","sol_apps_cta":"Browse the apps","sol_apps_h1":"Products that run on your own gateway.","sol_apps_receipt":"Token cost only. It is your gateway doing the work.","sol_apps_sub":"Turn one on and it inherits everything you have already set up — your routing, your guardrails, your budgets, your logs.","sol_data_residency_b1":"Declare a region per workspace; every compliance report is stamped with it and filed under a region-partitioned path. Physically regionalized storage is a deployment choice, not something the gateway does for you.","sol_data_residency_b2":"A cross-region read is denied rather than served — an artifact is never handed over under a residency it cannot satisfy.","sol_data_residency_b3":"Retention is the part enforced per request: payloads sit apart from the request log, and a zero-retention route only picks a ZDR-eligible channel.","sol_data_residency_cta":"See framework coverage","sol_data_residency_h1":"Declare your region. Have it on every report.","sol_data_residency_receipt":"A disclosure and evidence-locality control. Not geo-pinned inference.","sol_data_residency_sub":"A workspace declares its data-residency region. Every compliance report is stamped with it, filed under it, and refused to a cross-region read.","sol_prompt_caching_b1":"Cache-eligible prefixes are billed at the provider’s cache rate across 5-minute and 1-hour ephemeral windows.","sol_prompt_caching_b2":"cached_tokens appears on every receipt, so the saving is auditable rather than asserted.","sol_prompt_caching_b3":"Nothing to configure in your client — cache_control is passed straight through to the provider that supports it.","sol_prompt_caching_cta":"See the price list","sol_prompt_caching_h1":"Pay full price once. Reuse at the cache rate.","sol_prompt_caching_receipt":"cached_tokens on every receipt. 5-minute and 1-hour windows.","sol_prompt_caching_sub":"Repeated prompt tokens bill at the provider’s cache rate — often a fraction of the input price — and the saving lands on the receipt rather than in a projection.","sol_story_api_keys_1_b":"The staging job, the nightly batch, the intern’s prototype — each gets its own key with its own model scope, its own ceiling and its own expiry. A key is cheap. A shared key that nobody dares rotate is not.","sol_story_api_keys_1_t":"One key per job.","sol_story_api_keys_2_b":"Every request carries the key that made it, so finding the source of a spike and switching it off are the same action. Nothing else on the account notices. The secret itself is shown at creation; revealing it again is possible, but role-gated and written to the audit log.","sol_story_api_keys_2_t":"Revocation without collateral.","sol_story_apps_1_b":"An app is not a separate product with a separate bill and a separate set of permissions. It runs on the gateway you already configured, so it inherits your routing, your guardrails, your budgets and your logs on the day you turn it on.","sol_story_apps_1_t":"It is your gateway doing the work.","sol_story_apps_2_b":"No seats, no per-repo pricing, no minimum. The tokens an app spends appear beside everything else you spend and obey the same caps — so a quiet month costs a quiet month’s worth.","sol_story_apps_2_t":"You pay for what ran.","sol_story_data_residency_1_b":"Set the workspace region and every compliance report is stamped with it, rendered into region-partitioned storage, and withheld from a cross-region read rather than served under a residency it cannot satisfy. What this is not: a claim that we geo-pin inference. Upstream providers process requests in their own regions, and the report says so in as many words.","sol_story_data_residency_1_t":"A region you declare, and can prove.","sol_story_data_residency_2_b":"Prompt payloads sit apart from the request log, so the audit trail — who called what, when, at what cost — outlives the content itself, which you can keep for hours or not at all. And a zero-retention route will only select a channel flagged ZDR-eligible: the check fails closed, so an unflagged channel is never quietly used instead.","sol_story_data_residency_2_t":"Retention is the enforced half.","sol_story_prompt_caching_1_b":"The system prompt, the schema, the few-shot examples, the document you are asking about — the same tokens, sent again and again. Cached, they bill at the provider’s cache rate, which is routinely a tenth of the input price.","sol_story_prompt_caching_1_t":"Most of your prompt never changes.","sol_story_prompt_caching_2_b":"cached_tokens is on every receipt next to the tokens you paid full price for. The saving is a number you can add up at the end of the month, not a percentage in a pitch.","sol_story_prompt_caching_2_t":"And you can check the arithmetic.","demo_accuracy_cap":"Accuracy Score · RouterArena · Jun 2026","demo_dash_cost":"cost / req","demo_dash_live":"live","demo_fo_provider_a":"Provider A","demo_fo_provider_b":"Provider B","demo_pii_never_billed":"never billed","demo_gb_graded":"graded","demo_gb_graded_val":"hard · 0.82","demo_gb_model":"model","demo_gb_provider":"provider","demo_gb_markup":"markup","demo_cache_input":"input","demo_cache_input_val":"12,000 tok","demo_cache_cached":"cached","demo_cache_cached_val":"10,800 tok","demo_cache_billed":"billed","demo_cache_billed_val":"cache rate","demo_cache_hit":"cache hit","demo_byok_your_key":"your key","demo_byok_billed_by":"billed by","demo_byok_prov":"OpenAI · direct","demo_byok_note":"your contract, your rate","demo_comp_mode":"observe → enforce","demo_comp_cc61":"CC6.1 access control","demo_comp_cc72":"CC7.2 monitoring","demo_comp_cc81":"CC8.1 change mgmt","demo_oid_own_key":"own key","demo_oid_budget":"$200 / mo","demo_oid_kill":"revoked · nothing else affected","demo_bud_workspace":"workspace budget","demo_bud_cap":"$500 cap","demo_bud_stop":"spend stopped at cap","demo_res_declared":"declared","demo_res_report":"report stamped","demo_res_stored":"stored in-region","demo_res_read":"read from us-east","demo_res_denied":"denied","demo_res_note":"retention 0h · zero-retention route","demo_keys_revoked":"revoked","demo_keys_active":"active","demo_app_name":"Code Review","demo_app_on":"on","demo_app_chip_routing":"routing","demo_app_chip_guardrails":"guardrails","demo_app_chip_budgets":"budgets","demo_app_chip_logs":"logs","demo_app_billed":"billed: token cost only","ad_tracking_settings_tab":"Ads & Tracking","ad_tracking_section":"Ad conversion tracking","ad_tracking_desc":"Controls the ad tags rendered into the site and the ad-network click-ID parameters captured for signup attribution. Changes apply on the next page load — no deploy needed.","ad_tracking_enabled_label":"Enable admin-configured ad tags","ad_tracking_meta_pixel_label":"Meta Pixel ID","ad_tracking_meta_pixel_placeholder":"Numeric pixel ID, e.g. 656083250933792 — empty removes the pixel","ad_tracking_meta_pixel_hint":"Rendered server-side into the page (script + noscript) with the sensitive-route guard. Clearing it removes the Meta Pixel without a deploy.","ad_tracking_meta_pixel_invalid":"Meta Pixel ID must be numeric (5–32 digits)","ad_tracking_click_ids_label":"Additional click-ID parameters","ad_tracking_click_ids_placeholder":"Add a parameter and press Enter, e.g. rdt_cid","ad_tracking_click_ids_hint":"Captured at landing and stored on the signup record, in addition to the built-in set (gclid, fbclid, ttclid, li_fat_id, msclkid, twclid, rdt_cid, sccid, epik, …).","ad_tracking_click_ids_invalid":"Parameter names may only contain letters, digits, _ and - (max 64 characters)","ad_tracking_gtm_note":"Google Tag Manager and Google Analytics are unchanged for now: GTM loads from index.html and GA via the GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_ID environment variable. They will move into this panel in a later phase.","ad_tracking_save":"Save","ad_tracking_saved":"Saved","ad_tracking_save_failed":"Save failed","ad_tracking_no_changes":"Nothing to update","ad_tracking_click_ids_reserved":"Credential-like or reserved parameter names (token, code, key, boost, redirect_url, utm_*, …) are not allowed","ad_tracking_tiktok_pixel_label":"TikTok Pixel ID","ad_tracking_linkedin_partner_label":"LinkedIn Partner ID","ad_tracking_twitter_pixel_label":"X (Twitter) Pixel ID","ad_tracking_reddit_pixel_label":"Reddit Pixel ID","ad_tracking_pixel_id_invalid":"The ID does not match this platform's expected format","ad_tracking_custom_snippet_label":"Custom head snippet","ad_tracking_custom_snippet_hint":"Raw HTML for ad networks without a dedicated field (Snap, Pinterest, Quora, …). Root admins only; 16 KB max. Injected on every page behind the same runtime guard as the built-in pixels — skipped on sensitive routes and OAuth callbacks.","ad_tracking_custom_snippet_too_long":"The custom snippet exceeds the 16 KB limit","ad_tracking_x_signup_event_label":"X signup event ID","ad_tracking_x_purchase_event_label":"X purchase event ID","ad_tracking_linkedin_signup_conv_label":"LinkedIn signup conversion ID","ad_tracking_linkedin_purchase_conv_label":"LinkedIn purchase conversion ID","ad_tracking_conversion_ids_section":"Conversion events","ad_tracking_conversion_ids_hint":"Signups, first API calls and payments are reported automatically to Meta, TikTok and Reddit once their pixel is configured. X and LinkedIn additionally need a per-event ID from X Events Manager / LinkedIn Campaign Manager — leave one empty to skip that network for that event.","ad_tracking_custom_snippet_markers":"The snippet must not contain the ad-tracking placeholder markers","ad_tracking_click_ids_too_many":"At most 20 additional click ID parameters are supported","auth_continue_status":"Finishing sign-in, redirecting you now…","ad_tracking_x_activation_event_label":"X first-API-call event ID","ad_tracking_linkedin_activation_conv_label":"LinkedIn first-API-call conversion ID","ad_tracking_matrix_section":"Which events reach which platform","ad_tracking_matrix_caption":"Live view of your current settings — it updates as you type, before anything is saved.","ad_tracking_matrix_event_col":"Event","ad_tracking_matrix_custom_col":"Custom snippet","ad_tracking_matrix_on":"Reported","ad_tracking_matrix_off":"Not configured","ad_tracking_matrix_needs_id":"Needs event ID","ad_tracking_matrix_conditional":"Sent as a custom event instead","ad_tracking_matrix_pageview_note":"Page views are not listed: every pixel fires its own on load and there is nothing per-event to configure. The three events above are the ones campaigns can optimize against.","ad_tracking_event_signup":"Signup","ad_tracking_event_signup_desc":"An account was created.","ad_tracking_event_activation":"First API call","ad_tracking_event_activation_desc":"The user's first successful API request. Reported once per user, and it usually lands days before any payment.","ad_tracking_event_purchase":"Purchase","ad_tracking_event_purchase_desc":"A payment completed.","ad_tracking_event_meta_purchase_note":"Meta requires an amount and the browser never sends one.","ad_tracking_event_custom_activation_note":"Only if the snippet sets window.__orcaAdConversionListener.","ad_tracking_multi_pixel_hint":"Each field above holds one ID per platform. To place a second pixel from the same platform — another ad account, an agency's pixel — add it here: every conversion is also dispatched as an orcarouter:conversion DOM event you can forward yourself. The activation event also requires the snippet to set window.__orcaAdConversionListener = true, as in the example: it is reported only once per user, so it is skipped rather than sent to a snippet that isn't listening.","ad_tracking_matrix_disabled_note":"Admin-configured ad tags are turned off, so nothing below is sent — no pixel is rendered regardless of the IDs saved here.","ad_tracking_load_failed":"Could not load the current settings, so editing is locked to avoid overwriting them:","ad_tracking_retry":"Retry","oauth_bind_success":"Binding successful!","ad_tracking_enable_skipped":"Not enabled: a pixel or event ID failed to save, and enabling now would publish the previously stored ID.","redeem_open_console_cta":"Go to my console","campaign_landing_template_desc":"What people see when they open the join link","landing_template_label":"Claim page","landing_template_default":"Standard claim page","landing_template_default_desc":"The general-purpose voucher page.","landing_template_github_oss":"Open source contributors","landing_template_github_oss_desc":"Developer-native copy and GitHub sign-in. Add ?gh=LOGIN&repo=OWNER/NAME to each outreach link — e.g. /redeem/CODE?gh=octocat&repo=vercel/ai. Without them the page quietly falls back to a generic version.","landing_template_github_oauth_off":"GitHub sign-in is currently off for this site, so claimants will not see a GitHub button. Enable the GitHub OAuth provider in settings, or expect them to use the other sign-in options.","redeem_trust_no_card":"No credit card","redeem_trust_no_card_claim":"No card to claim","redeem_trust_card_required":"Card required to claim","redeem_elig_new_users":"New accounts only","redeem_oss_elig_label":"Eligibility requirements","redeem_oss_audience":"Intended for {{label}}","redeem_elig_new_users_window":"New accounts (first {{v}}h)","redeem_elig_country":"Available in {{v}}","redeem_elig_domain":"{{v}} addresses only","redeem_terms_applied_match_drained":"enrols you — no match funded right now","redeem_terms_applied_match_pending":"enrols you — the match opens later","redeem_terms_applied_match":"matched on your next qualifying top-up","redeem_terms_applied_match_min":"matched on your next qualifying top-up of ${{min}}+","redeem_terms_applied_squad":"released when your squad resolves","redeem_terms_applied_squad_fill":"released when your squad fills","redeem_terms_applied_boost":"applied when you collect","redeem_terms_valid_until":"Valid until {{v}}","redeem_terms_applied":"applied when you claim","redeem_terms_valid_days":"Valid {{v}} days","redeem_terms_valid_day":"Valid 1 day","redeem_terms_no_expiry":"no expiry","redeem_terms_no_renew":"nothing renews","redeem_supply_left":"{{n}} of {{max}} left","redeem_oss_eyebrow":"Open source program","redeem_oss_headline_repo":"{{amount}} of AI credit for {{repo}} contributors","redeem_oss_headline_generic":"{{amount}} of AI credit for open source contributors","redeem_oss_ident_repo":"Invitation for {{repo}} contributors","redeem_oss_ident_generic":"Invited to the OrcaRouter open source program","redeem_oss_ident_source":"This invitation was sourced from public commit metadata — no private data was used.","redeem_oss_sub_scoped":"One OpenAI-compatible endpoint.","redeem_oss_sub":"One OpenAI-compatible endpoint. 200+ models.","redeem_oss_trust_squad":"Unlocks when your squad resolves","redeem_oss_trust_squad_fill":"Unlocks when your squad fills","redeem_oss_trust_boost":"Collect after your share window","redeem_oss_trust_fast":"About 60 seconds","redeem_oss_trust_norepo":"No repository access","redeem_elig_region":"Limited by region","redeem_elig_email_domain":"Limited to certain email domains","campaign_preset_oss_contributor":"Open source outreach","campaign_preset_oss_contributor_desc":"Starter grant, developer claim page, anti-abuse armed","redeem_terms_auto_topup_required":"auto top-up required","redeem_terms_auto_topup_optional":"auto top-up optional","redeem_oss_headline_repo_noamount":"AI credit for {{repo}} contributors","redeem_oss_headline_generic_noamount":"AI credit for open source contributors","models_sidebar_active_count":"{{count}} active","email_alias_restriction_label":"Block Gmail alias signups (+ and .)","email_alias_restriction_hint":"Rejects gmail.com / googlemail.com signups whose address contains + or . — Google ignores both, so a single mailbox can mint unlimited accounts. Other providers are untouched: their dots are significant, and their + subaddressing is allowed by decision.","airwallex_topup_savecard_switch_label":"Save the card during a one-time Airwallex top-up and turn auto top-up on","airwallex_topup_savecard_switch_extra":"Default off, and only takes effect while the Airwallex off-session switch above is also on — storing a card that cannot be charged is pointless. When on, the top-up checkout asks to save the card and auto top-up is enabled for workspaces that never configured it. The checkout then only offers card / Apple Pay / Google Pay, since wallets cannot authorise later charges; wallet payments still complete and credit normally, they just do not save a card.","subscription_cancel_renewal":"Cancel renewal","subscription_cancel_confirm_title":"Cancel this subscription?","subscription_cancel_confirm_body":"It stays active until the end of the current period, then will not renew. No further charges will be made.","subscription_cancel_success":"Renewal cancelled. Your subscription stays active until the end of the period.","subscription_activated":"Subscription activated","subscription_activation_pending":"Payment received. Activation is still processing — refresh in a moment if your subscription is not listed yet.","airwallex_subscription_switch_label":"Sell subscriptions through Airwallex","airwallex_subscription_switch_extra":"Default off. Independent of the off-session switch above: subscriptions run on the Billing product line with their own customer and payment-source objects. When on, plans bound to an Airwallex Price are purchased through the Airwallex hosted subscription checkout — the first period is paid on-session (3DS available) and renewals are charged automatically by Airwallex. Requires the Airwallex webhook secret and the Billing event group enabled in the Airwallex console.","subscription_activation_failed":"We could not confirm this subscription payment. Please contact support if you were charged.","workspace_acq_title":"Acquisition","workspace_acq_channel":"Channel","admin_workspaces_col_channel":"Channel","workspace_acq_referrer":"Referrer","workspace_acq_signup_method":"Signup method","workspace_acq_country":"Country","workspace_acq_utm_source":"Source","workspace_acq_utm_medium":"Medium","workspace_acq_utm_campaign":"Campaign","workspace_acq_utm_content":"Content","workspace_acq_click_ids":"Click IDs","workspace_acq_search_term_paid":"Search term (paid)","workspace_acq_search_term_paid_none":"Not a paid click","workspace_acq_organic_title":"Likely search terms (organic)","workspace_acq_confidence":"Confidence","workspace_acq_confidence_high":"High","workspace_acq_confidence_medium":"Medium","workspace_acq_confidence_low":"Low","workspace_acq_clicks":"clicks","workspace_acq_journey":"Journey","workspace_acq_journey_none":"No pre-signup visits recorded","workspace_acq_organic_note":"Inferred, not observed. Google does not reveal per-visitor search queries. These are the organic queries that drove clicks to {{path}} on {{date}}, the first page this customer reached from Google organic search before signing up, ranked by click share.","workspace_acq_organic_no_data":"No organic clicks to {{path}} are recorded for {{date}}. Either Search Console has not published that day yet (it lags about two days), or the page was published with impressions but no clicks — either way there is nothing to infer a term from.","workspace_acq_loaded":"Acquisition data loaded.","workspace_acq_journey_truncated":"This customer has more pre-signup visits than are shown. Only the earliest are listed, so a later landing may be missing.","workspace_acq_organic_not_mirrored":"Search Console data for {{path}} on {{date}} was never fetched. Either that day falls outside the sync window (widen OR_GSC_WINDOW_DAYS and re-sync), or its sync failed and the next sweep will retry it.","workspace_acq_organic_no_landing":"Organic inference needs the landing page this visitor arrived on. No retained landing data exists for this customer — either the signup predates visit tracking, or the visits have passed the retention window.","workspace_acq_organic_not_search":"This visitor did not arrive from a search engine, so there is no search term to infer.","acquisition_tab_organic":"Organic queries","acq_organic_queries_heading":"Top organic queries","acq_organic_landings_heading":"Organic landing pages","acq_organic_col_query":"Query","acq_organic_col_clicks":"Clicks","acq_organic_col_impressions":"Impressions","acq_organic_col_position":"Avg. position","acq_organic_col_landing":"Landing page","acq_organic_col_signups":"Signups","acq_organic_data_through":"Data through {{date}}","acq_organic_signups_from":"Signups are counted from {{date}} onward. Search Console has not mirrored any earlier day in this range, so the signup column covers a shorter span than the dates you selected.","acq_organic_floor_note":"Totals come from Search Console's page-level data and include clicks from queries Google withheld. The query list itself is incomplete: long-tail terms are withheld for privacy, so the listed queries will not add up to the totals. Data lags about two days, so the most recent days read empty. Signups count visitors whose first Google-referred landing was that page, before they signed up.","acq_organic_signups_truncated":"Signup counts are a floor: this window exceeded the attribution scan limit.","acq_organic_empty":"No organic search data for this window","workspace_acq_load_failed":"Acquisition data could not be loaded. Retry to see where this customer came from.","workspace_acq_unavailable":"Acquisition data is not available yet.","workspace_acq_organic_engine_unsupported":"This visitor arrived from a search engine other than Google. We only mirror Google Search Console data, so their query is not available.","workspace_acq_organic_withheld":"Google withheld {{withheld}} of {{total}} clicks to this page as anonymised queries, so the terms above do not account for all of them.","workspace_acq_organic_reported_basis":"No page-level total was available for this day, so these shares are of the reported queries only and overstate each term.","acq_organic_refresh":"Refresh organic queries","acq_organic_load_failed":"Organic search data could not be loaded for this range. Retry to try again.","workspace_acq_organic_paid_touch":"This was a paid ad click, not an organic visit. Any keyword is the one shown above, observed exactly rather than inferred — auto-tagged campaigns often pass none.","workspace_acq_organic_all_withheld":"Search Console published {{path}} for {{date}} and recorded clicks, but withheld every query as anonymised. No terms will become available for this day.","executive_drill_pager_showing":"Showing","executive_drill_pager_prev":"Previous","executive_drill_pager_next":"Next","executive_drill_pager_page_size":"Per page","executive_drill_page_total":"Page total","executive_drill_grand_total":"Grand total","acq_program_campaign":"Hackathon","acq_program_squad":"Squad","acq_program_boost":"Booster","acq_program_redemption":"Voucher","acq_program_partner":"Partner","acq_program_referral":"Referral","acq_program_boost_helper":"Boost helper","acq_program_discord":"Discord","acq_program_organic":"Organic","admin_workspaces_col_program":"Program","users_col_program":"Program","admin_ws_programs_title":"Programs","admin_ws_programs_first_touch":"First touch","admin_ws_programs_empty":"No program history","admin_ws_programs_fetch_failed":"Failed to load programs","admin_ws_programs_col_program":"Program","admin_ws_programs_col_ref":"Reference","admin_ws_programs_col_at":"Claimed","admin_ws_programs_col_granted":"Granted","executive_daily_group_programs":"+ Programs","executive_daily_group_byok":"+ BYOK","executive_daily_col_new_byok":"New BYOK","executive_drill_mode_pivot":"Pivot","executive_drill_mode_signups":"Signups","executive_drill_mode_byok":"BYOK","executive_roster_col_user":"User","executive_roster_col_email":"Email","executive_roster_col_workspace":"Workspace","executive_roster_col_program":"Program","executive_roster_col_source":"Source","executive_roster_col_signed_up":"Signed up","executive_roster_col_first_call":"First call","executive_roster_col_lifetime":"Lifetime","executive_roster_col_provider":"Provider","executive_roster_col_first_byok":"First BYOK","executive_roster_col_byok_share":"BYOK share","executive_roster_col_fee":"Fee","admin_workspaces_filter_all":"All","executive_daily_program_cell_aria":"{{count}} new signups from {{program}} on {{date}} — show who","executive_dim_acq_program":"Acquisition program","executive_dim_acq_program_ref":"Program instance","executive_daily_byok_cell_aria":"{{count}} workspaces adopted BYOK on {{date}} — show which","executive_export_truncated":"Export capped at {{rows}} of {{total}} rows — narrow the range or pick a coarser dimension for the complete report.","token_search_placeholder":"Search by key name","token_batch_limit_btn":"Limit all keys","token_batch_limit_title":"Set limit for all keys","token_batch_limit_desc":"Applies one recurring spend limit to every key you can edit. Lifetime credit limits are not changed. Any key can be adjusted individually afterwards — the later edit wins. Selecting None clears the recurring limit from all keys.","token_batch_limit_success":"Updated {{updated}} keys ({{unchanged}} unchanged)","token_batch_limit_skipped":"{{count}} protected keys were skipped (admin-only)","token_batch_limit_apply":"Apply to all keys","token_batch_limit_applying":"Applying…","token_batch_limit_failed":"{{failed}} keys failed to update — their limits are unchanged. Updated {{updated}}.","token_search_no_results":"No keys match your search","token_search_no_results_desc":"Try a different name or clear the search.","token_search_clear":"Clear search","token_dialog_close":"Close","token_batch_limit_evict_failed":"{{count}} keys were updated but may keep their old limit for up to a minute (cache refresh failed).","token_search_results_count":"{{count}} keys found","workspace_acq_search_term_paid_missing":"Paid click, but the campaign did not pass a keyword","workspace_acq_organic_trail_truncated":"This visitor has more pre-signup visits than we scan, and none of the earliest ones came from Google. A later search visit may exist that we did not reach, so this is not a conclusion that they never arrived from search.","workspace_acq_organic_restricted":"Search Console query data requires the marketing or revenue analytics permission. Your role can see this customer, but not their search terms.","workspace_acq_subsection_unavailable":"This could not be loaded. It is a read failure, not an empty result — retry in a moment.","acq_channel_direct":"Direct","acq_channel_organic_search":"Organic Search","acq_channel_prefix_paid":"Paid","acq_channel_prefix_social":"Social","acq_channel_prefix_referral":"Referral","acq_channel_network_other":"Other","compare_intro_no_provider":"A head-to-head comparison of {{a}} and {{b}} on OrcaRouter — pricing, context window, latency, throughput and benchmark quality, side by side, so you can pick the right model for your workload.","workspace_acq_loading":"Loading acquisition data…","workspace_acq_journey_no_stitch":"This signup is not linked to any browsing session, so no pre-signup trail could be recorded — usually a signup that predates visit tracking.","acq_organic_loading":"Loading organic search report…","workspace_acq_stale_refresh":"Could not refresh this section. The values below are from an earlier load and may be out of date.","acq_organic_loaded":"Organic search report updated.","onb_cc_all_clients":"All {{count}} clients","onb_cc_run_plain":"Run it in {{client}} — your requests show up in the request log.","keys_tab_keys":"Keys","keys_tab_connect":"Connect","keys_row_connect":"Connect this key","keys_row_menu_aria":"Key actions","connect_no_keys":"Create an API key first — the setup guides fill your key into each config.","connect_key_missing":"That key no longer exists, or you do not have access to it. Pick another key from the Keys tab.","connect_key_unusable":"This key cannot make requests right now — check its status on the Keys tab. The setup below is still correct for it.","connect_reveal_stale_identity":"The signed-in account changed while this key was being revealed. Try again.","connect_load_failed":"Could not load your keys. Reload the page to try again.","connect_loading":"Loading your API keys…","plan_team_trial_btn":"Start {{days}}-day free trial","zc_banner_title":"API requests will fail — no spendable credit.","zc_add_credits_btn":"Add credits","zc_ask_admin_hint":"Ask a workspace admin to add